lio-site/commit/1b49fdb2fd97e5fbf23f7616df841637d6e17e50","node_id":"C_kwDOT8irxNoAKDFiNDlmZGIyZmQ5N2U1ZmJmMjNmNzYxNmRmODQxNjM3ZDZlMTdlNTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/im-kaushal/portfolio-site/commit/f0952ce1dd017e1902d15a9d827bc6959d2bbab1","sha":"f0952ce1dd017e1902d15a9d827bc6959d2bbab1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/im-kaushal/portfolio-site/commits/f0952ce1dd017e1902d15a9d827bc6959d2bbab1"}],"sha":"1b49fdb2fd97e5fbf23f7616df841637d6e17e50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/im-kaushal/portfolio-site/commits/1b49fdb2fd97e5fbf23f7616df841637d6e17e50"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/8329?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/vercel","id":35613825,"login":"vercel[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90MzU2MTM4MjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/im-kaushal/portfolio-site/commits/f0952ce1dd017e1902d15a9d827bc6959d2bbab1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T20:46:36Z","email":"35613825+vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"vercel[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T20:46:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Install and configure Vercel Web Analytics (#20)\n\n## Vercel Web Analytics Installation\n\nSuccessfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the portfolio site.\n\n### Changes Made\n\n**1. Installed Package**\n- Added `@vercel/analytics` version ^2.0.1 to project dependencies\n- Used pnpm package manager (project''s configured package manager)\n\n**2. Modified Files**\n\n**apps/web/package.json**\n- Added `@vercel/analytics` to dependencies\n\n**apps/web/src/App.tsx**\n- Imported `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/react`\n- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the app structure, right after the Routes and within the SmoothScrollProvider\n\n**pnpm-lock.yaml**\n- Updated with new dependency resolution for @vercel/analytics and its dependencies\n\n### Implementation Details\n\nFollowing the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I identified this as a **React + Vite** project and implemented the framework-specific integration:\n\n1. **Framework Detection**: Analyzed project structure and found it uses React with Vite as the build tool\n2. **Installation**: Used `pnpm add @vercel/analytics` to install the package\n3. **Integration**: Added the `<Analytics />` component to the App component following React/Vite best practices\n4. **Placement**: Positioned the Analytics component at the root level inside SmoothScrollProvider to track all page views across the entire application\n\n### Verification Completed\n\n✅ **TypeScript type checking** - Passed with no errors\n✅ **ESLint** - No linting errors introduced\n✅ **Production build** - Successfully built with vite (1,008.29 kB bundle)\n✅ **Tests** - All tests passed\n\n### Next Steps\n\nAfter deployment to Vercel:\n1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Analytics)\n2. Deploy the application to activate analytics tracking\n3. Verify analytics data collection by checking the browser''s Network tab for requests to the analytics endpoint\n4. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard after sufficient traffic accumulation\n\n### Notes\n\n- The Analytics component is lightweight and does not impact performance\n- No additional configuration is required for basic page view tracking\n- The component works automatically in production when deployed to Vercel\n- No build artifacts (dist/) were staged as they are properly excluded by .gitignore\n\nCo-authored-by: Vercel <vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c7e67b41c87c6cddab9846d047c334ad9df083e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/im-kaushal/portfolio-site/git/trees/c7e67b41c87c6cddab9846d047c334ad9df083e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/im-kaushal/portfolio-site/git/commits/f0952ce1dd017e1902d15a9d827bc6959d2bbab1","verification":{"payload":"tree c7e67b41c87c6cddab9846d047c334ad9df083e1\nparent 0a020162ef97aa4b87b0ab47a8d0cdcea64c1089\nauthor vercel[bot] <35613825+vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790714796 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790714796 +0530\n\nInstall and configure Vercel Web Analytics (#20)\n\n## Vercel Web Analytics Installation\n\nSuccessfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the portfolio site.\n\n### Changes Made\n\n**1. Installed Package**\n- Added `@vercel/analytics` version ^2.0.1 to project dependencies\n- Used pnpm package manager (project''s configured package manager)\n\n**2. Modified Files**\n\n**apps/web/package.json**\n- Added `@vercel/analytics` to dependencies\n\n**apps/web/src/App.tsx**\n- Imported `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/react`\n- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the app structure, right after the Routes and within the SmoothScrollProvider\n\n**pnpm-lock.yaml**\n- Updated with new dependency resolution for @vercel/analytics and its dependencies\n\n### Implementation Details\n\nFollowing the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I identified this as a **React + Vite** project and implemented the framework-specific integration:\n\n1. **Framework Detection**: Analyzed project structure and found it uses React with Vite as the build tool\n2. **Installation**: Used `pnpm add @vercel/analytics` to install the package\n3. **Integration**: Added the `<Analytics />` component to the App component following React/Vite best practices\n4. **Placement**: Positioned the Analytics component at the root level inside SmoothScrollProvider to track all page views across the entire application\n\n### Verification Completed\n\n✅ **TypeScript type checking** - Passed with no errors\n✅ **ESLint** - No linting errors introduced\n✅ **Production build** - Successfully built with vite (1,008.29 kB bundle)\n✅ **Tests** - All tests passed\n\n### Next Steps\n\nAfter deployment to Vercel:\n1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Analytics)\n2. Deploy the application to activate analytics tracking\n3. Verify analytics data collection by checking the browser''s Network tab for requests to the analytics endpoint\n4. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard after sufficient traffic accumulation\n\n### Notes\n\n- The Analytics component is lightweight and does not impact performance\n- No additional configuration is required for basic page view tracking\n- The component works automatically in production when deployed to Vercel\n- No build artifacts (dist/) were staged as they are properly excluded by .gitignore\n\nCo-authored-by: Vercel <vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvCOsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxH0QAAr3EsAX2BdAEAFKaNJVeCUa\nGnmkZm4Jz/t33lBf6wX5ccoSW5pNtYZRK9LWVbz2Reto/sttTCvALTwe1iMTco9i\nBwB/jYBy1a5IfDsiYu46tphP7j0pWRcI5o6vRpb9hWMTFKy3RHiJ4HEgnDLURKAl\nFVjNFReJmCzjahLF0IjN1pwEaTw8hNr/ynn4US/9ioE+gcCWumhO2fmgS6Z8mxru\nYk47jZ3jVdgW00Fw3l6R9NnR73+Q+S9Dx2fnnbpyt1DWA1LeL01uGC5RVN70LqlJ\npvxYWXfMYahWLEdnGg1ZDVZ4RzHJBx6i+jdG1BRG24mIQPS6GkLi4jVisL5QSoN0\nzcWFFhmItACGPGENiW+jB1ffRQ0Ewr