e8dc278d37613a8af62488e47d689bbe51bbcf49"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/5215e5c02bab2f0936002f657e2a1fb74fffa661","sha":"5215e5c02bab2f0936002f657e2a1fb74fffa661","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/5215e5c02bab2f0936002f657e2a1fb74fffa661"}],"sha":"f52757d411aa643f6e378990eb0e5fbc6e77c235","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/f52757d411aa643f6e378990eb0e5fbc6e77c235"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/5215e5c02bab2f0936002f657e2a1fb74fffa661/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T16:15:01Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T16:15:01Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(wallet): make the connection actually completable, and close three more findings\n\nReview on PR #150 found four defects in the page-provider increment. All four\nwere real.\n\nThe connection could never complete (P1). vault.create and vault.unlock had no\ncaller anywhere in the package, only their handlers in background.ts, so\nunlockedPayload was never assigned, grantedAccounts always returned nothing, and\nevery eth_requestAccounts failed however the provider and the site grant were\nset up. The PR claimed connection worked; it did not. That is the fault\nACCEPTANCE.md section 3 names, a surface that renders but cannot execute its\nfunction, and shipping the provider is what made the missing unlock path\nload-bearing.\n\nThe popup now creates and unlocks the vault. The decision is extracted to\nvault-form.ts so it can be tested rather than living in DOM handlers: an\nexisting vault is only ever opened and never recreated over its stored\ndescriptors, a password below the vault''s own minimum is refused before the\nworker is asked, and creation requires a well-formed address. No key material is\ninvolved; a descriptor records which address an approved external signer holds.\n\nThe provider never reached an already-open tab (P1). registerContentScripts\ncovers later document loads only, so enabling a site did nothing until a reload\nnobody had asked for. enableSite now injects both worlds into the tab the popup\nnames, after checking that tab is still on the granted origin, because injection\nis per tab and a tab may have navigated away. A failed injection leaves the\nregistration and the grant standing rather than undoing them.\n\nGrant restoration was not awaited (P2). Chrome restarts the MV3 worker to\ndeliver an event, so a request could reach routeProviderRequest before the\nstorage read finished: the first call from an enabled site refused as\nunauthorized, a retry succeeding. That is the worst shape a permission check can\ntake. The promise is now held and awaited by every handler that reads a grant.\n\nAn expired grant kept its host permission (P2). Expiry dropped the grant and\nunregistered its scripts but left the optional host permission in place, so an\norigin absent from the popup''s list stayed authorized indefinitely.\nrestoreSiteAccess now hands back host access for every origin whose grants have\nall expired, as disable already did, while keeping it for an origin that is\nexpired and granted again.\n\nBoth structural fixes verified by mutation: removing the open-tab injection\nfails only \"runs the provider in the tab that is already open\", and removing the\nexpired-grant revocation fails only \"hands back the host permission of a grant\nthat expired\".\n\nwallet-extension tests 24 to 34 across 6 files. Web 639 in 48 files, Go\ngofmt/vet/test ./..., format:check, lint, typecheck, extension build with\nprovider.js and bridge.js still free of module syntax, security:secrets across\n602 files, agent:test 109/109. The awaited restoration and the popup DOM wiring\nare verified by inspection; neither has a test harness here. Browser-loaded\nexecution against a live page remains not run.\n\ndocs/STATUS.md evidence only - counts, 58 rows and gates unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"904bf9a38ccf9397c54e82816085498df894a206","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/trees/904bf9a38ccf9397c54e82816085498df894a206"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/commits/5215e5c02bab2f0936002f657e2a1fb74fffa661","verification":{"payload":"tree 904bf9a38ccf9397c54e82816085498df894a206\nparent 29d23c16fc5fc51d9f3bb4f276f6e25d7b4a1f66\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1791476101 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1791476101 +0000\n\nfix(wallet): make the connection actually completable, and close three more findings\n\nReview on PR #150 found four defects in the page-provider increment. All four\nwere real.\n\nThe connection could never complete (P1). vault.create and vault.unlock had no\ncaller anywhere in the package, only their handlers in background.ts, so\nunlockedPayload was never assigned, grantedAccounts always returned nothing, and\nevery eth_requestAccounts failed however the provider and the site grant were\nset up. The PR claimed connection worked; it did not. That is the fault\nACCEPTANCE.md section 3 names, a surface that renders but cannot execute its\nfunction, and shipping the provider is what made the missing unlock path\nload-bearing.\n\nThe popup now creates and unlocks the vault. The decision is extracted to\nvault-form.ts so it can be tested rather than living in DOM handlers: an\nexisting vault is only ever opened and never recreated over its stored\ndescriptors, a password below the vault''s own minimum is refused before the\nworker is asked, and creation requires a well-formed address. No key material is\ninvolved; a descriptor records which address an approved external signer holds.\n\nThe provider never reached an already-open tab (P1). registerContentScripts\ncovers later document loads only, so enabling a site did nothing until a reload\nnobody had asked for. enableSite now injects both worlds into the tab the popup\nnames, after checking that tab is still on the granted origin, because injection\nis per tab and a tab may have navigated away. A failed injection leaves the\nregistration and the grant standing rather than undoing them.\n\nGrant restoration was not awaited (P2). Chrome restarts the MV3 worker to\ndeliver an event, so a request could reach routeProviderRequest before the\nstorage read finished: the first call from an enabled site refused as\nunauthorized, a retry succeeding. That is the worst shape a permission check can\ntake. The promise is now held and awaited by every handler that reads a grant.\n\nAn expired grant kept its host permission (P2). Expiry dropped the grant and\nunregistered its scripts but left the optional host permission in place, so an\norigin absent from the popup''s list stayed authorized indefinitely.\nrestoreSiteAccess now hands back host access for every origin whose grants have\nall expired, as disable already did, while keeping it for an origin that is\nexpired and granted again.\n\nBoth structural fixes verified by mutation: removing the open-tab injection\nfails only \"runs the provider in the tab that is already open\", and removing the\nexpired-grant revocation fails only \"hands back the host permission of a grant\nthat expired\".\n\nwallet-extension tests 24 to 34 across 6 files. Web 639 in 48 files, Go\ngofmt/vet/test ./..., format:check, lint, typecheck, extension build with\nprovider.js and bridge.js still free of module syntax, security:secrets across\n602 files, agent:test 109/109. The awaited restoration and the popup DOM wiring\nare verified by inspection; neither has a test harness here. Browser-loaded\nexecution against a live page remains not run.\n\ndocs/STATUS.md evidence only - counts, 58 rows and gates unchanged.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLXUWDHh\nSQUl4aqBuejl/gCodN98CJvHkSiqlVkssg1F6kQ7fmSsnHmkD4DbLnPPgJ9AqBn6n0/x1xtgJ1s+\nFg0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T16:16:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/5215e5c02bab2f0936002f657e2a1fb74fffa661","node_id":"C_kwDOT8pe1toAKDUyMTVlNWMwMmJhYjJmMDkzNjAwMmY2NTdlMmExZmI3NGZmZmE2NjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/29d23c16fc5fc51d9f3bb4f276f6e25d7b4a1f66","sha":"29d23c16fc5fc51d9f3bb4f276f6e25d7b4a1f66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/29d23c16fc5fc51d9f3bb4f276f6e25d7b4a1f66"}],"sha":"5215e5c02bab2f0936002f657e2a1fb74fffa661","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/5215e5c02bab2f0936002f657e2a1fb74fffa661"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/29d23c16fc5fc51d9f3bb4f276f6e25d7b4a1f66/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T16:02:39Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T16:02:39Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(config): remove two hardcoded port defaults\n\nAGENTS.md, \"Current deployment execution and port allocation\", already requires\nthat a port not be hardcoded in product behaviour and that configured public\nURLs carry scheme, domain, port and entry path. Two places in the code\ncontradicted that, so this implements the existing rule rather than adding one.\n\napps/web/src/app/api/orders/route.ts supplied the default HTTPS port when\nARTFI_WEB_URL named none, accepting the bare host together with that implied\nport and rejecting every other. A deployment serving on a selected port\nanswered 403 on order publication with nothing naming the cause, and a\nport-less configuration silently pinned the deployment to the default port. The\nconfigured authority is now compared exactly as configured.\n\napps/api/internal/httpapi/handler.go substituted http://localhost:3000 for an\nunset ARTFI_WEB_ORIGIN. In a deployment that allowed a loopback origin nobody\nuses and blocked the configured one, with no error naming the cause: every\nbrowser call failed CORS while the service looked healthy. An unset origin now\nsends no Access-Control-Allow-Origin header at all, because an empty header is\nstill a header and reads as deliberate.\n\nTwo further exact-match checks share the same configured value, the session\norigin binding in user_auth.go and user-auth.ts with operator-auth.ts, so\nARTFI_WEB_URL and ARTFI_WEB_ORIGIN must match the browser-visible origin\nincluding its port. No port value is written in the repository.\n\nPort 443 examples removed from native-order-route.test.ts and\nxiongan-wallet.test.ts, with regressions both ways: an authority that names a\nport accepts only that port, one that names none matches no ported Host. A port\nwhose digits merely contain 443, such as 18443, is a different port and is left\nalone.\n\nLocal on the rebased tree: Web 639 tests in 48 files, wallet-extension 24, Go\ngofmt/vet/test ./..., format:check, lint, typecheck, security:secrets across 600\nfiles, agent:test 109/109. docs/STATUS.md evidence only - counts, 58 rows and\ngates unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"59405b0e4f70d5ea144a39ee6c3321b3801d49fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/trees/59405b0e4f70d5ea144a39ee6c3321b3801d49fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/commits/29d23c16fc5fc51d9f3bb4f276f6e25d7b4a1f66","verification":{"payload":"tree 59405b0e4f70d5ea144a39ee6c3321b3801d49fd\nparent a362d9ed21b4788b5bc8def4c492a5d30b83f1ee\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1791475359 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1791475359 +0000\n\nfix(config): remove two hardcoded port defaults\n\nAGENTS.md, \"Current deployment execution and port allocation\", already requires\nthat a port not be hardcoded in product behaviour and that configured public\nURLs carry scheme, domain, port and entry path. Two places in the code\ncontradicted that, so this implements the existing rule rather than adding one.\n\napps/web/src/app/api/orders/route.ts supplied the default HTTPS port when\nARTFI_WEB_URL named none, accepting the bare host together with that implied\nport and rejecting every other. A deployment serving on a selected port\nanswered 403 on order publication with nothing naming the cause, and a\nport-less configuration silently pinned the deployment to the default port. The\nconfigured authority is now compared exactly as configured.\n\napps/api/internal/httpapi/handler.go substituted http://localhost:3000 for an\nunset ARTFI_WEB_ORIGIN. In a deployment that allowed a loopback origin nobody\nuses and blocked the configured one, with no error naming the cause: every\nbrowser call failed CORS while the service looked healthy. An unset origin now\nsends no Access-Control-Allow-Origin header at all, because an empty header is\nstill a header and reads as deliberate.\n\nTwo further exact-match checks share the same configured value, the session\norigin binding in user_auth.go and user-auth.ts with operator-auth.ts, so\nARTFI_WEB_URL and ARTFI_WEB_ORIGIN must match the browser-visible origin\nincluding its port. No port value is written in the repository.\n\nPort 443 examples removed from native-order-route.test.ts and\nxiongan-wallet.test.ts, with regressions both ways: an authority that names a\nport accepts only that port, one that names none matches no ported Host. A port\nwhose digits merely contain 443, such as 18443, is a different port and is left\nalone.\n\nLocal on the rebased tree: Web 639 tests in 48 files, wallet-extension 24, Go\ngofmt/vet/test ./..., format:check, lint, typecheck, security:secrets across 600\nfiles, agent:test 109/109. docs/STATUS.md evidence only - counts, 58 rows and\ngates unchanged.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLKXMd6H\ne1YRR4afo/RLJJPyvnVeCPR5dqQs/S6szqvPFxO4tBD6T472tGYRK5AU6VJajtBjOl0Xj29UtSCi\n5gU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T16:02:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/29d23c16fc5fc51d9f3bb4f276f6e25d7b4a1f66","node_id":"C_kwDOT8pe1toAKDI5ZDIzYzE2ZmM1ZmM1MWQ5ZjNiYjRmMjc2ZjZlMjVkN2I0YTFmNjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/a362d9ed21b4788b5bc8def4c492a5d30b83f1ee","sha":"a362d9ed21b4788b5bc8def4c492a5d30b83f1ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/a362d9ed21b4788b5bc8def4c492a5d30b83f1ee"}],"sha":"29d23c16fc5fc51d9f3bb4f276f6e25d7b4a1f66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/29d23c16fc5fc51d9f3bb4f276f6e25d7b4a1f66"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/a362d9ed21b4788b5bc8def4c492a5d30b83f1ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T19:57:12Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T15:56:52Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(wallet): announce an EIP-6963 provider so ArtFi can connect\n\nArtFi and the wallet could not connect in production. The deployment was not at\nfault: io.artcch.com answers over HTTPS on the canonical port with HSTS, and\n/api/health reported status ok on chain 560048 at build 033dba4. The cause was a\nmissing protocol.\n\nArtFi''s web app registers exactly one connector, RainbowKit''s injectedWallet,\nwith no WalletConnect connector and an empty projectId. That connector requires\nan EIP-6963 announcement inside ArtFi''s own origin, and nothing in the ecosystem\nmade one. The Xiongan DApp is a separate web origin and exposes no cross-origin\nprovider. This repository''s own extension declared only background and action:\nno content script, no dynamic injection, no page-facing surface at all, so\npermissions.ts and transactions.ts had modelled per-origin EIP-1193 grants and\nHoodi-only confirmation that no page could ever reach.\n\nThis adds the missing half. provider.ts runs in the page''s world and announces\nthe provider; bridge.ts relays from the isolated world, which is the only world\nthat may speak to the service worker; rpc.ts answers.\n\nThe origin is never taken from the page. It arrives as the browser''s\nsender.origin, because a page that could name its own origin could borrow\nanother site''s grant. A regression covers that: a grant for one origin leaves\nanother origin with no accounts.\n\nSigning stays where it was. The vault holds account descriptors and no key\nmaterial, and the stated boundary is that an approved hardware or WalletConnect\nadapter is the only signer. ExternalSigner has no implementation, so all eight\nsigning aliases are refused by name rather than answered with something that\nresembles a signature. eth_chainId, eth_accounts and eth_requestAccounts are\nanswered, so connection works and signing says why it does not.\n\nThree choices worth stating. eth_chainId is answered before any grant, because\nwagmi reads it while building the connector and refusing it would deadlock the\nconnection the grant enables. eth_accounts returns an empty list for an\nunenabled site, which is what EIP-1193 means by not connected; throwing would\nmake every page load look like a broken wallet. eth_requestAccounts refuses an\nunenabled origin, because a page must not authorize itself.\n\nHost access stays per-origin and opt-in, which the extension''s design already\nrequired. The page scripts are registered at run time for one origin after the\nperson enables it in the popup, rather than declared against every HTTPS site;\ndisabling unregisters them and hands the host permission back. Grants are\npersisted and rehydrated at startup because registered scripts outlive the\nservice worker while in-memory grants do not, and the two drifting apart would\nleave a page meeting a provider that disowns its grant. The vault stays\nmemory-only. window.ethereum is left untouched, so other wallets still work.\n\nwallet-extension tests go from 6 to 24. Local: extension typecheck and build,\nrepository format:check, lint, typecheck, security:secrets across 550 files, and\nagent:test. The built provider.js and bridge.js were checked to contain no\nmodule syntax, which a script registered through chrome.scripting requires.\n\nBrowser-loaded extension execution against a live page was not run here and\nremains required evidence, with current-head CI.\n\nA stale Sepolia claim in the manifest description, popup and README is corrected\nto Hoodi 560048, which transactions.ts already enforced.\n\ndocs/STATUS.md gains evidence only: no status value, count, gate or row changes.","tree":{"sha":"d2862805b0815a96e09d9aa407ab6d9ccf9d567f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/trees/d2862805b0815a96e09d9aa407ab6d9ccf9d567f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/commits/a362d9ed21b4788b5bc8def4c492a5d30b83f1ee","verification":{"payload":"tree d2862805b0815a96e09d9aa407ab6d9ccf9d567f\nparent e8dc278d37613a8af62488e47d689bbe51bbcf49\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1791057432 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1791475012 +0000\n\nfeat(wallet): announce an EIP-6963 provider so ArtFi can connect\n\nArtFi and the wallet could not connect in production. The deployment was not at\nfault: io.artcch.com answers over HTTPS on the canonical port with HSTS, and\n/api/health reported status ok on chain 560048 at build 033dba4. The cause was a\nmissing protocol.\n\nArtFi''s web app registers exactly one connector, RainbowKit''s injectedWallet,\nwith no WalletConnect connector and an empty projectId. That connector requires\nan EIP-6963 announcement inside ArtFi''s own origin, and nothing in the ecosystem\nmade one. The Xiongan DApp is a separate web origin and exposes no cross-origin\nprovider. This repository''s own extension declared only background and action:\nno content script, no dynamic injection, no page-facing surface at all, so\npermissions.ts and transactions.ts had modelled per-origin EIP-1193 grants and\nHoodi-only confirmation that no page could ever reach.\n\nThis adds the missing half. provider.ts runs in the page''s world and announces\nthe provider; bridge.ts relays from the isolated world, which is the only world\nthat may speak to the service worker; rpc.ts answers.\n\nThe origin is never taken from the page. It arrives as the browser''s\nsender.origin, because a page that could name its own origin could borrow\nanother site''s grant. A regression covers that: a grant for one origin leaves\nanother origin with no accounts.\n\nSigning stays where it was. The vault holds account descriptors and no key\nmaterial, and the stated boundary is that an approved hardware or WalletConnect\nadapter is the only signer. ExternalSigner has no implementation, so all eight\nsigning aliases are refused by name rather than answered with something that\nresembles a signature. eth_chainId, eth_accounts and eth_requestAccounts are\nanswered, so connection works and signing says why it does not.\n\nThree choices worth stating. eth_chainId is answered before any grant, because\nwagmi reads it while building the connector and refusing it would deadlock the\nconnection the grant enables. eth_accounts returns an empty list for an\nunenabled site, which is what EIP-1193 means by not connected; throwing would\nmake every page load look like a broken wallet. eth_requestAccounts refuses an\nunenabled origin, because a page must not authorize itself.\n\nHost access stays per-origin and opt-in, which the extension''s design already\nrequired. The page scripts are registered at run time for one origin after the\nperson enables it in the popup, rather than declared against every HTTPS site;\ndisabling unregisters them and hands the host permission back. Grants are\npersisted and rehydrated at startup because registered scripts outlive the\nservice worker while in-memory grants do not, and the two drifting apart would\nleave a page meeting a provider that disowns its grant. The vault stays\nmemory-only. window.ethereum is left untouched, so other wallets still work.\n\nwallet-extension tests go from 6 to 24. Local: extension typecheck and build,\nrepository format:check, lint, typecheck, security:secrets across 550 files, and\nagent:test. The built provider.js and bridge.js were checked to contain no\nmodule syntax, which a script registered through chrome.scripting requires.\n\nBrowser-loaded extension execution against a live page was not run here and\nremains required evidence, with current-head CI.\n\nA stale Sepolia claim in the manifest description, popup and README is corrected\nto Hoodi 560048, which transactions.ts already enforced.\n\ndocs/STATUS.md gains evidence only: no status value, count, gate or row changes.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMzaa82y\nodJ46bQrnHTg4wF5x36kjFMOaRf2Kchq9zm+6EfX7mAsWgdrParu6Q8qPnfi/cz6mJB1KyWKIQyg\ntQY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T16:02:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/a362d9ed21b4788b5bc8def4c492a5d30b83f1ee","node_id":"C_kwDOT8pe1toAKGEzNjJkOWVkMjFiNDc4OGI1YmM4ZGVmNGM0OTJhNWQzMGI4M2YxZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/e8dc278d37613a8af62488e47d689bbe51bbcf49","sha":"e8dc278d37613a8af62488e47d689bbe51bbcf49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/e8dc278d37613a8af62488e47d689bbe51bbcf49"}],"sha":"a362d9ed21b4788b5bc8def4c492a5d30b83f1ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/a362d9ed21b4788b5bc8def4c492a5d30b83f1ee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287057209?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Gira