hnology","id":287057209,"login":"GiraffeTechnology","node_id":"U_kgDOERwlOQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/bde3b206909bb8d7965adcf558c4cd32c7472398/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:22:04Z","email":"abcdyi2021@gmail.com","name":"Michael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T16:22:04Z","email":"abcdyi2021@gmail.com","name":"Michael"},"message":"fix(ci): adapt Next lint plugins to ESLint 10 rule APIs\n\nUse official @eslint/compat 2.1.1 fixupConfigRules without disabling\nrules or downgrading ESLint. Add the exact dependency with pnpm 11.22.0.\nPreserve every existing importer, package, snapshot and libc selector.\nAddresses quality run 34681466952 getFilename failure.\nRuntime lint and tests remain pending independent execution.","tree":{"sha":"53f9c31070589ab51ad36bace0c46d64dc49b830","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/trees/53f9c31070589ab51ad36bace0c46d64dc49b830"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/commits/bde3b206909bb8d7965adcf558c4cd32c7472398","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287057209?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology","id":287057209,"login":"GiraffeTechnology","node_id":"U_kgDOERwlOQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiraffeTechnology","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/bde3b206909bb8d7965adcf558c4cd32c7472398","node_id":"C_kwDOT8pe1toAKGJkZTNiMjA2OTA5YmI4ZDc5NjVhZGNmNTU4YzRjZDMyYzc0NzIzOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/02a2e61a2bf1cb86b470cca700f647b75d25a1a1","sha":"02a2e61a2bf1cb86b470cca700f647b75d25a1a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/02a2e61a2bf1cb86b470cca700f647b75d25a1a1"}],"sha":"bde3b206909bb8d7965adcf558c4cd32c7472398","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/bde3b206909bb8d7965adcf558c4cd32c7472398"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/511abd0baf3d1bb0d313bfa16787cd2527244124/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:33:25Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:33:25Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(market): make the mirrored activity history walkable, and give it a screen\n\n`AGENTS.md`''s S-XM checkpoint names this as the slice after PR #114''s findings:\ncomplete cursor-paginated activity history in API, OpenAPI, client and UI. Two\nthings were wrong with `/v1/market/activity`. It served a `limit` alone, capped\nat 100, so the most any reader could see was the hundred most recent events\nwhile the rest of the history sat in the mirror unreachable. And no screen\nreached it at all, which `PRD.md` §3.2 counts as progress rather than a\nhandover.\n\nKeyset, not offset. Rows arrive continuously, and offset paging over a feed that\ngrows at its head skips and repeats rows as it walks — the reader would be told\na complete history while silently missing events. The cursor is the ordering\ntuple of the last row served, (event_timestamp, received_at, event_id)\ndescending; the first two are the sort the handler already used and neither is\nunique, so the primary key breaks the tie and makes the order strict. The\nexisting idx_external_market_activity covers the seek, and the predicate is\nwritten as the expanded comparison rather than MySQL''s row-value form because\nthe row-value syntax does not use that index. One row beyond the page decides\nwhether another page exists and is not served, so a client is never told there\nis more when there is not.\n\nThe end is stated, never inferred. `nextCursor` is absent once the history has\nended; a short page is not the end, since the server may return fewer rows and\nstill have more.\n\nA cursor is a position in a public read-only feed, not an authority. It is\nopaque by encoding rather than by secrecy, carries a version tag, and every\nfield is re-validated on the way in — nothing reaches a query but a timestamp\npair and a 64-character hex id. One this endpoint did not issue is refused with\n400 rather than rounded to the head: silently restarting would serve the newest\npage to a reader who asked for an older one, with nothing to tell them.\n\n`/market/activity` is the screen, reachable from navigation on desktop and\nmobile, built from the shared market classes so a re-skin costs stylesheet work\nrather than rebuilt components. Each row carries source, event type, chain,\ncollection, token, order, price, observed time, freshness and the venue link the\nsource reported — re-validated, never constructed (XM.5). An unreachable mirror\nsays so and does not render the empty state: \"the mirror has observed no\nactivity\" would be a claim about the market made from a failed request, and the\ntwo are opposite statements to a reader deciding whether a market is quiet or\nbroken.\n\nWeb 186/186, Playwright 156 passed with 2 intentional skips across desktop and\nmobile, Forge 136/136, Go gofmt/vet/test -race, OpenAPI regenerated with no\ndrift beyond the documented change, and the format, lint, typecheck, build,\nsecurity, agent, chain-consistency and charity verifier gates. The integration\ntest now walks the whole history one event at a time and asserts each is served\nexactly once; it needs MySQL and did not run here.\n\nNo status value moves: VERIFIED 7, IMPLEMENTED-NOT-VERIFIED 43, PENDING-GATE 5,\nBLOCKED 5, NOT-IMPLEMENTED 47, OUT-OF-SCOPE 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE","tree":{"sha":"9bcd538b2674be8d574342813cc68d1b3c2a10a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/trees/9bcd538b2674be8d574342813cc68d1b3c2a10a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/commits/511abd0baf3d1bb0d313bfa16787cd2527244124","verification":{"payload":"tree 9bcd538b2674be8d574342813cc68d1b3c2a10a3\nparent e2491b0f8e21f2b62bbf37780f06257c319ff0b0\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790696005 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790696005 +0000\n\nfeat(market): make the mirrored activity history walkable, and give it a screen\n\n`AGENTS.md`''s S-XM checkpoint names this as the slice after PR #114''s findings:\ncomplete cursor-paginated activity history in API, OpenAPI, client and UI. Two\nthings were wrong with `/v1/market/activity`. It served a `limit` alone, capped\nat 100, so the most any reader could see was the hundred most recent events\nwhile the rest of the history sat in the mirror unreachable. And no screen\nreached it at all, which `PRD.md` §3.2 counts as progress rather than a\nhandover.\n\nKeyset, not offset. Rows arrive continuously, and offset paging over a feed that\ngrows at its head skips and repeats rows as it walks — the reader would be told\na complete history while silently missing events. The cursor is the ordering\ntuple of the last row served, (event_timestamp, received_at, event_id)\ndescending; the first two are the sort the handler already used and neither is\nunique, so the primary key breaks the tie and makes the order strict. The\nexisting idx_external_market_activity covers the seek, and the predicate is\nwritten as the expanded comparison rather than MySQL''s row-value form because\nthe row-value syntax does not use that index. One row beyond the page decides\nwhether another page exists and is not served, so a client is never told there\nis more when there is not.\n\nThe end is stated, never inferred. `nextCursor` is absent once the history has\nended; a short page is not the end, since the server may return fewer rows and\nstill have more.\n\nA cursor is a position in a public read-only feed, not an authority. It is\nopaque by encoding rather than by secrecy, carries a version tag, and every\nfield is re-validated on the way in — nothing reaches a query but a timestamp\npair and a 64-character hex id. One this endpoint did not issue is refused with\n400 rather than rounded to the head: silently restarting would serve the newest\npage to a reader who asked for an older one, with nothing to tell them.\n\n`/market/activity` is the screen, reachable from navigation on desktop and\nmobile, built from the shared market classes so a re-skin costs stylesheet work\nrather than rebuilt components. Each row carries source, event type, chain,\ncollection, token, order, price, observed time, freshness and the venue link the\nsource reported — re-validated, never constructed (XM.5). An unreachable mirror\nsays so and does not render the empty state: \"the mirror has observed no\nactivity\" would be a claim about the market made from a failed request, and the\ntwo are opposite statements to a reader deciding whether a market is quiet or\nbroken.\n\nWeb 186/186, Playwright 156 passed with 2 intentional skips across desktop and\nmobile, Forge 136/136, Go gofmt/vet/test -race, OpenAPI regenerated with no\ndrift beyond the documented change, and the format, lint, typecheck, build,\nsecurity, agent, chain-consistency and charity verifier gates. The integration\ntest now walks the whole history one event at a time and asserts each is served\nexactly once; it needs MySQL and did not run here.\n\nNo status value moves: VERIFIED 7, IMPLEMENTED-NOT-VERIFIED 43, PENDING-GATE 5,\nBLOCKED 5, NOT-IMPLEMENTED 47, OUT-OF-SCOPE 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFPcEI9V\nBX22vq7KuujCJ7r6djAvSbNOITf51KOJHw8wWz/3ZxTWSf0UIEXvdM2wcAETsc2ZaIePWzedJ9aX\nFgs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T15:33:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/511abd0baf3d1bb0d313bfa16787cd2527244124","node_id":"C_kwDOT8pe1toAKDUxMWFiZDBiYWYzZDFiYjBkMzEzYmZhMTY3ODdjZDI1MjcyNDQxMjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/e2491b0f8e21f2b62bbf37780f06257c319ff0b0","sha":"e2491b0f8e21f2b62bbf37780f06257c319ff0b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/e2491b0f8e21f2b62bbf37780f06257c319ff0b0"}],"sha":"511abd0baf3d1bb0d313bfa16787cd2527244124","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/511abd0baf3d1bb0d313bfa16787cd2527244124"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/e2491b0f8e21f2b62bbf37780f06257c319ff0b0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:25:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:25:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs: record the four review findings and their fixes\n\nReview on PR #127 found four defects in the two entries above it, all real and\nall fixed at 1857c5e. Two of those entries were too generous when written — one\ndescribed a surface as showing \"the token allowlist\" while it read only the asset\nside, and the other introduced the environment fallback that let a deployment\nappear on every catalog page at once. This entry corrects them rather than\nediting them.\n\nNo count or status moves: VERIFIED 7, IMPLEMENTED-NOT-VERIFIED 43,\nPENDING-GATE 5, BLOCKED 5, NOT-IMPLEMENTED 47, OUT-OF-SCOPE 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE","tree":{"sha":"99ce8184d2db30cda03bb5dcc23736ab6240e4e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/trees/99ce8184d2db30cda03bb5dcc23736ab6240e4e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/commits/e2491b0f8e21f2b62bbf37780f06257c319ff0b0","verification":{"payload":"tree 99ce8184d2db30cda03bb5dcc23736ab6240e4e4\nparent 1857c5eb43dffc9e9f3895472e9299891bd8cf7d\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790666705 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790666705 +0000\n\ndocs: record the four review findings and their fixes\n\nReview on PR #127 found four defects in the two entries above it, all real and\nall fixed at 1857c5e. Two of those entries were too generous when written — one\ndescribed a surface as showing \"the token allowlist\" while it read only the asset\nside, and the other introduced the environment fallback that let a deployment\nappear on every catalog page at once. This entry corrects them rather than\nediting them.\n\nNo count or status moves: VERIFIED 7, IMPLEMENTED-NOT-VERIFIED 43,\nPENDING-GATE 5, BLOCKED 5, NOT-IMPLEMENTED 47, OUT-OF-SCOPE 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ8y9jc5\nvqbpTXRrtEfEUsmHMLYtPl/xES5REWkOS83NZEiwqEqAKJvnflwD5tTmovpvMi4DJpysBFo/Hc4E\nFws=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T07:25:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/e2491b0f8e21f2b62bbf37780f06257c319ff0b0","node_id":"C_kwDOT8pe1toAKGUyNDkxYjBmOGUyMWYyYjYyYmJmMzc3ODBmMDYyNTdjMzE5ZmYwYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/1857c5eb43dffc9e9f3895472e9299891bd8cf7d","sha":"1857c5eb43dffc9e9f3895472e9299891bd8cf7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/1857c5eb43dffc9e9f3895472e9299891bd8cf7d"}],"sha":"e2491b0f8e21f2b62bbf37780f06257c319ff0b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/e2491b0f8e21f2b62bbf37780f06257c319ff0b0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/1857c5eb43dffc9e9f3895472e9299891bd8cf7d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:23:37Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:23:37Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(web): address four review findings on the settlement surfaces\n\n**A deployment belongs to one page, not to all of them** (P1). `AssetDetail` is\nshared by every slug in `lib/catalog.ts` — six invented artworks that map to no\ndeployed token — and both settlement surfaces read their contract from the\nenvironment with no identifier from the artwork. Once configured, every catalog\ndetail page would have offered the same real holding, approval and signing\nsurface beneath a different artwork''s title, so a holder could authorize a sale\nof an asset the page did not describe. That is a fixture dressed as live data\n(`AGENTS.md` §5, `ACCEPTANCE.md` §3) and a signature over terms the signer did\nnot mean.\n\nA deployment now names the one slug it belongs to. `assetDeploymentBinding`\ndecides which of three things is true for a page — bound here, deployed and\nbelonging elsewhere, or nothing deployed — and an unnamed deployment binds\nnowhere, so every route but the named one stays inert and says which case it is.\n\n**The zero address is not a party or a token** (P2). A blank payment-token field\nbecame `0x00…0`, which `isAddress` accepts; the market does not — it refuses to\nallowlist that token and refuses to fill against it. The form produced and\ndisplayed a signed authorization that could never settle anywhere. A blank field\nnow stays blank and surfaces the existing `payment-token-missing` problem before\nsigning, and both validators reject the zero address for the seller, the asset or\ncollection, and the payment token, while keeping it for the buyer field, where it\nmeans \"anyone may fill\".\n\n**Approve only a payment token confirmed allowlisted** (P1). The fill path sent\nthe buyer''s ERC-20 approval without checking the pasted intent''s payment token,\nthough the ABI already exposed `allowedPaymentToken`. For a token that was never\nallowlisted, or whose permission was withdrawn after signing, the buyer paid for\nan approval and left a live allowance behind for a fill that then reverted. The\nstanding is read and the approval blocked before it is requested, and an unread\nstanding does not pass: waiting costs a retry, guessing costs a stranded\nallowance.\n\n**Page through to the end for a charity edition''s venue** (P2). The venue lookup\nread only page one of `/v1/market/assets`, whose page size caps at 100. Past that\nmany mirrored token ids an edition on a later page reported as having no observed\nmarketplace activity and silently lost its venue link while a durable record\nexisted. `findCharityVenueRecord` walks until it finds the edition, a page comes\nback empty, or everything `total` promised has been seen.\n\nFour regressions, each verified by mutation: restoring the previous behaviour\nmakes that test fail and no other. The binding and the pagination were extracted\nso the decisions are testable rather than locked inside a component.\n\nWeb 176/176, Playwright 142 passed with 2 intentional skips across desktop and\nmobile, Forge 136/136, gofmt/go vet/go test -race, format, lint, typecheck,\nbuild, and the security, agent, chain-consistency, release, charity, Hoodi and\ncontracts-lint gates.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE","tree":{"sha":"6fb93e8175daf6d5d8263f73941eacfba74f3243","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/trees/6fb93e8175daf6d5d8263f73941eacfba74f3243"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/commits/1857c5eb43dffc9e9f3895472e9299891bd8cf7d","verification":{"payload":"tree 6fb93e8175daf6d5d8263f73941eacfba74f3243\nparent 48d8b8269abe0efc1a9635abe958903330ab2365\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790666617 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790666617 +0000\n\nfix(web): address four review findings on the settlement surfaces\n\n**A deployment belongs to one page, not to all of them** (P1). `AssetDetail` is\nshared by every slug in `lib/catalog.ts` — six invented artworks that map to no\ndeployed token — and both settlement surfaces read their contract from the\nenvironment with no identifier from the artwork. Once configured, every catalog\ndetail page would have offered the same real holding, approval and signing\nsurface beneath a different artwork''s title, so a holder could authorize a sale\nof an asset the page did not describe. That is a fixture dressed as live data\n(`AGENTS.md` §5, `ACCEPTANCE.md` §3) and a signature over terms the signer did\nnot mean.\n\nA deployment now names the one slug it belongs to. `assetDeploymentBinding`\ndecides which of three things is true for a page — bound here, deployed and\nbelonging elsewhere, or nothing deployed — and an unnamed deployment binds\nnowhere, so every route but the named one stays inert and says which case it is.\n\n**The zero address is not a party or a token** (P2). A blank payment-token field\nbecame `0x00…0`, which `isAddress` accepts; the market does not — it refuses to\nallowlist that token and refuses to fill against it. The form produced and\ndisplayed a signed authorization that could never settle anywhere. A blank field\nnow stays blank and surfaces the existing `payment-token-missing` problem before\nsigning, and both validators reject the zero address for the seller, the asset or\ncollection, and the payment token, while keeping it for the buyer field, where it\nmeans \"anyone may fill\".\n\n**Approve only a payment token confirmed allowlisted** (P1). The fill path sent\nthe buyer''s ERC-20 approval without checking the pasted intent''s payment token,\nthough the ABI already exposed `allowedPaymentToken`. For a token that was never\nallowlisted, or whose permission was withdrawn after signing, the buyer paid for\nan approval and left a live allowance behind for a fill that then reverted. The\nstanding is read and the approval blocked before it is requested, and an unread\nstanding does not pass: waiting costs a retry, guessing costs a stranded\nallowance.\n\n**Page through to the end for a charity edition''s venue** (P2). The venue lookup\nread only page one of `/v1/market/assets`, whose page size caps at 100. Past that\nmany mirrored token ids an edition on a later page reported as having no observed\nmarketplace activity and silently lost its venue link while a durable record\nexisted. `findCharityVenueRecord` walks until it finds the edition, a page comes\nback empty, or everything `total` promised has been seen.\n\nFour regressions, each verified by mutation: restoring the previous behaviour\nmakes that test fail and no other. The binding and the pagination were extracted\nso the decisions are testable rather than locked inside a component.\n\nWeb 176/176, Playwright 142 passed with 2 intentional skips across desktop and\nmobile, Forge 136/136, gofmt/go vet/go test -race, format, lint, typecheck,\nbuild, and the security, agent, chain-consistency, release, charity, Hoodi and\ncontracts-lint gates.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQE4mtl1N\nPDDp6YSH6KktLGPwJymAtPTyj0KSRWXIz2mMOcdZJM49MhVH7blOvFDhv9yXo7d9bXTxxtdITWMp\nnwE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T07:23:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/1857c5eb43dffc9e9f3895472e9299891bd8cf7d","node_id":"C_kwDOT8pe1toAKDE4NTdjNWViNDNkZmZjOWU5ZjM4OTU0NzJlOTI5OTg5MWJkOGNmN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/48d8b8269abe0efc1a9635abe958903330ab2365","sha":"48d8b8269abe0efc1a9635abe958903330ab2365","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/48d8b8269abe0efc1a9635abe958903330ab2365"}],"sha":"1857c5eb43dffc9e9f3895472e9299891bd8cf7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/1857c5eb43dffc9e9f3895472e9299891bd8cf7d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/48d8b8269abe0efc1a9635abe958903330ab2365/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T06:47:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T06:47:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs: record that this session cannot delete a ref, and how to run the prune\n\n`git push origin --delete` and `DELETE /git/refs/heads/:branch` both come back\n403 \"Write access to this GitHub API path is not permitted through this proxy\".\nPushing a branch and opening a pull request are allowed; removing a ref is not.\nThe 32 refs stay on the remote, so the ledger now carries the prune as a single\ncommand for anyone with ordinary push access, and the restore for any one of\nthem beside it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE","tree":{"sha":"41de30c04ea00944350c59757c91e82255994872","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/trees/41de30c04ea00944350c59757c91e82255994872"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/commits/48d8b8269abe0efc1a9635abe958903330ab2365","verification":{"payload":"tree 41de30c04ea00944350c59757c91e82255994872\nparent 0f3e68aef8c1afc3b98683a6091af84ef3f14d45\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790664427 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790664427 +0000\n\ndocs: record that this session cannot delete a ref, and how to run the prune\n\n`git push origin --delete` and `DELETE /git/refs/heads/:branch` both come back\n403 \"Write access to this GitHub API path is not permitted through this proxy\".\nPushing a branch and opening a pull request are allowed; removing a ref is not.\nThe 32 refs stay on the remote, so the ledger now carries the prune as a single\ncommand for anyone with ordinary push access, and the restore for any one of\nthem beside it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQICQ9B9I\n2+VB5LPILXBzl81Kev5UcnkW+A0U1zZuKkZQvQmJuulhhuuBmlTmOjCDrBMQywOYt/v/TJ/3AgJW\n5Qo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T06:47:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/48d8b8269abe0efc1a9635abe958903330ab2365","node_id":"C_kwDOT8pe1toAKDQ4ZDhiODI2OWFiZTBlZmMxYTk2MzVhYmU5NTg5MDMzMzBhYjIzNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/0f3e68aef8c1afc3b98683a6091af84ef3f14d45","sha":"0f3e68a