 branch that is the head or the base of an open pull request —\nwhich preserves Codex''s in-flight agent stack, the Dependabot branches and the\nolder drafts — and remove the rest. Bases are kept as well as heads, because\ndeleting the base of a stacked pull request closes it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE","tree":{"sha":"8cfb1138f2fd83e7448fb023ecd5074e30473094","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/trees/8cfb1138f2fd83e7448fb023ecd5074e30473094"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/commits/0f3e68aef8c1afc3b98683a6091af84ef3f14d45","verification":{"payload":"tree 8cfb1138f2fd83e7448fb023ecd5074e30473094\nparent bf4b68ce8585e10e540bce5de0e647f215ee2bb3\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790664119 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790664119 +0000\n\ndocs: record every branch about to be pruned, with its tip\n\nThe repository held 55 remote branches, the oldest from 2026-08-19. Thirty-two\nof them carry no open pull request and are being removed; twenty-eight of those\ncarry commits `main` does not have, so each tip is written down and any of them\nis restored with a single push.\n\nThe rule is mechanical so that nothing goes on taste: keep `main`, the active\nbranch, and every branch that is the head or the base of an open pull request —\nwhich preserves Codex''s in-flight agent stack, the Dependabot branches and the\nolder drafts — and remove the rest. Bases are kept as well as heads, because\ndeleting the base of a stacked pull request closes it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKqNSOrw\nsIvD