ps://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/bf4b68ce8585e10e540bce5de0e647f215ee2bb3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T20:07:30Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T20:07:30Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs: record the delivery state against ACCEPTANCE.md 6.2\n\nEvery stage of `PRD.md` §3.2.3 now has a screen for its function; two did not\nthis morning. The record states what that does and does not mean, and separates\nwhat is still needed into inputs the client supplies, decisions the client makes,\nand engineering that is open and blocked on neither.\n\nNo stage is declared delivered, for two reasons that are the client''s and not\ntechnical questions. §6.2 condition 2 asks for G1 human visual sign-off against\n`pics/*.png` and `fractional_steps/*`, which have never existed here — M3.10, the\none BLOCKED row — and §3.2.4 says whether Figma replaces that baseline is a\nclient decision an agent must not assume. And nothing has been exercised at\nruntime: no deployed contract, no reachable mirror, no transaction hash or\nreceipt, and §3 rules out inferring evidence. CI has not executed since\n2026-09-19, which removes a further class of it.\n\nRecord only. It creates no requirement, gate, status value or delivery\ncondition, and no status value moves: VERIFIED 7, IMPLEMENTED-NOT-VERIFIED 43,\nPENDING-GATE 5, BLOCKED 5, NOT-IMPLEMENTED 47, OUT-OF-SCOPE 0, identical to the\nprevious head.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE","tree":{"sha":"6adc34e006fe421b2cbbb6fee35b9516ccd89229","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/trees/6adc34e006fe421b2cbbb6fee35b9516ccd89229"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/commits/bf4b68ce8585e10e540bce5de0e647f215ee2bb3","verification":{"payload":"tree 6adc34e006fe421b2cbbb6fee35b9516ccd89229\nparent 5691fe5ce13f1da1cfb436e5f065c1fe7dd22c57\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790539650 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790539650 +0000\n\ndocs: record the delivery state against ACCEPTANCE.md 6.2\n\nEvery stage of `PRD.md` §3.2.3 now has a screen for its function; two did not\nthis morning. The record states what that does and does not mean, and separates\nwhat is still needed into inputs the client supplies, decisions the client makes,\nand engineering that is open and blocked on neither.\n\nNo stage is declared delivered, for two reasons that are the client''s and not\ntechnical questions. §6.2 condition 2 asks for G1 human visual sign-off against\n`pics/*.png` and `fractional_steps/*`, which have never existed here — M3.10, the\none BLOCKED row — and §3.2.4 says whether Figma replaces that baseline is a\nclient decision an agent must not assume. And nothing has been exercised at\nruntime: no deployed contract, no reachable mirror, no transaction hash or\nreceipt, and §3 rules out inferring evidence. CI has not executed since\n2026-09-19, which removes a further class of it.\n\nRecord only. It creates no requirement, gate, status value or delivery\ncondition, and no status value moves: VERIFIED 7, IMPLEMENTED-NOT-VERIFIED 43,\nPENDING-GATE 5, BLOCKED 5, NOT-IMPLEMENTED 47, OUT-OF-SCOPE 0, identical to the\nprevious head.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCnoDVz5\n7MPRlRgNAw4VsSEK4Wnre3Il8C7Q8MJ0kAPvVOkoSzpLx9Mubi80kyBviEMon+NqcppMPhjWCgOV\n0Qo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T20:07:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/bf4b68ce8585e10e540bce5de0e647f215ee2bb3","node_id":"C_kwDOT8pe1toAKGJmNGI2OGNlODU4NWUxMGU1NDBiY2U1ZGUwZTY0N2YyMTVlZTJiYjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/5691fe5ce13f1da1cfb436e5f065c1fe7dd22c57","sha":"5691fe5ce13f1da1cfb436e5f065c1fe7dd22c57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/5691fe5ce13f1da1cfb436e5f065c1fe7dd22c57"}],"sha":"bf4b68ce8585e10e540bce5de0e647f215ee2bb3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/bf4b68ce8585e10e540bce5de0e647f215ee2bb3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/5691fe5ce13f1da1cfb436e5f065c1fe7dd22c57/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T20:05:31Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T20:05:31Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(charity): give an edition the way out to its venue\n\n`PRD.md` §4.8 XM.4 requires a user to be able to reach OpenSea for every product\nline, and §3.2.3''s `S-CH` row makes a venue deep link part of what an edition\npage must show. Charity opens on OpenSea first (`AGENTS.md` §1.1 invariant 6),\nso until the line opens on ArtFi that link is how an edition is bought at all.\nThe edition page had no link out of any kind: it stated that ArtFi settles no\norder for the edition and stopped there, which tells a buyer what cannot happen\nhere without telling them where it can.\n\nThe link is attributed, never constructed. The surface asks the mirror for the\nrecords observed against the configured charity collection, matches this\nedition on contract *and* token id, and shows the URL the venue itself\nreported, re-validated by `venueLink` on the way to the page. It never\nassembles `https://opensea.io/assets/<chain>/<contract>/<id>` from what it\nknows, because a URL no observed event supports is a claim about the venue that\nXM.5 forbids and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §7.8 fails an audit over.\n\nSo four states, each a different statement and none of them a guess: an\nobserved record with a safe URL is the link; an observed record without one says\nso; nothing observed says so, which is not the same thing; and an unreachable\nmirror says that, with no cached or invented answer behind it. The matching and\nstate logic is pure and unit tested, including every URL shape the ingest rule\nrejects — plain HTTP, embedded credentials, a lookalike host, a subdomain of the\nallowed host, a `javascript:` scheme — and including the case where another\ncollection carries the same token id.\n\nThe CH.8 rights notice keeps its place ahead of everything, and a browser test\nholds it there: `ACCEPTANCE.md` §7.17 fails an audit where an edition is\ndisplayed or offered without it.\n\nNo status value moves. XM.4 and XM.5 keep `IMPLEMENTED-NOT-VERIFIED` — no\ndeployed collection, no reachable mirror and no observed charity record has been\nrendered here. CH.1–CH.11 are untouched.\n\nWeb 156/156, Playwright 142 passed with 2 intentional skips across desktop and\nmobile, format, lint, typecheck, build and the secret scan clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE","tree":{"sha":"3e289fcab7c791e3cd91b36917e2536e0e9852f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/trees/3e289fcab7c791e3cd91b36917e2536e0e9852f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/commits/5691fe5ce13f1da1cfb436e5f065c1fe7dd22c57","verification":