nholds it there: `ACCEPTANCE.md` §7.17 fails an audit where an edition is\ndisplayed or offered without it.\n\nNo status value moves. XM.4 and XM.5 keep `IMPLEMENTED-NOT-VERIFIED` — no\ndeployed collection, no reachable mirror and no observed charity record has been\nrendered here. CH.1–CH.11 are untouched.\n\nWeb 156/156, Playwright 142 passed with 2 intentional skips across desktop and\nmobile, format, lint, typecheck, build and the secret scan clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKN/Jo41\n1fPWQKtDFDkmM7sLJYNkKlL1pUQml27Dd7+hAod2iJ6ZEe+Ey1ibUzxt7fQJoOXvMbpcUYJsRqH/\n1As=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T20:05:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/5691fe5ce13f1da1cfb436e5f065c1fe7dd22c57","node_id":"C_kwDOT8pe1toAKDU2OTFmZTVjZTEzZjFkYTFjZmI0MzZlNWYwNjVjMWZlN2RkMjJjNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/e008aad747a579cffe8627a6b507b6cbb6534701","sha":"e008aad747a579cffe8627a6b507b6cbb6534701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/e008aad747a579cffe8627a6b507b6cbb6534701"}],"sha":"5691fe5ce13f1da1cfb436e5f065c1fe7dd22c57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/5691fe5ce13f1da1cfb436e5f065c1fe7dd22c57"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/e008aad747a579cffe8627a6b507b6cbb6534701/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T19:57:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T19:57:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(market): give fraction settlement the screen it never had\n\n`PRD.md` §3.2 makes a stage deliverable when its function is operable from a\nscreen. The signature-settled fixed-price path the client ruling of 2026-08-30\nrequires (§4.2.2) was on chain in `ArtFiMarket.sol` with nothing reaching it —\nthe fraction page said so itself: \"Fraction trading has no screen yet\". That is\nprogress, not a handover.\n\nA holder authorizes a sale of up to some number of fractions by signing EIP-712\nterms; a buyer settles part or all of it. The fractions never leave the holder''s\nwallet in between, ArtFi is never counterparty, and nothing here moves a\nholder''s tokens without the signature they produced for that fill. Partial fills\nare the difference from the whole-artwork surface: one signature settles\ncumulatively up to its maximum, so both sides see what is left, and the holder\ncan retire one authorization or all of them — neither blocked by a pause, since\nan administrative action must not keep alive an authorization its author\nwithdrew.\n\nFour things the surface refuses to hide, each being a fill that would otherwise\nrevert with nothing to explain it: the token allowlist, the buyer''s remaining\npilot spend cap, the cumulative fill counter, and the seller''s current epoch.\nThe last two are read from chain rather than taken from the pasted terms, which\nis the only way either can be true: another buyer may have taken part of the\nsame authorization, and the seller may have withdrawn it, since that text was\nwritten. Approval is its own step for an exact amount on each leg — the seller''s\ncovers the authorized maximum, the buyer''s covers this fill — never unlimited.\nWith no deployed market or fraction token the panel names the missing\nprerequisite and offers nothing.\n\nTwo corrections to the whole-artwork surface, which is the same shape. Its buyer\npath compared a pasted intent''s epoch against itself, which can never detect the\nwithdrawal the check exists for. And it had no configuration path at all:\nnothing passes a collection, so no deployment could have switched it on. Both\nsurfaces now take deployment configuration as a fallback to their props.\n\nBrowser and contract are pinned to one digest, asserted from the contract''s own\ntypehash in `FractionSaleIntent.t.sol` and from viem in `fraction-intent.test.ts`,\nso a field renamed, reordered or retyped on either side fails a test on both\nrather than producing a signature the market rejects at fill time.\n\nNo status value moves. M2.4–M2.9 stay NOT-IMPLEMENTED: a signature that lives in\none browser is not an order store, a lifecycle service or a matching engine, and\nthe panel says so on screen rather than implying a live book. M3.1 stays\nNOT-IMPLEMENTED — auctions keep escrow under the same ruling. The fixture figures\non the fraction page are unchanged and stay labelled.\n\nWeb 147/147, Playwright 132 passed with 2 intentional skips across desktop and\nmobile, Forge 136/136, mirror 49/49, gofmt/go vet/go test -race, format, lint,\ntypecheck, build, and the security, agent, release and chain-consistency gates.\nThe MySQL migration job needs a container runtime and was not run here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE","tree":{"sha":"bc3f1325a8c04fcb19a96f8a559629dcbd6ce239","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/trees/bc3f1325a8c04fcb19a96f8a559629dcbd6ce239"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/commits/e008aad747a579cffe8627a6b507b6cbb6534701","verification":{"payload":"tree bc3f1325a8c04fcb19a96f8a559629dcbd6ce239\nparent f8d9df971d6fba6040cdb5114624bdad0e98d81c\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790539033 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790539033 +0000\n\nfeat(market): give fraction settlement the screen it never had\n\n`PRD.md` §3.2 makes a stage deliverable when its function is operable from a\nscreen. The signature-settled fixed-price path the client ruling of 2026-08-30\nrequires (§4.2.2) was on chain in `ArtFiMarket.sol` with nothing reaching it —\nthe fraction page said so itself: \"Fraction trading has no screen yet\". That is\nprogress, not a handover.\n\nA holder authorizes a sale of up to some number of fractions by signing EIP-712\nterms; a buyer settles part or all of it. The fractions never leave the holder''s\nwallet in between, ArtFi is never counterparty, and nothing here moves a\nholder''s tokens without the signature they produced for that fill. Partial fills\nare the difference from the whole-artwork surface: one signature settles\ncumulatively up to its maximum, so both sides see what is left, and the holder\ncan retire one authorization or all of them — neither blocked by a pause, since\nan administrative action must not keep alive an authorization its author\nwithdrew.\n\nFour things the surface refuses to hide, each being a fill that would otherwise\nrevert with nothing to explain it: the token allowlist, the buyer''s remaining\npilot spend cap, the cumulative fill counter, and the seller''s current epoch.\nThe last two are read from chain rather than taken from the pasted terms, which\nis the only way either can be true: another buyer may have taken part of the\nsame authorization, and the seller may have withdrawn it, since that text was\nwritten. Approval is its own step for an exact amount on each leg — the seller''s\ncovers the authorized maximum, the buyer''s covers this fill — never unlimited.\nWith no deployed market or fraction token the panel names the missing\nprerequisite and offers nothing.\n\nTwo corrections to the whole-artwork surface, which is the same shape. Its buyer\npath compared a pasted intent''s epoch against itself, which can never detect the\nwithdrawal the check exists for. And it had no configuration path at all:\nnothing passes a collection, so no deployment could have switched it on. Both\nsurfaces now take deployment configuration as a fallback to their props.\n\nBrowser and contract are pinned to one digest, asserted from the contract''s own\ntypehash in `FractionSaleIntent.t.sol` and from viem in `fraction-intent.test.ts`,\nso a field renamed, reordered or retyped on either side fails a test on both\nrather than producing a signature the market rejects at fill time.\n\nNo status value moves. M2.4–M2.9 stay NOT-IMPLEMENTED: a signature that lives in\none browser is not an order store, a lifecycle service or a matching engine, and\nthe panel says so on screen rather than implying a live book. M3.1 stays\nNOT-IMPLEMENTED — auctions keep escrow under the same ruling. The fixture figures\non the fraction page are unchanged and stay labelled.\n\nWeb 147/147, Playwright 132 passed with 2 intentional skips across desktop and\nmobile, Forge 136/136, mirror 49/49, gofmt/go vet/go test -race, format, lint,\ntypecheck, build, and the security, agent, release and chain-consistency gates.\nThe MySQL migration job needs a container runtime and was not run here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEA7rALH\nJplMUV9UncJAk6xJy76ptl3rokwF8rbQKy7+XgqcH0HvYfJduoOdfNMGH+qWkaHrxACFE2/YuMay\nSAo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T19:57:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/e008aad747a579cffe8627a6b507b6cbb6534701","node_id":"C_kwDOT8pe1toAKGUwMDhhYWQ3NDdhNTc5Y2ZmZTg2MjdhNmI1MDdiNmNiYjY1MzQ3MDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/f8d9df971d6fba6040cdb5114624bdad0e98d81c","sha":"f8d9df971d6fba6040cdb5114624bdad0e98d81c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/f8d9df971d6fba6040cdb5114624bdad0e98d81c"}],"sha":"e008aad747a579cffe8627a6b507b6cbb6534701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/e008aad747a579cffe8627a6b507b6cbb6534701"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/f8d9df971d6fba6040cdb5114624bdad0e98d81c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T19:33:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T19:33:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs: record the three mirror findings as closed, with local evidence\n\n`AGENTS.md`''s S-XM checkpoint said PR #114 was not ready to hand over on three\naccepted, unresolved findings. They are fixed at `1cb630a`, so the checkpoint\nnow names the commit, the four regressions and the gates that ran, and keeps\nwhat did not run: the MySQL migration job, managed TEST_ONLY database\nexecution, the live OpenSea stream run, and independent review of this head.\n\n`docs/STATUS.md` gains the matching evidence entry. No status value moves —\ntable rows by value are identical to the previous head: VERIFIED 7,\nIMPLEMENTED-NOT-VERIFIED 43, PENDING-GATE 5, BLOCKED 5, NOT-IMPLEMENTED 47,\nOUT-OF-SCOPE 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE","tree":{"sha":"907740ad8d3cea9d6434af1050c2c1fa3b6cedef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/trees/907740ad8d3cea9d6434af1050c2c1fa3b6cedef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/commits/f8d9df971d6fba6040cdb5114624bdad0e98d81c","verification":{"payload":"tree 907740ad8d3cea9d6434af1050c2c1fa3b6cedef\nparent 1cb630a3ead08f88f13c0ed62126941ddbb09fc4\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790537587 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790537587 +0000\n\ndocs: record the three mirror findings as closed, with local evidence\n\n`AGENTS.md`''s S-XM checkpoint said PR #114 was not ready to hand over on three\naccepted, unresolved findings. They are fixed at `1cb630a`, so the checkpoint\nnow names the commit, the four regressions and the gates that ran, and keeps\nwhat did not run: the MySQL migration job, managed TEST_ONLY database\nexecution, the live OpenSea stream run, and independent review of this head.\n\n`docs/STATUS.md` gains the matching evidence entry. No status value moves —\ntable rows by value are identical to the previous head: VERIFIED 7,\nIMPLEMENTED-NOT-VERIFIED 43, PENDING-GATE 5, BLOCKED 5, NOT-IMPLEMENTED 47,\nOUT-OF-SCOPE 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIXGOxQo\nzvR13zucH/761/XSl7Jpym464NY/zVFBZZTf5StmTcb9eQ1T00yjd6gTJWTZUKCE/BPq4yI9DXxL\n0Q4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T19:33:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/f8d9df971d6fba6040cdb5114624bdad0e98d81c","node_id":"C_kwDOT8pe1toAKGY4ZDlkZjk3MWQ2ZmJhNjA0MGNkYjUxMTQ2MjRiZGFkMGU5OGQ4MWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/1cb630a3ead08f88f13c0ed62126941ddbb09fc4","sha":"1cb630a3ead08f88f13c0ed62126941ddbb09fc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/1cb630a3ead08f88f13c0ed62126941ddbb09fc4"}],"sha":"f8d9df971d6fba6040cdb5114624bdad0e98d81c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/f8d9df971d6fba6040cdb5114624bdad0e98d81c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/1cb630a3ead08f88f13c0ed62126941ddbb09fc4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T19:31:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T19:31:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"market-mirror: fix the three accepted PR #114 review findings\n\nThe S-XM checkpoint in AGENTS.md records PR #114 as not ready to hand over\nbecause three accepted findings were left unresolved. All three are in the\nOpenSea mirror''s durable backfill path.\n\nOrdered, crash-recoverable finalization (discussion_r4056400240). Deferred-lease\ncommit unlinked events.ndjson and checkpoints.ndjson concurrently and released\nthe writer lock even when only one of them went. A crash or a one-sided failure\nbetween the two could leave a checkpoint naming a spool that no longer existed,\nand every later start then failed at the spool''s existence check, so the mirror\ncould not run again until someone repaired the directory by hand. The pointer\nnow goes first and the payload only once the pointer is gone, so a partial\ncleanup can only ever leave an orphaned payload; and an orphaned pointer, from\nwhatever cause, is now discarded and the snapshot re-derived instead of treated\nas terminal.\n\nRecovery overlap stops at the newest committed page (discussion_r4056400243).\nOne boundary was retained per collection and, because a collection is paged from\nits head downwards, that was its oldest committed page. Restart therefore walked\nback over nearly the whole committed history before it recognised anything, so a\nspool that fits once but not twice hit ENOSPC on every retry. Every retained\npage boundary now counts; all of them lie inside the region the spool is\ntruncated to, so stopping at the first match is safe as well as cheapest.\n\nThe initial REST crawl is abortable (discussion_r4056400246). Aborting the\nsnapshot upload stops the publication of what has been staged and does nothing\nto a crawl that is still fetching pages while holding the durable writer lock.\nThe crawl now has its own signal, which the fatal stream path aborts, so a\nreconnect acknowledgement that times out ends the traversal instead of waiting\nfor every remaining page of a history that is about to be thrown away.\n\nAlso checks the return value of a mock ERC20 transfer in FractionSaleIntent.t.sol,\nwhich was the only remaining forge lint warning.\n\nFour regressions, each verified by mutation to fail against the previous\nbehaviour. Local gates on this tree: market-mirror 49/49, Web 125/125,\nPlaywright 118 passed with 2 intentional skips, Forge 135/135, Go vet/gofmt and\nthe API suite with -race, format/lint/typecheck/build, and the security, agent,\nrelease and chain-consistency gates. The MySQL migration job needs a container\nruntime and was not run here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE","tree":{"sha":"8a0ebf8cabe8303da2187f7bea1ef5f49fe836d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/trees/8a0ebf8cabe8303da2187f7bea1ef5f49fe836d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/commits/1cb630a3ead08f88f13c0ed62126941ddbb09fc4","verification":{"payload":"tree 8a0ebf8cabe8303da2187f7bea1ef5f49fe836d3\nparent 084efc6cd8f374df7bc3883f7bdfcd7addca7b1b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790537467 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790537467 +0000\n\nmarket-mirror: fix the three accepted PR #114 review findings\n\nThe S-XM checkpoint in AGENTS.md records PR #114 as not ready to hand over\nbecause three accepted findings were left unresolved. All three are in the\nOpenSea mirror''s durable backfill path.\n\nOrdered, crash-recoverable finalization (discussion_r4056400240). Deferred-lease\ncommit unlinked events.ndjson and checkpoints.ndjson concurrently and released\nthe writer lock even when only one of them went. A crash or a one-sided failure\nbetween the two could leave a checkpoint naming a spool that no longer existed,\nand every later start then failed at the spool''s existence check, so the mirror\ncould not run again until someone repaired the directory by hand. The pointer\nnow goes first and the payload only once the pointer is gone, so a partial\ncleanup can only ever leave an orphaned payload; and an orphaned pointer, from\nwhatever cause, is now discarded and the snapshot re-derived instead of treated\nas terminal.\n\nRecovery overlap stops at the newest committed page (discussion_r4056400243).\nOne boundary was retained per collection and, because a collection is paged from\nits head downwards, that was its oldest committed page. Restart therefore walked\nback over nearly the whole committed history before it recognised anything, so a\nspool that fits once but not twice hit ENOSPC on every retry. Every retained\npage boundary now counts; all of them lie inside the region the spool is\ntruncated to, so stopping at the first match is safe as well as cheapest.\n\nThe initial REST crawl is abortable (discussion_r4056400246). Aborting the\nsnapshot upload stops the publication of what has been staged and does nothing\nto a crawl that is still fetching pages while holding the durable writer lock.\nThe crawl now has its own signal, which the fatal stream path aborts, so a\nreconnect acknowledgement that times out ends the traversal instead of waiting\nfor every remaining page of a history that is about to be thrown away.\n\nAlso checks the return value of a mock ERC20 transfer in FractionSaleIntent.t.sol,\nwhich was the only remaining forge lint warning.\n\nFour regressions, each verified by mutation to fail against the previous\nbehaviour. Local gates on this tree: market-mirror 49/49, Web 125/125,\nPlaywright 118 passed with 2 intentional skips, Forge 135/135, Go vet/gofmt and\nthe API suite with -race, format/lint/typecheck/build, and the security, agent,\nrelease and chain-consistency gates. The MySQL migration job needs a container\nruntime and was not run here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAuSOBRa\nSiNWMRk4xziT8znpi3KRdHAekQzxE4eJ5onxF003GVWJTiHkqrncRnfGOjKg3TZEOgzd2KKTY3VE\n6g0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T19:31:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/1cb630a3ead08f88f13c0ed62126941ddbb09fc4","node_id":"C_kwDOT8pe1toAKDFjYjYzMGEzZWFkMDhmODhmMTNjMGVkNjIxMjY5NDFkZGJiMDlmYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commit/084efc6cd8f374df7bc3883f7bdfcd7addca7b1b","sha":"084efc6cd8f374df7bc3883f7bdfcd7addca7b1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/084efc6cd8f374df7bc3883f7bdfcd7addca7b1b"}],"sha":"1cb630a3ead08f88f13c0ed62126941ddbb09fc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/1cb630a3ead08f88f13c0ed62126941ddbb09fc4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/084efc6cd8f374df7bc3883f7bdfcd7addca7b1b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T07:06:52Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T07:06:52Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs: record why #114 and #115 are back in\n\nClient decision of 2026-09-26: do not split them out. The reverts are\nreverted and both are included again.\n\nRecorded rather than smoothed over, because the branch now contains a\ncontradiction that a reader is entitled to see: `AGENTS.md`''s S-XM\ncheckpoint — which arrived as part of #114''s own content — states that\n#114 \"is not ready to merge or hand over\", on three accepted, unresolved\nreview findings. That text is left exactly as it is. The decision to\nproceed is the client''s; the record of the open findings is Codex''s; the\nthree findings are unchanged by this merge.\n\nVerified rather than assumed, on the restored tree:\n\n- **No status value moved.** Table rows by value are identical to the\n  pre-restore head: VERIFIED 7, IMPLEMENTED-NOT-VERIFIED 43,\n  PENDING-GATE 5, BLOCKED 5, NOT-IMPLEMENTED 47. A raw string count rises\n  by one only because Codex''s restored narrative says \"XM.3 remains\n  IMPLEMENTED-NOT-VERIFIED\" in prose.\n- **`docs/STATUS.md` is the clean copy**, valid UTF-8, carrying all four\n  contributions. The corrupted version on #115''s branch did not come\n  back.\n- **The operations surface is byte-identical across the restore** —\n  `operations/page.tsx`, `operations-status.tsx`, `ops-checks.ts` and\n  their spec have an empty diff. One `operations-status` case failed once\n  in a full-suite run, then passed 12 of 12 across three repeats. It\n  aborts routes, so it is a race in the test, not a regression, and it is\n  left alone: changing someone else''s passing test is not part of a\n  restore.\n\nLocal evidence on this head: forge 135, vitest 125, playwright 117 pass\nwith 1 flake and 2 skips across desktop and mobile, market-mirror suite,\n`go vet` / `gofmt` / `go test -race`, and every format, lint, typecheck,\nbuild, secret, chain-consistency and release-verifier gate. CI itself\nstill cannot execute — see the note above it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE","tree":{"sha":"aed16029663f4f534d477e3b6f340b501e1a3170","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/trees/aed16029663f4f534d477e3b6f340b501e1a3170"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/commits/084efc6cd8f374df7bc3883f7bdfcd7addca7b1b","verification":{"payload":"tree aed16029663f4f534d477e3b6f340b501e1a3170\nparent f25731f3d5df34d7c186bb21c9b64831324efc60\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790406412 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790406412 +0000\n\ndocs: record why #114 and #115 are back in\n\nClient decision of 2026-09-26: do not split them out. The reverts are\nreverted and both are included again.\n\nRecorded rather than smoothed over, because the branch now contains a\ncontradiction that a reader is entitled to see: `AGENTS.md`''s S-XM\ncheckpoint — which arrived as part of #114''s own content — states that\n#114 \"is not ready to merge or hand over\", on three accepted, unresolved\nreview findings. That text is left exactly as it is. The decision to\nproceed is the client''s; the record of the open findings is Codex''s; the\nthree findings are unchanged by this merge.\n\nVerified rather than assumed, on the restored tree:\n\n- **No status value moved.** Table rows by value are identical to the\n  pre-restore head: VERIFIED 7, IMPLEMENTED-NOT-VERIFIED 43,\n  PENDING-GATE 5, BLOCKED 5, NOT-IMPLEMENTED 47. A raw string count rises\n  by one only because Codex''s restored narrative says \"XM.3 remains\n  IMPLEMENTED-NOT-VERIFIED\" in prose.\n- **`docs/STATUS.md` is the clean copy**, valid UTF-8, carrying all four\n  contributions. The corrupted version on #115''s branch did not come\n  back.\n- **The operations surface is byte-identical across the restore** —\n  `operations/page.tsx`, `operations-status.tsx`, `ops-checks.ts` and\n  their spec have an empty diff. One `operations-status` case failed once\n  in a full-suite run, then passed 12 of 12 across three repeats. It\n  aborts routes, so it is a race in the test, not a regression, and it is\n  left alone: changing someone else''s passing test is not part of a\n  restore.\n\nLocal evidence on this head: forge 135, vitest 125, playwright 117 pass\nwith 1 flake and 2 skips across desktop and mobile, market-mirror suite,\n`go vet` / `gofmt` / `go test -race`, and every format, lint, typecheck,\nbuild, secret, chain-consistency and release-verifier gate. CI itself\nstill cannot execute — see the note above it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCTx5mMk\nw4TBs/FD+ZNxWxGc/p3NzzGEpVkLsaXauyyQur93IP49R1q3DW0SC6w9rtqNQmOB+ilgfxaxHszX\nRwU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T07:06:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_