de/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/commits/441f6c1426add1b0f7b47739cd1e1e42f08ad2af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T06:55:30Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T06:55:30Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs: record that CI has never executed, and why 8af87e8 merged anyway\n\nDiagnosed rather than assumed. Every `quality` run from 276 to 307\nfailed, across every branch and every triggering actor — the Codex\nbranches, dependabot, and `main`''s own two README commits (runs 299 and\n300). The signature is identical each time: `runner_id: 0`, no runner\nname, no `steps`, two seconds, and HTTP 404 for every job''s log.\n\n**No runner was ever assigned and nothing was ever executed.** That rules\nout the workflow file: an unresolvable action reference would assign a\nrunner and log the failure. It is an account-level condition outside this\nrepository, it predates all of this work, and it blocks every pull\nrequest including #114.\n\nSo the rule \"merge after CI passes\" is currently unsatisfiable for\nanything. Client decision of 2026-09-26 is to keep the merge and run the\nfull workflow on `main` once CI is restored, rather than revert.\n\nRecorded so nobody reads \"merged\" as \"CI-verified\". Until that run\nexists, nothing on this head is CI-verified; what stands behind it is\nlocal evidence, listed in the note.\n\n`docs/STATUS.md` gains evidence only. No status value moved.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE","tree":{"sha":"73f0d7474124eb9b5a29d25ca9cf34868185e613","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/trees/73f0d7474124eb9b5a29d25ca9cf34868185e613"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/GiraffeTechnology/ArtFi/git/commits/441f6c1426add1b0f7b47739cd1e1e42f08ad2af","verification":{"payload":"tree 73f0d7474124eb9b5a29d25ca9cf34868185e613\nparent 8af87e8c3e3d41ae5d4c6cb0345fb25c342aca0f\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790405730 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790405730 +0000\n\ndocs: record that CI has never executed, and why 8af87e8 merged anyway\n\nDiagnosed rather than assumed. Every `quality` run from 276 to 307\nfailed, across every branch and every triggering actor — the Codex\nbranches, dependabot, and `main`''s own two README commits (runs 299 and\n300). The signature is identical each time: `runner_id: 0`, no runner\nname, no `steps`, two seconds, and HTTP 404 for every job''s log.\n\n**No runner was ever assigned and nothing was ever executed.** That rules\nout the workflow file: an unresolvable action reference would assign a\nrunner and log the failure. It is an account-level condition outside this\nrepository, it predates all of this work, and it blocks every pull\nrequest including #114.\n\nSo the rule \"merge after CI passes\" is currently unsatisfiable for\nanything. Client decision of 2026-09-26 is to keep the merge and run the\nfull workflow on `main` once CI is restored, rather than revert.\n\nRecorded so nobody reads \"merged\" as \"CI-verified\". Until that run\nexists, nothing on this head is CI-verified; what stands behind it is\nlocal evidence, listed in the note.\n\n`docs/STATUS.md` gains evidence only. No status value moved.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CpdXJvic82vY3nEZSQH8JE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGaR0Gjo\nD1uBgPN4I90cQLbgmVvKKoTXyKzjTyycb+M+XTah/l+LnSlwEtIgisGSSV/H/RAXGzVVGCeYhtWN\nFA8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-