dDate":"2026-08-19T06:05:31Z","committedDate":"2026-08-19T06:05:31Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"Abhimishra2424","providerType":"User"},"email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:16:30.996Z","repositoryId":1339104481,"sha":"0235a2e98f467cb7c3945862adb54724c55cb094"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"Abhimishra2424","providerType":"User"},"email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-19T05:50:25Z","committedDate":"2026-08-19T05:50:25Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"Abhimishra2424","providerType":"User"},"email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:16:30.996Z","repositoryId":1339104481,"sha":"ae51cd0789444f45b230fdab0e2d887f892ebf49"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"Abhimishra2424","providerType":"User"},"email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-19T05:09:45Z","committedDate":"2026-08-19T05:09:45Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"Abhimishra2424","providerType":"User"},"email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:16:30.996Z","repositoryId":1339104481,"sha":"84358fad24324faf2f765985ae2396b0b59c732c"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"Abhimishra2424","providerType":"User"},"email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-19T05:07:31Z","committedDate":"2026-08-19T05:07:31Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"Abhimishra2424","providerType":"User"},"email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:16:30.996Z","repositoryId":1339104481,"sha":"820c57520e8c88033e0e9f6c69125db1fd907ee6"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"Abhimishra2424","providerType":"User"},"email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-19T04:46:11Z","committedDate":"2026-08-19T04:46:11Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"Abhimishra2424","providerType":"User"},"email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:16:30.996Z","repositoryId":1339104481,"sha":"052cd046e825690926ed51ef5df59531e73636f5"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"Abhimishra2424","providerType":"User"},"email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-19T04:43:59Z","committedDate":"2026-08-19T04:43:59Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"Abhimishra2424","providerType":"User"},"email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:16:30.996Z","repositoryId":1339104481,"sha":"d67c470d56edeea9ebac12780bb9e05b86dd4813"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:16:30.996Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/2429c57909eb25bfe8d59792622453e7bdb02d79/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T04:11:39Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T04:11:39Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"message":"v1.2.0 — both toolbar menus redesigned\n\nThey had grown into long undifferentiated lists that said nothing about their\nown state. On a 25-column salary register the Columns menu was 18 rows of\ntick + label + two arrow buttons — 36 controls stacked in a popover whose actual\njob is the checkboxes — and the Freeze menu was 38 near-identical entries with\nthe current one somewhere inside it.\n\nColumns:\n- A title bar with a live count, \"12 of 18\". Neither menu reported its own\n  state, so the only way to know how much was hidden was to read every entry\n  looking for the unticked ones.\n- Real checkboxes instead of a bare tick. With a tick alone \"hidden\" is the\n  ABSENCE of a mark, and a list where most rows are ticked reads as a column of\n  floating checkmarks with a few gaps in it.\n- One drag grip per row in place of the two arrow buttons. The grip is still a\n  button and ArrowUp/ArrowDown still move the column — dropping the arrows\n  cannot mean dropping keyboard reordering with them.\n- The three resets are one compact footer line. They are housekeeping, not\n  choices, and stacked full-width they were as prominent as the column list.\n\nFreeze:\n- The current state in the title bar: \"3 left · none right\".\n- The two edges as named groups (Left edge / Right edge) with radio dots rather\n  than ticks — one boundary out of many is a radio choice, and a tick said \"on\"\n  where it needed to say \"this one\".\n\nThe menu drag is deliberately simpler than the header drag on the table: no rAF\nloop, no rect cache (the list can scroll mid-drag, so it asks the DOM what is\nunder the pointer each move). It commits once on pointerup, for the same reason\nthe header drag does — the column defs feed every visible row.\n\nNew `components` slots: CheckboxIcon, RadioIcon, GripIcon. MenuHeading takes a\n`note`.\n\nAnyone who styled the menus: the resets are `.ft-menu-action` inside\n`.ft-menu-actions` (were `.ft-menu-item`), each row has one `.ft-menu-move` not\ntwo, and `.ft-menu-group` is the new per-edge label.\n\nTests: 94 DOM checks (+10), including the drag end to end — pointerdown on a\ngrip, the carried row marked, the insertion edge on the target, and the column\nlanding at the end on drop. jsdom implements neither PointerEvent nor pointer\ncapture, so both are stubbed at the top of the file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"50d5b538d0d5ed1cf44b13810e800f8657f4639d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/trees/50d5b538d0d5ed1cf44b13810e800f8657f4639d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/commits/2429c57909eb25bfe8d59792622453e7bdb02d79","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/2429c57909eb25bfe8d59792622453e7bdb02d79","node_id":"C_kwDOT9Ec4doAKDI0MjljNTc5MDllYjI1YmZlOGQ1OTc5MjYyMjQ1M2U3YmRiMDJkNzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/167471c5599c72a3c9bb3becbc2d5e587bfb2722","sha":"167471c5599c72a3c9bb3becbc2d5e587bfb2722","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/167471c5599c72a3c9bb3becbc2d5e587bfb2722"}],"sha":"2429c57909eb25bfe8d59792622453e7bdb02d79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/2429c57909eb25bfe8d59792622453e7bdb02d79"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/167471c5599c72a3c9bb3becbc2d5e587bfb2722/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T04:00:40Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T04:00:40Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"message":"v1.1.2 — the Columns menu read as one block of colour; move arrows are drawn now\n\nFound by opening the menus on a 25-column salary register.\n\n- The \"selected\" tint keyed off `aria-checked`. That is what a CHECKBOX entry\n  carries, and in the Columns menu nearly every column is visible — so nearly\n  every row was tinted and the highlight carried no information at all. It is\n  now scoped to `aria-current`, which only the radio entries set (the Freeze\n  menu''s current boundary). The tick alone says \"shown\"; a HIDDEN column is\n  dimmed, which is the signal that was actually missing.\n\n  The dim rule is scoped to `role=\"menuitemcheckbox\"` on purpose: a radio list\n  also marks its unselected entries `aria-checked=\"false\"`, and greying all but\n  one of those would read as \"unavailable\" rather than \"not chosen\".\n\n- The move controls were the `↑` / `↓` characters, drawn by whatever font the\n  host page uses — thin, differently sized and vertically off in most of them.\n  They are an inline chevron now, in a 20px square with a real hover area.\n\n- Menus are 248px wide rather than 210: \"Leave Travel Allowance\" plus the two\n  move buttons did not fit, so the label was clipped.\n\nTests: 84 DOM checks (+4), asserting the checked-checkbox rule is gone, the\naria-current one stays, the dim is checkbox-scoped, and the move controls render\nan element rather than text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"78da818406d66fd7548cf2ac9a2616df37e6252a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/trees/78da818406d66fd7548cf2ac9a2616df37e6252a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/commits/167471c5599c72a3c9bb3becbc2d5e587bfb2722","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/167471c5599c72a3c9bb3becbc2d5e587bfb2722","node_id":"C_kwDOT9Ec4doAKDE2NzQ3MWM1NTk5YzcyYTNjOWJiM2JlY2JjMmQ1ZTU4N2JmYjI3MjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/3e80bcc81c6cac3aefcd9a9d030105a4baa46a9c","sha":"3e80bcc81c6cac3aefcd9a9d030105a4baa46a9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/3e80bcc81c6cac3aefcd9a9d030105a4baa46a9c"}],"sha":"167471c5599c72a3c9bb3becbc2d5e587bfb2722","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/167471c5599c72a3c9bb3becbc2d5e587bfb2722"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/3e80bcc81c6cac3aefcd9a9d030105a4baa46a9c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T03:37:22Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T03:37:22Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"message":"v1.1.1 — `label` for the menus, and the Columns menu''s clipped move arrows\n\nBoth found by putting 1.1.0 into a real screen: a payroll salary register, whose\nheaders carry their own sort control and so are elements rather than strings.\n\n- `label` — a plain-text column name for the Columns and Freeze menus. A node\n  `Header` left both menus with nothing to print, so they fell back to the\n  column id and listed the report by field name: `employee_code`, `comp_CONV`,\n  `full_name` where the table itself showed \"Emp Code\", \"Conveyance Allowance\",\n  \"Employee Name\". A string Header still works untouched; `label` wins over it\n  when both are given. README §3 and §13.7 say so now rather than advising\n  people to keep Header a string, which was a workaround, not an answer.\n\n- The Columns menu''s up/down arrows were pushed past the menu''s right edge and\n  clipped. The entry and the arrows share a flex row, and `width: 100%` on a\n  flex child is 100% of the ROW — so the entry claimed all of it. The row is now\n  `.ft-menu-row` and the entry flexes into what is left.\n\nAlso: a CSS comment I added carried backticks around a property name, inside a\nsheet that is one JS template literal. It parsed as the end of the string. No\nbackticks in stylesheet.js — there is a note in it now.\n\nTests: 80 DOM checks (+6), covering `label` in both menus, the id fallback when\na node Header has no label, a string Header still naming itself, and the row\nkeeping both move buttons. Golden snapshots unchanged — the menus only exist\nonce opened, so none of this reaches the server-rendered markup.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"55f7980a2d57fdf149f2b54cfc7ad022bec9a04b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/trees/55f7980a2d57fdf149f2b54cfc7ad022bec9a04b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/commits/3e80bcc81c6cac3aefcd9a9d030105a4baa46a9c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/3e80bcc81c6cac3aefcd9a9d030105a4baa46a9c","node_id":"C_kwDOT9Ec4doAKDNlODBiY2M4MWM2Y2FjM2FlZmNkOWE5ZDAzMDEwNWE0YmFhNDZhOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/3f499ab0aa40ce9c61d3350e37d4f18656d98009","sha":"3f499ab0aa40ce9c61d3350e37d4f18656d98009","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/3f499ab0aa40ce9c61d3350e37d4f18656d98009"}],"sha":"3e80bcc81c6cac3aefcd9a9d030105a4baa46a9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/3e80bcc81c6cac3aefcd9a9d030105a4baa46a9c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/3f499ab0aa40ce9c61d3350e37d4f18656d98009/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T13:16:31Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T13:16:31Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"message":"v1.1.0 — theming: CSS-variable tokens, per-slot classNames, replaceable components, unstyled\n\nThe release is about fitting into someone else''s UI. Everything is additive: no\nprop was removed or renamed, and a 1.0 table upgrades with no code change.\n\nFour layers, each off by default, each reaching something the one before it cannot:\n\n- `theme` / `tokens` — 56 CSS custom properties, ten of them core with the rest\n  derived through a ladder, so six variables re-theme the whole table and one\n  re-themes exactly one thing. `theme=\"dark\"` and `theme=\"auto\"` ship built in.\n  This is the only layer that reaches all three places colour lived: the inline\n  styles, the injected stylesheet''s :hover / :focus-visible / [aria-checked]\n  rules, and the row background a JS handler writes onto element.style.\n- `classNames` — 21 slots, merged after the built-in ft-* class so a flat\n  specificity setup (Tailwind and friends) wins on source order.\n- `components` — 12 slots: the filter input, the toolbar buttons, the menus and\n  their parts, the spinner, the empty state and every icon. `null` renders\n  nothing. This is the layer that makes it look like someone''s design system\n  rather than a recoloured copy of ours.\n- `unstyled` — no injected sheet and no paint, keeping only what IS the freeze\n  and the virtualization. The split lives at each call site via skin(), not in a\n  central list of \"removable properties\", so the next visual cannot land on the\n  wrong side of it by accident.\n\nDeployment fixes that came with it:\n- `styleNonce`, and `freeze-table/styles.css` emitted by the build from the same\n  source as the injected string, for a CSP with no ''unsafe-inline''.\n- The sheet now goes to the table''s own root node, so a table inside a shadow\n  root is styled instead of silently unstyled.\n- The <style> id carries a schema version, so two copies of the package on one\n  page no longer means the first one styles both.\n\nTwo bugs found by driving the demo in a browser, both of which would have made\nthe feature look like it worked while doing nothing:\n\n- The defaults out-cascaded the consumer. `.ft-root{--ft-bg:…}` and a caller''s\n  `.my-table{--ft-bg:…}` are both one class deep, and this sheet is injected at\n  MOUNT — after every stylesheet the page loaded — so the tie went to the\n  library and the theme was ignored, with nothing in the markup to explain it.\n  The token blocks are now :where()-wrapped (specificity 0-0-0) and the element\n  is inserted as head.firstChild. Pinned by a jsdom cascade test that asserts it\n  against the worst case, our sheet appended last.\n- `--ft-font` was applied through the CSS `font` shorthand, which requires a\n  size — so `font: Inter, sans-serif` is invalid and the browser dropped the\n  declaration. `inherit` is legal in both, which is why the default worked and\n  the token never did. It is `font-family` now.\n\nTwo visible changes on upgrade, both consequences of the above: the root sets\ncolor and background from --ft-text / --ft-bg (body cells used to inherit the\npage''s text colour onto hard-coded white rows), and `selectedBg` defaults to the\n--ft-row-selected token so the selection follows the theme. Passing the prop\nstill wins.\n\nNew in src/lib: theme.js (the token maps, with LIGHT doubling as the inline\nvar() fallback table), stylesheet.js (the sheet as pure React-free data, so the\nbuild can emit it as a .css file too) and slots.js (cx, the slot resolvers and\nthe unstyled gate). New exports: styleText, CORE_TOKENS, LIGHT, DARK,\ntokenNames, tokenProp, CLASS_SLOTS, COMPONENT_SLOTS.\n\nreact-table trap worth recording: decorateColumn MUTATES each column object, so\nwhatever `defaultColumn` stamps on a column the first time survives for the life\nof that object. Closing the default Filter over a FilterInput therefore froze\nthat slot at mount. The resolved slot map is forwarded onto the table instance\nas `ui` — the route userList and context already take — and read fresh instead.\n\nTests: 30 golden snapshots (all 30 rewritten, since every element now paints\nthrough var(); the diff was read for geometry, which is byte-identical), 150\nunit checks including the token/slot registries, and 74 jsdom checks covering\nthe cascade, the theme stamp, the tokens prop, the class slots, a replaced\ncomponent, a null slot and unstyled. One pre-existing test bug fixed on the way:\na footer total asserted en-US grouping and failed on any en-IN machine.\n\nDemo: eight presets — Default, Dark, Auto, Brand, ERP, Custom CSS, Slots,\nUnstyled — every one of them driven from example/demo.css rather than from JSX,\nbecause the thing being demonstrated is that a consumer''s stylesheet is enough.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"da313148f1bcee3a52c3b8d2a2b18bf3ee2e7d05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/trees/da313148f1bcee3a52c3b8d2a2b18bf3ee2e7d05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/commits/3f499ab0aa40ce9c61d3350e37d4f18656d98009","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/3f499ab0aa40ce9c61d3350e37d4f18656d98009","node_id":"C_kwDOT9Ec4doAKDNmNDk5YWIwYWE0MGNlOWM2MWQzMzUwZTM3ZDRmMTg2NTZkOTgwMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/881f05ec285f86a4aac81696692be008da32d7ff","sha":"881f05ec285f86a4aac81696692be008da32d7ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/881f05ec285f86a4aac81696692be008da32d7ff"}],"sha":"3f499ab0aa40ce9c61d3350e37d4f18656d98009","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/3f499ab0aa40ce9c61d3350e37d4f18656d98009"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/881f05ec285f86a4aac81696692be008da32d7ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T06:23:32Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T06:23:32Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"message":"v1.0.0 — column type/footer shorthands, built-in toolbar, layout save/restore, src split into modules\n\nThe release is about how much a caller has to write for the same table. Every 0.x\nprop, column key and ref method still works and still means what it did.\n\nNew:\n- `type` (text/number/currency/date/datetime/boolean/serial) and `footer`\n  (sum/avg/min/max/count) column shorthands, plus format/decimals/dateFormat/\n  booleanLabels/blankZero — a column is one line again instead of a Cell, an\n  align, a width pair and a reduce.\n- `toolbar`: the Columns and Freeze menus, rendered by the component. It drives\n  the same ref API a hand-built menu always did, and sits outside .ft-wrap so the\n  freeze is untouched.\n- getLayout()/setLayout()/resetLayout(), `defaultLayout`, `onLayoutChange` — all\n  four layout choices as one value, for views saved per user rather than per\n  browser.\n- `context`, so a Cell reaches the caller''s callbacks without a column factory.\n- `status` in place of the loading + dataFetched pair.\n- locale/currencySymbol/dateFormat/dateTimeFormat, setColumnWidths(map).\n\nTwo behaviour changes:\n- A `width` with no `minWidth` now sets the minWidth too. A column narrower than\n  react-table''s 90px floor used to be silently widened, and the only fix was to\n  repeat the number.\n- `height` keeps its unit. height=\"100%\" used to parse to a 100-pixel table.\n\nRefactor: FreezeTable.js was 1796 lines; it is now a 379-line shell over\nsrc/lib (pure column maths and the shorthand layer), src/hooks (one concern\neach) and src/components. Behaviour is unchanged and held there by 30 golden\nsnapshots that compare the whole server-rendered markup byte-for-byte — every\none of them identical across the split.\n\nTests: `npm test` is now build + smoke + golden + 113 unit checks over src/lib +\n50 jsdom checks that mount the bundle and drive it (windowing, keyboard\nnavigation, the toolbar menus, the layout round-trip). Rows render only after\nthe row band is measured, so none of that half was covered before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1986d8b893d676999ebc44d4c27c656913f6828a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/trees/1986d8b893d676999ebc44d4c27c656913f6828a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/commits/881f05ec285f86a4aac81696692be008da32d7ff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/881f05ec285f86a4aac81696692be008da32d7ff","node_id":"C_kwDOT9Ec4doAKDg4MWYwNWVjMjg1Zjg2YTRhYWM4MTY5NjY5MmJlMDA4ZGEzMmQ3ZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/497dbeba6a349ca263d88d9dda611b84b9e38339","sha":"497dbeba6a349ca263d88d9dda611b84b9e38339","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/497dbeba6a349ca263d88d9dda611b84b9e38339"}],"sha":"881f05ec285f86a4aac81696692be008da32d7ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/881f05ec285f86a4aac81696692be008da32d7ff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/497dbeba6a349ca263d88d9dda611b84b9e38339/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T13:56:20Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T13:56:20Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"message":"add an npm run release script that loads .env for the auth token\n\nA bare npm publish resolves .npmrc''s ${NPM_TOKEN} to nothing (nothing sources\n.env) and fails with a 401.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"75c800ffb38d6fb2b5c7337e014556dab2c09b6e","url":"https://api.git