,"email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"message":"v0.4.0 — freeze columns against the right edge too\n\nColumns could only be frozen against the left edge. Wide lists usually\nwant the identity columns held on the left AND the row''s actions or its\ntotal held on the right, so `pinned: ''right''` now freezes a trailing run\nthe same way `pinned: true` freezes a leading one.\n\nSymmetry throughout: a `rightPinCount` alongside `pinCount`, its own\nviewport cap and localStorage key (`ctPinR:<key>`), and\ngetRightPinCount / getMaxRightPinCount / setRightPinCount on the ref. The\nright block is measured first and the left one funded from what is left,\nso the two caps cannot both claim the same viewport.\n\nThe Action column joins the right block whenever it is non-empty, mirroring\nthe status strip joining the left one — either would otherwise be stranded\noutside its own block. The right block''s boundary column carries the same\nblue pin marker, and casts its shadow leftwards until the scroll reaches\nthe end.\n\nImplementation mirrors the left side exactly: `position: sticky` with a\n`right` offset equal to the total width of the frozen columns beyond it.\nNothing new runs per scroll frame.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"438667dbb8b2af7bd2755be46344c0cd569f4cd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/trees/438667dbb8b2af7bd2755be46344c0cd569f4cd2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/commits/425aa76aec314c8891f6d2573317e3825b94311d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/425aa76aec314c8891f6d2573317e3825b94311d","node_id":"C_kwDOT9Ec4doAKDQyNWFhNzZhZWMzMTRjODg5MWY2ZDI1NzMzMTdlMzgyNWI5NDMxMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/6e00c9035c5954936b41f81bd5bbe91fa4f09dd1","sha":"6e00c9035c5954936b41f81bd5bbe91fa4f09dd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/6e00c9035c5954936b41f81bd5bbe91fa4f09dd1"}],"sha":"425aa76aec314c8891f6d2573317e3825b94311d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/425aa76aec314c8891f6d2573317e3825b94311d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/6e00c9035c5954936b41f81bd5bbe91fa4f09dd1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T06:17:56Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T06:17:56Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"message":"v0.3.1 — row snapping off by default, and suspended while scrolling\n\nContinuous wheel scrolling stuttered: `proximity` snapping re-settles the\nscroll onto a row on every wheel notch, so the list caught repeatedly\ninstead of gliding.\n\nSnapping and free scrolling genuinely trade against each other, and free\nscrolling is the better default — the partial row along the header''s edge\nis cosmetic, the stutter is felt on every scroll. `rowSnap` now defaults\nto false.\n\nWhen it is enabled it no longer stutters either: snapping is switched off\nwhile the wheel is turning and restored ~160 ms after it stops, so the\nscroll glides and settles once at the end.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e108774ad13f1f1f38f7c41f5d8ce23de91c28ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/trees/e108774ad13f1f1f38f7c41f5d8ce23de91c28ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/commits/6e00c9035c5954936b41f81bd5bbe91fa4f09dd1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/6e00c9035c5954936b41f81bd5bbe91fa4f09dd1","node_id":"C_kwDOT9Ec4doAKDZlMDBjOTAzNWM1OTU0OTM2YjQxZjgxYmQ1YmJlOTFmYTRmMDlkZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/63a6adac345f31996833b46a64228159cac1f111","sha":"63a6adac345f31996833b46a64228159cac1f111","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/63a6adac345f31996833b46a64228159cac1f111"}],"sha":"6e00c9035c5954936b41f81bd5bbe91fa4f09dd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/6e00c9035c5954936b41f81bd5bbe91fa4f09dd1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/63a6adac345f31996833b46a64228159cac1f111/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T06:13:40Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T06:13:40Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"message":"v0.3.0 — draw the scrollbars so the vertical bar sits beside the rows\n\n.ft-wrap spans the header and the footer as well as the rows, so its\nnative vertical scrollbar ran the full height of the table: the thumb sat\nbeside the header, which does not scroll, and read as a bug.\n\nThat bar cannot simply be moved onto the body. An element that scrolls in\ny is a scroll container in x too, so the body would become the sticky\nscrollport for the pinned cells and the frozen columns would slide away\nwith the rest of the row — the react-window problem this component was\nrewritten to escape.\n\nSo the native bars are hidden and redrawn as overlays on a new\npositioned root element, with the vertical track inset by the measured\nheader and footer heights so it spans the row band exactly. Both axes are\ndrawn, not just the vertical one: Firefox''s scrollbar-width takes no\naxis, and drawing both keeps them identical across browsers.\n\nWheel, trackpad, keyboard and touch scrolling stay native. Thumbs are\npositioned from the rAF-throttled handler that already drives the\nwindowing, so no extra render happens per frame. Dragging a thumb\nsuspends row snapping for the duration, which otherwise made the drag\nfeel sticky.\n\nBreaking: there is a new root element, and `className` / `style` now land\non it rather than on the scroller.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"034b58c65d3c7524d35ed75d0430068637fe3a7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/trees/034b58c65d3c7524d35ed75d0430068637fe3a7f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/commits/63a6adac345f31996833b46a64228159cac1f111","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/63a6adac345f31996833b46a64228159cac1f111","node_id":"C_kwDOT9Ec4doAKDYzYTZhZGFjMzQ1ZjMxOTk2ODMzYjQ2YTY0MjI4MTU5Y2FjMWYxMTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/0235a2e98f467cb7c3945862adb54724c55cb094","sha":"0235a2e98f467cb7c3945862adb54724c55cb094","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/0235a2e98f467cb7c3945862adb54724c55cb094"}],"sha":"63a6adac345f31996833b46a64228159cac1f111","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/63a6adac345f31996833b46a64228159cac1f111"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/0235a2e98f467cb7c3945862adb54724c55cb094/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T06:05:31Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T06:05:31Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"message":"v0.2.1 — settle vertical scrolling on a row boundary\n\nSince ft-wrap is the single scrollport and the header is sticky inside it,\nrows scroll under the header, so a freely-scrolled list always left a\nhalf-row sliced off along the header''s bottom edge — it read as a\nrendering fault rather than as scroll position.\n\nVertical scrolling now snaps to a row: `scroll-snap-type: y proximity`\nplus `scroll-snap-align: start` on each row, with `scroll-padding-top`\nset to the measured header height so a snapped row lands just below the\nheader instead of at the hidden top of the scrollport. Pure CSS, nothing\nper frame in JS, and the horizontal axis is untouched.\n\n`proximity` rather than `mandatory`: rows are windowed, so snap targets\ncome and go while scrolling, and mandatory snapping fights that as well\nas programmatic scrolls and the end of the list.\n\nNew `rowSnap` prop (default true) turns it off.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c873ae7ec9804d303bd6360020c1e7d094784219","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/trees/c873ae7ec9804d303bd6360020c1e7d094784219"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/commits/0235a2e98f467cb7c3945862adb54724c55cb094","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/0235a2e98f467cb7c3945862adb54724c55cb094","node_id":"C_kwDOT9Ec4doAKDAyMzVhMmU5OGY0NjdjYjdjMzk0NTg2MmFkYjU0NzI0YzU1Y2IwOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commit/ae51cd0789444f45b230fdab0e2d887f892ebf49","sha":"ae51cd0789444f45b230fdab0e2d887f892ebf49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/ae51cd0789444f45b230fdab0e2d887f892ebf49"}],"sha":"0235a2e98f467cb7c3945862adb54724c55cb094","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/0235a2e98f467cb7c3945862adb54724c55cb094"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Abhimishra2424","id":47156246,"login":"Abhimishra2424","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTU2MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/commits/ae51cd0789444f45b230fdab0e2d887f892ebf49/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T05:50:25Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T05:50:25Z","email":"abmishra700@gmail.com","name":"Abhishek Mishra"},"message":"v0.2.0 — bundle react-table instead of requiring it as a peer\n\nInstalling into a React 19 app failed outright: react-table v7''s peer\nrange is frozen at React 18 (the v7 line is archived), so npm declined to\ninstall it and the consumer''s build died with\n\n    Can''t resolve ''react-table'' in .../node_modules/freeze-table/dist\n\nreact-table also ships CommonJS/UMD only, so there was no clean ESM path\neither. It is now bundled into both builds (the production build — callers\nnever talk to react-table directly, so its dev warnings are not useful\nhere), leaving `react` as the sole peer dependency and making\n`npm i freeze-table` sufficient on React 16 through 19.\n\nA second copy alongside an app''s own react-table cannot conflict: v7 is\nplain hooks with no shared context.\n\nIts MIT notice is reproduced in LICENSE and in the banner of every built\nfile. Builds grow from ~42 kB to ~100 kB unminified.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"097bef5827e295ba518b1e2a5a021732089030f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/trees/097bef5827e295ba518b1e2a5a021732089030f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Abhimishra2424/freeze-table/git/commits/ae51cd0789444f45b230fdab0e2d887f892ebf49","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47156246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abhimishra2424/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"