://api.github.com/users/ramsandspace-glitch/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramsandspace-glitch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramsandspace-glitch/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramsandspace-glitch","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ram02112/DepGraph/commits/7622c1cd554448a30a10186478c39d004734861c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T12:37:58Z","email":"ram.sandspace@gmail.com","name":"ramsandspace-glitch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T12:37:58Z","email":"ram.sandspace@gmail.com","name":"ramsandspace-glitch"},"message":"Full-stack graph application answering three questions about an\norganisation''s dependency estate: which applications contain a vulnerable\npackage, what chain pulls it in, and what single upgrade clears the most\nrisk.\n\nStack: Node 20, Express 4, React 18 + Vite, plain JavaScript with ES\nmodules, neo4j-driver over Bolt. One Express process serves the API and\nthe built client in production.\n\nBackend: layered route → service → repository → Cypher constant, with all\nCypher isolated in cypher.js and every value passed as a parameter.\nDeterministic dataset generator and idempotent batch loader seed 3,464\nnodes and 17,371 relationships.\n\nClient: seven routes, design tokens, skeleton loading states, and\nPathChain — dependency chains rendered as a vertical lockfile tree.","tree":{"sha":"dc7a151affdb07df9a85f669d1739ba14aacf93e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ram02112/DepGraph/git/trees/dc7a151affdb07df9a85f669d1739ba14aacf93e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Ram02112/DepGraph/git/commits/7622c1cd554448a30a10186478c39d004734861c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230960028?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/u