lms/designer/commit/d4fb73f7f6d16ccd5832dddfe256bcd6ff0c643e","sha":"d4fb73f7f6d16ccd5832dddfe256bcd6ff0c643e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/commits/d4fb73f7f6d16ccd5832dddfe256bcd6ff0c643e"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/coolms/designer/commit/54e996b35e83cdaa77fde4822652e5f13270c879","sha":"54e996b35e83cdaa77fde4822652e5f13270c879","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/commits/54e996b35e83cdaa77fde4822652e5f13270c879"}],"sha":"3361c754480b162e3e86bc4bf4ed82325c5476f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/commits/3361c754480b162e3e86bc4bf4ed82325c5476f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7189630?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thugstar","id":7189630,"login":"thugstar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODk2MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/commits/54e996b35e83cdaa77fde4822652e5f13270c879/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:42:02Z","email":"d.popov@altgraphic.com","name":"Dmitry Popov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:42:02Z","email":"d.popov@altgraphic.com","name":"Dmitry Popov"},"message":"The bundle check reads an import statement, not a property named from\n\nThe zero-dependency check grepped dist/index.mjs for anything ending in from\" and a non-dot character. The bundle legitimately contains key === \"from\" and \"data-transition-from\" from the state-machine and DRD editors, so the check failed on its own package with no external import anywhere in it. The pattern now anchors on an import or export statement, or a dynamic import(), and still catches a bare specifier there.","tree":{"sha":"c2d4ffe3105cdc01c0f330b7480cda03e5f623bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/git/trees/c2d4ffe3105cdc01c0f330b7480cda03e5f623bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/git/commits/54e996b35e83cdaa77fde4822652e5f13270c879","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7189630?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thugstar","id":7189630,"login":"thugstar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODk2MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/coolms/designer/commit/54e996b35e83cdaa77fde4822652e5f13270c879","node_id":"C_kwDOT9ZoF9oAKDU0ZTk5NmIzNWU4M2NkYWE3N2ZkZTQ4MjI2NTJlNWYxMzI3MGM4Nzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/coolms/designer/commit/39fad407a86a6fe1fc91a159864cd47ad9ec60d1","sha":"39fad407a86a6fe1fc91a159864cd47ad9ec60d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/commits/39fad407a86a6fe1fc91a159864cd47ad9ec60d1"}],"sha":"54e996b35e83cdaa77fde4822652e5f13270c879","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/commits/54e996b35e83cdaa77fde4822652e5f13270c879"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7189630?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thugstar","id":7189630,"login":"thugstar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODk2MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/commits/39fad407a86a6fe1fc91a159864cd47ad9ec60d1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T22:09:04Z","email":"d.popov@altgraphic.com","name":"Dmitry Popov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T22:09:04Z","email":"d.popov@altgraphic.com","name":"Dmitry Popov"},"message":"Ascii in comments and changelogs\n\nSame rule as the PHP pass, applied to the TypeScript sources and the changelogs.\n\nComment ranges come from the TypeScript parser, and two things had to be got\nright before the numbers meant anything:\n\n  - getLeadingCommentRanges SCANS FORWARD from the position it is handed. Given\n    a position inside a template literal it reports the `//` of `https://` as a\n    line comment, so literal spans are collected first and any range touching\n    one is refused.\n  - the invariant is the PARSED leaf-token stream, with JSDoc nodes skipped. A\n    raw scanner has no parser context and swallows a whole template region --\n    comments included -- into one token; and a JSDoc node''s text IS the comment.\n    Each mistake made the check refuse hundreds of files it should have passed.\n\nLETTERS AND EMOJI ARE KEPT, as before. The paperclip in the attachment comment\nand the object-replacement character in the editor comment are both the SUBJECT\nof the sentence -- the second is a literal in the code on the next line.\n\nVerified: for every file, the token stream is identical before and after.\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1c80b2c661671f1bbc6e0501e088c9f6219e0286","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/git/trees/1c80b2c661671f1bbc6e0501e088c9f6219e0286"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/git/commits/39fad407a86a6fe1fc91a159864cd47ad9ec60d1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7189630?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thugstar","id":7189630,"login":"thugstar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODk2MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/coolms/designer/commit/39fad407a86a6fe1fc91a159864cd47ad9ec60d1","node_id":"C_kwDOT9ZoF9oAKDM5ZmFkNDA3YTg2YTZmZTFmYzkxYTE1OTg2NGNkNDdhZDllYzYwZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/coolms/designer/commit/3d74516b5eab889655211cfbb30f440d8cf88f38","sha":"3d74516b5eab889655211cfbb30f440d8cf88f38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/commits/3d74516b5eab889655211cfbb30f440d8cf88f38"}],"sha":"39fad407a86a6fe1fc91a159864cd47ad9ec60d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/commits/39fad407a86a6fe1fc91a159864cd47ad9ec60d1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7189630?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thugstar","id":7189630,"login":"thugstar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODk2MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/commits/3d74516b5eab889655211cfbb30f440d8cf88f38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T15:42:09Z","email":"d.popov@altgraphic.com","name":"Dmitry Popov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T15:42:09Z","email":"d.popov@altgraphic.com","name":"Dmitry Popov"},"message":"Name a stand-in rather than the consuming application in a fixture\n\nThe guard reported an application class in the render test: a published\npackage must not name code that consumes it. It is fixture data, so the specific\nclass carried no information -- `Acme\\\\` says the same thing about shape and\nclaims nothing about anyone''s application.\n\nIt surfaced only after the previous commit, because the guard scans tracked\nfiles and this one was untracked until then. Worth knowing for the next package:\na clean guard run against a tree with untracked work in it is not a clean guard\nrun.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nReworded: the original named a technology or an application class\nthat a reader of this package should not have to know about.","tree":{"sha":"d956389ee8867c44d343a17f82247e4037920b56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/git/trees/d956389ee8867c44d343a17f82247e4037920b56"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/git/commits/3d74516b5eab889655211cfbb30f440d8cf88f38","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7189630?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thugstar","id":7189630,"login":"thugstar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODk2MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/coolms/designer/commit/3d74516b5eab889655211cfbb30f440d8cf88f38","node_id":"C_kwDOT9ZoF9oAKDNkNzQ1MTZiNWVhYjg4OTY1NTIxMWNmYmIzMGY0NDBkOGNmODhmMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/coolms/designer/commit/94b957f47dcddb08a33553f7028d4875f6902aed","sha":"94b957f47dcddb08a33553f7028d4875f6902aed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/commits/94b957f47dcddb08a33553f7028d4875f6902aed"}],"sha":"3d74516b5eab889655211cfbb30f440d8cf88f38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/commits/3d74516b5eab889655211cfbb30f440d8cf88f38"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7189630?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thugstar","id":7189630,"login":"thugstar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODk2MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/commits/94b957f47dcddb08a33553f7028d4875f6902aed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T15:40:51Z","email":"d.popov@altgraphic.com","name":"Dmitry Popov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T15:40:51Z","email":"d.popov@altgraphic.com","name":"Dmitry Popov"},"message":"Publish a read-only render path\n\n`createEditor` builds the shell and stops there, so drawing a diagram required\na submodule import plus three members of the Editor handle that carry an\ninternal-API caveat -- a seam published at one end only. `renderDiagram` is the\nother end: model in, mounted diagram out, `DiagramView.toSvg` to serialize,\nusing nothing a consumer is told not to depend on.\n\nThe three deserializers go with it. Without them \"model in\" is a requirement no\npublic API could meet, and the seam would be closed at one end again one step\nearlier. Serializers stay out: writing a definition back belongs to an editing\nhost, which assembles the surface itself.\n\nEditing is unchanged and still assembled by the host -- it needs a palette, a\nproperty panel and a save path, all of which differ per surface.\n\nThe state machine''s wire format is described by its shape rather than by the\nframework that emits it. The publish guard flagged the entry point for naming a\nframework this package does not depend on and cannot, which is correct: a\nreader of the published API would infer a coupling that does not exist. The\nsame sentence was in renderDiagram.ts and was NOT reported, because untracked\nfiles are not scanned -- committing the reported fix alone would have re-broken\nthe guard on a line nobody had been shown.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d47b4dd1d1c9bf3c6da3bcdbe18a316c2bbb066d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/git/trees/d47b4dd1d1c9bf3c6da3bcdbe18a316c2bbb066d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/git/commits/94b957f47dcddb08a33553f7028d4875f6902aed","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7189630?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/follo