ccd5832dddfe256bcd6ff0c643e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/commits/d4fb73f7f6d16ccd5832dddfe256bcd6ff0c643e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7189630?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thugstar","id":7189630,"login":"thugstar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODk2MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/commits/f779764ab087b03455e5bc4d77d99133eb2bc085/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T16:27:18Z","email":"d.popov@altgraphic.com","name":"Dmitry Popov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T16:27:18Z","email":"d.popov@altgraphic.com","name":"Dmitry Popov"},"message":"Dark mode, a theming contract that can be reached, and a changelog\n\nDark mode for all four surfaces, driven by `data-theme` on any ancestor rather\nthan `prefers-color-scheme`: an editor embedded in an application has to match\nthe application, and asking the browser makes the two disagree on any machine\nwhose OS setting and chosen theme differ.\n\nThe dividing line for what flips is SATURATION, not selector. A BPMN task''s\nrect carries both a paper fill and a near-black stroke -- both must flip, or\nthe shape is a white hole in a dark canvas and its outline vanishes into its\nown fill -- while the start event''s green and the end event''s red mean\nsomething and stay. Classifying by selector gets all four wrong, and they are\nin the same rule.\n\n59 chrome literals tokenised, 40 notation literals left alone, behind a core\nvocabulary of 28 tokens on `.coolms-designer`. The 21 role tokens keep their\nnames and their declaring elements but resolve THROUGH the core, so the dark\nblock re-points one set and the whole surface follows.\n\nTwo documentation lies fixed at source. The stylesheet header and the contract\ncomment both told the next person to override from `:root`, which paints\nnothing: every token is declared on the element that consumes it, and a\ndeclaration on an element beats a value inherited from an ancestor. It is not\na specificity contest -- the two rules match different elements, so they never\ncompete, and no amount of specificity on a `:root` selector changes it. That\nmatters because the specificity framing predicts a more specific root selector\nwould work, and none does.\n\nCHANGELOG.md is new, and `files` now carries it -- written and then excluded\nfrom the tarball would have defeated the point. It starts at this publish, so\nnothing in it is reconstructed.\n\nDated rather than left as \"unreleased\": a heading that says unreleased is\nfalse the moment it publishes, which is the same defect that had\ncore-angular''s npm page telling readers the package was not on npm.\n\nThe stylesheet and the theming work are the Site session''s; this commit\ncarries them because that session has no commit mandate in this workstream and\nmine does. The date on the changelog heading is mine.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f47bd79b857fc081832e989ba84ad262a966a22a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/git/trees/f47bd79b857fc081832e989ba84ad262a966a22a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/git/commits/f779764ab087b03455e5bc4d77d99133eb2bc085","ve