7d8fcedc7764c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T14:31:53Z","email":"d.popov@altgraphic.com","name":"Dmitry Popov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T14:31:53Z","email":"d.popov@altgraphic.com","name":"Dmitry Popov"},"message":"Ship a message extractor, and split two colliding keys it found\n\nA catalogue has to be generated from the fallbacks, not written by hand:\nthe fallbacks are what the code actually renders, so anything maintained\nalongside them drifts, and the drift is invisible -- the editor keeps\nshowing its inline English while the catalogue quietly describes\nsomething else.\n\n`npm run i18n:extract` prints `{key: english}` for every message. It\nparses `t(''key'', ''fallback'')` with a small scanner rather than a regex,\nbecause the fallbacks wrap across lines, contain escaped quotes and\napostrophes, and mix quote styles -- all of which a regex gets wrong\nquietly. Three keys are composed at runtime from closed sets; those are\nexpanded from the same maps that hold their English, and a composed key\nwith no expansion rule fails the run rather than leaving a hole.\n\nWriting it immediately paid: it found TWO KEYS CARRYING TWO DIFFERENT\nENGLISH TEXTS. The boundary-event and catch-event field tables were both\nscoped `common` by the earlier conversion, so \"On timeout\" and \"Wait\"\nshared one key, as did two different subtype descriptions. A catalogue\ncan hold only one translation per key, so one of each pair would have\nrendered the wrong sentence in every translated locale. They are now\nscoped apart.\n\nAlso closes three gaps in the translator chain: the BPMN-Lite and\nstate-machine property panels and the DMN table editor each DEFAULT their\nown provider when a host supplies none, and those defaults were building\nEnglish ones -- so a host could pass a translator to the editor and still\nget English fields.\n\n970 tests, typecheck and build pass.","tree":{"sha":"1d4afa54f93e7307c6e682ab5e5f390a8a8631cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/git/trees/1d4afa54f93e7307c6e682ab5e5f390a8a8631cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/git/commits/20d291cbfb02455d7db89f0c2517d8fcedc7764c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7189630?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thugstar","id":7189630,"login":"thugstar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODk2MzA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thugstar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/coolms/designer/commit/20d291cbfb02455d7db89f0c2517d8fcedc7764c","node_id":"C_kwDOT9ZoF9oAKDIwZDI5MWNiZmIwMjQ1NWQ3ZGI4OWYwYzI1MTdkOGZjZWRjNzc2NGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/coolms/designer/commit/8ab1a9212d6b16565da7283719e10cd9a1f91964","sha":"8ab1a9212d6b16565da7283719e10cd9a1f91964","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/commits/8ab1a9212d6b16565da7283719e10cd9a1f91964"}],"sha":"20d291cbfb02455d7db89f0c2517d8fcedc7764c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coolms/designer/commits/20d291cbfb02455d7db89f0c2517d8fcedc7764c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7192008?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coolms/events{/privacy}","followers_url