.com/anthonidev","id":61163166,"login":"anthonidev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMTYzMTY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonidev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonidev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonidev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonidev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonidev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anthonidev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthonidev/pokedex-microfront/commits/d578b625082d3f8389cc71376a6e28575d6f4b5d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T13:57:20Z","email":"softwaretoni21@gmail.com","name":"anthonidev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T13:57:20Z","email":"softwaretoni21@gmail.com","name":"anthonidev"},"message":"feat: prepare the 3 apps for a static Vercel deploy\n\n- Module Federation needs each remote''s entry URL at build time. Shell''s\n  vite.config.ts now reads VITE_MF1_ENTRY_URL/VITE_MF2_ENTRY_URL, falling\n  back to the localhost dev servers so `pnpm dev` needs no setup.\n- vercel.json per app: SPA rewrite on Shell (client-side routes 404 on\n  refresh otherwise), Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * on both remotes\n  (Module Federation loads their remoteEntry.js cross-origin from Shell''s\n  domain — fails silently without CORS headers).\n- README: Deploy section with the concrete Vercel dashboard steps (3\n  separate projects, deploy order, where the env vars go) and an updated\n  Testing section (was still describing zero coverage).\n\nNo backend of its own (PokeAPI is called straight from the browser), so\nthis stays framework-static — no Docker, no server process needed.","tree":{"sha":"7ae723e3ecc51818433f286d99526ce56a773227","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthonidev/pokedex-microfront/git/trees/7ae723e3ecc51818433f286d99526ce56a773227"},"url":"https://a