:"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/6c6126ff659d8cb1928c07097704427ff847a887/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:14:17Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:14:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(host+every-plugin): SlotResolver, snapshot-owned serving caches, export-map generation (C6+C7+C8) (#310)\n\n* refactor(host): SlotResolver — one entryUrls seam over the 9-site matrix; SSR resolvers, UiRemoteEntry, buster conventions die (C6)\n\n* refactor(host): RuntimeSnapshot owns the serving compose + client-config caches — atomic swap by construction, swap-under-traffic test (C7, absorbs regression-prod-stacks/09 E7)\n\n* refactor(every-plugin): export map derived from tsdown entries + dead-surface sweep (C8, major)\n\n* refactor: review fixes — comments stripped, shared-entry dedupe, derived criticality, BosEnv-tight entryUrls, subpath guard, enforced local-slot invariant\n\n* fix(host): dev-local compose payload omits manifestUrl for local slots\n\nTwo post-rebase corrections:\n- C7''s body no longer uses Context/Layer — trim them from the effect import\n  (conflict-resolution leftover against the #307 lint-cleanup base).\n- the dev-local compose test still expected manifestUrl on the plugin remote,\n  but it sets ui.localPath, and local slots never carry a browser manifest\n  (a relative entry would resolve against the page origin and register the\n  wrong container). Drop the field; remote-slot presence is covered by the\n  payload and client-mirror tests.","tree":{"sha":"7f376bff2ec6bee9d4c0535c85075c4b8ee6836a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/trees/7f376bff2ec6bee9d4c0535c85075c4b8ee6836a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/commits/6c6126ff659d8cb1928c07097704427ff847a887","verification":{"payload":"tree 7f376bff2ec6bee9d4c0535c85075c4b8ee6836a\nparent 4ecd6ad9da736b92019602be4fc7ff421b5d4101\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1790964857 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790964857 -0500\n\nrefactor(host+every-plugin): SlotResolver, snapshot-owned serving caches, export-map generation (C6+C7+C8) (#310)\n\n* refactor(host): SlotResolver — one entryUrls seam over the 9-site matrix; SSR resolvers, UiRemoteEntry, buster conventions die (C6)\n\n* refactor(host): RuntimeSnapshot owns the serving compose + client-config caches — atomic swap by construction, swap-under-traffic test (C7, absorbs regression-prod-stacks/09 E7)\n\n* refactor(every-plugin): export map derived from tsdown entries + dead-surface sweep (C8, major)\n\n* refactor: review fixes — comments stripped, shared-entry dedupe, derived criticality, BosEnv-tight entryUrls, subpath guard, enforced local-slot invariant\n\n* fix(host): dev-local compose payload omits manifestUrl for local slots\n\nTwo post-rebase corrections:\n- C7''s body no longer uses Context/Layer — trim them from the effect import\n  (conflict-resolution leftover against the #307 lint-cleanup base).\n- the dev-local compose test still expected manifestUrl on the plugin remote,\n  but it sets ui.localPath, and local slots never carry a browser manifest\n  (a relative entry would resolve against the page origin and register the\n  wrong container). Drop the field; remote-slot presence is covered by the\n  payload and client-mirror tests.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv/R5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQB4QAABAfKTvRWDWfkQ4QNgIS8qx\nai6R5hBA7PDYLJRrSDnk7QgcCD9yy2Ns1iu7E+OSNqoudLi3EAAEyXKlRP0v7UOr\nlo16JktNFeXS+d1pqSDp84YmPnTpOy643l3oi2i65QaUrj2Uq+b+cjb3E+Ryhzv7\nP21sQQeD0fy8/g/iT+ibGPCBIH4FLllF1bMEnm3oGcwgxt7THTvgGgAvz6X0ewYa\nT4JG0ODk50WRrDjh502Vk21YJliCEMfiI0bwgBwNezNTeQoyAk3eyg+E1OyRmKLD\nFpZtkP0t49Ge1gmsIS5qgwfzfBPb9yLaUpfkbg0zM5qIJG7wdkSFMDsEhIobypNG\nXmRfa/ArdPhmncoeiJKmf7iijuYmqFWjsPCyOzbVXnSgKhvx8SqypUAkhzBrjKLx\njcgk0L8IAZtGpbgYkkqCvCk2uMIGaFqmMD1Y0CFiXegycbhBZQNnR6A27gi4OitC\nFIe0uLSS93hBYLplQT92W16/psJ+/uTWru++h5B7lKcqsxqHD/QXHYiuevT/GnE6\noFYeAvryio9/qhnYkX91EEwc9ueZUQtRxHOhtbz2m/Le7v7JPI4VzrwcQF7CGcL8\ngBxZzlAgI+ecIT9pzeeZaam4h5KaVJQbDz2adpSAHQFmyEq00QsKh9A++HOA+gDu\npaapGoUq6VXhtN6C4JZ/\n=xqnx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T18:14:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/6c6126ff659d8cb1928c07097704427ff847a887","node_id":"C_kwDOT-K1MdoAKDZjNjEyNmZmNjU5ZDhjYjE5MjhjMDcwOTc3MDQ0MjdmZjg0N2E4ODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/4ecd6ad9da736b92019602be4fc7ff421b5d4101","sha":"4ecd6ad9da736b92019602be4fc7ff421b5d4101","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/4ecd6ad9da736b92019602be4fc7ff421b5d4101"}],"sha":"6c6126ff659d8cb1928c07097704427ff847a887","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/6c6126ff659d8cb1928c07097704427ff847a887"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/4ecd6ad9da736b92019602be4fc7ff421b5d4101/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:14:17Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:14:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(every-plugin): PluginIdentity + SharedDependencySpec (C1+C2) (#309)\n\n* feat(every-plugin): PluginIdentity module — one derivation for npm/remote/container names; plugins/apps → plugins/registry through it (C1, app-model/11 rename)\n\n* feat(every-plugin): SharedDependencySpec — one shared-dep policy, loud unresolved versions, 4 consumers (C2, app-model/12)\n\n* test(everything-dev): follow plugins/apps → plugins/registry rename in repo-layout tests\n\nThe C1 rename (plugins/apps → plugins/registry, config key apps → registry)\npredates these integration tests; their REPO_ROOT-backed scaffolds and golden\nassertions still selected the old plugin key, so nothing was copied and the\nassertions failed. Update them to the registry key/path.\n\n* fix(every-plugin): dev-serve plugin id is the npm name — restore slug/schema agreement with the host\n\nThe host initializes plugins with the npm package name (runtimeId =\nplugin.name), whose migration slug takes the basename of the scope\n(''@everything-dev/proposals-plugin'' -> ''proposals''). resolveDevPluginId\nreturned the pre-normalized remote name, which normalizes to a different\nslug (''everything_dev_proposals''), so the plugin dev process applied its\nmigrations into a different schema than the host checks. The shared\njournal then reported every migration as already applied while the drift\ncheck found no tables, failing every plugin load in dev mode\n(drift-safe-repair) and hanging the dev regression suites.\n\nUse the raw npm name so both initialize sites agree on slug/schema;\nregisterRemote derives the remote name from it exactly as the host does.","tree":{"sha":"30845eed8ac0e1b5f44fbe2f2f44e7903b2edcd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/trees/30845eed8ac0e1b5f44fbe2f2f44e7903b2edcd8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/commits/4ecd6ad9da736b92019602be4fc7ff421b5d4101","verification":{"payload":"tree 30845eed8ac0e1b5f44fbe2f2f44e7903b2edcd8\nparent 0a692fc7b0f0c7cdd664e39327f5ed8f85fd1686\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1790964857 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790964857 -0500\n\nfeat(every-plugin): PluginIdentity + SharedDependencySpec (C1+C2) (#309)\n\n* feat(every-plugin): PluginIdentity module — one derivation for npm/remote/container names; plugins/apps → plugins/registry through it (C1, app-model/11 rename)\n\n* feat(every-plugin): SharedDependencySpec — one shared-dep policy, loud unresolved versions, 4 consumers (C2, app-model/12)\n\n* test(everything-dev): follow plugins/apps → plugins/registry rename in repo-layout tests\n\nThe C1 rename (plugins/apps → plugins/registry, config key apps → registry)\npredates these integration tests; their REPO_ROOT-backed scaffolds and golden\nassertions still selected the old plugin key, so nothing was copied and the\nassertions failed. Update them to the registry key/path.\n\n* fix(every-plugin): dev-serve plugin id is the npm name — restore slug/schema agreement with the host\n\nThe host initializes plugins with the npm package name (runtimeId =\nplugin.name), whose migration slug takes the basename of the scope\n(''@everything-dev/proposals-plugin'' -> ''proposals''). resolveDevPluginId\nreturned the pre-normalized remote name, which normalizes to a different\nslug (''everything_dev_proposals''), so the plugin dev process applied its\nmigrations into a different schema than the host checks. The shared\njournal then reported every migration as already applied while the drift\ncheck found no tables, failing every plugin load in dev mode\n(drift-safe-repair) and hanging the dev regression suites.\n\nUse the raw npm name so both initialize sites agree on slug/schema;\nregisterRemote derives the remote name from it exactly as the host does.","reason":"valid","signature"