s{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/a56e1da34181619bd109206d795bd7125c110ffc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:31:37Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T03:31:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(cli): self-healing dev preflight — two-command contributor setup (#303)\n\n* feat(cli): self-healing dev preflight — bos dev starts docker compose when local Postgres is down\n\n- Preflight failures now carry tcpReachable so recoverable (nothing-listening)\n  failures are distinguishable from credential/auth failures\n- New infra/docker.ts: pure shouldAutoStartDocker guard, daemon-aware\n  isDockerAvailable, runDockerComposeUp (extracted from cli/init.ts)\n- devBootstrap: when all failures are unreachable local services, the compose\n  file exists, docker is reachable, and the stack is not test-mode, run\n  docker compose up -d --wait under the dormant timing label and re-probe\n  once before failing; regression stacks (BOS_TEST/NODE_ENV=test/\n  BOS_NO_PERSIST_PORTS) never auto-start compose\n- bos init next-steps output and generated child docs drop the manual\n  docker compose / cp .env.example steps\n- CONTRIBUTING.md and AGENTS.md quick starts are now bun install && bun run dev\n\n* feat(dev): clean bootstrap output — piped compose, spinner label, quiet INFO logs\n\n- runDockerComposeUp captures output (stdio pipe + ANSI-stripped tail) instead\n  of inheriting the TTY, so docker compose''s progress renderer no longer\n  collides with the CLI spinner; bos init''s docker prompt consumes the result\n- dev phase label \"docker compose up\" renders as \"Starting local Postgres...\";\n  success is silent, failure appends the compose output tail to the preflight\n  error for diagnosis\n- dev bootstrap runs under References.MinimumLogLevel derived from\n  --log-level / BOS_LOG_LEVEL / DEBUG (default Warn), suppressing bootstrap\n  INFO logs like the [env] ... updated drift lines; --log-level info restores","tree":{"sha":"d92d6207201037ac898efb93f8b908e6b090f57f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/trees/d92d6207201037ac898efb93f8b908e6b090f57f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/commits/a56e1da34181619bd109206d795bd7125c110ffc","verification":{"payload":"tree d92d6207201037ac898efb93f8b908e6b090f57f\nparent 613206ea39c31ace52b75eb62d224afa49e79575\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1790911897 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790911897 -0500\n\nfeat(cli): self-healing dev preflight — two-command contributor setup (#303)\n\n* feat(cli): self-healing dev preflight — bos dev starts docker compose when local Postgres is down\n\n- Preflight failures now carry tcpReachable so recoverable (nothing-listening)\n  failures are distinguishable from credential/auth failures\n- New infra/docker.ts: pure shouldAutoStartDocker guard, daemon-aware\n  isDockerAvailable, runDockerComposeUp (extracted from cli/init.ts)\n- devBootstrap: when all failures are unreachable local services, the compose\n  file exists, docker is reachable, and the stack is not test-mode, run\n  docker compose up -d --wait under the dormant timing label and re-probe\n  once before failing; regression stacks (BOS_TEST/NODE_ENV=test/\n  BOS_NO_PERSIST_PORTS) never auto-start compose\n- bos init next-steps output and generated child docs drop the manual\n  docker compose / cp .env.example steps\n- CONTRIBUTING.md and AGENTS.md quick starts are now bun install && bun run dev\n\n* feat(dev): clean bootstrap output — piped compose, spinner label, quiet INFO logs\n\n- runDockerComposeUp captures output (stdio pipe + ANSI-stripped tail) instead\n  of inheriting the TTY, so docker compose''s progress renderer no longer\n  collides with the CLI spinner; bos init''s docker prompt consumes the result\n- dev phase label \"docker compose up\" renders as \"Starting local Postgres...\";\n  success is silent, failure appends the compose output tail to the preflight\n  error for diagnosis\n- dev bootstrap runs under References.MinimumLogLevel derived from\n  --log-level / BOS_LOG_LEVEL / DEBUG (default Warn), suppressing bootstrap\n  INFO logs like the [env] ... updated drift lines; --log-level info restores","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvyWZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAciwQAKwKP/PfB47yZd20GGpbKOTP\n5O15Eh/hx4LtrUdLAQ2/YsBxPRwyZ84Ykvi9TctPvvULoMXxGHRj+4iWP2qqlZNw\nMLOliHtlSqWZE5+eIzQYRiYYf71Ct+OwHnTTvcjBMR0aLf7R5e/V2/Xxu89oxYFC\nVLLKxPmlxCuFCTJ9Tt9c0ld2m8qD4rB5zzPMAyVTYx6r/4FNFxg9zOevKyqPru2M\npEVboNR3aelU2LN2QhXMCANjyvBV7RGL9hjaSzaMnrszRjpYtSC7U6V0o+FKpsyH\nnj0AbkGoM7a1WYtFKxUae+sQzK/esv9MdUIJszJN21bF0cu7WMPw/GyFCC1Z7u/y\n1tnfzRVILytgj4bTpsp9AXNOoRxE/9oFW/8Ssad9jyAD7X1nCYuO1SFysARaYByl\n6fNG2Y8/dHQXpNudVK7iWgEkcCi4lywbljWo8OkABOJPsNY/uUkcDqBqKhoFliCd\nWf5zEnV5eU9fz/Q5bz2NlZRDe1O+tRON39+pB8PyynC1xi8c3BzwfC/kaakjACsH\nCIw/tGJsoAXkM2LQLt4C2XPv56cPleFYEsIn1fwdy28cJKz1a56gPO/nLPawMCcx\nBbzScREhHDz1pzgMf/nv13byVzwa/zdd9bPpMDFXEPob2u6+sv6iKZWBaxfKD5yg\nLvE8ZmAdjJxRPNKyqbQd\n=u5+w\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T03:31:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/a56e1da34181619bd109206d795bd7125c110ffc","node_id":"C_kwDOT-K1MdoAKGE1NmUxZGEzNDE4MTYxOWJkMTA5MjA2ZDc5NWJkNzEyNWMxMTBmZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/613206ea39c31ace52b75eb62d224afa49e79575","sha":"613206ea39c31ace52b75eb62d224afa49e79575","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/613206ea39c31ace52b75eb62d224afa49e79575"}],"sha":"a56e1da34181619bd109206d795bd7125c110ffc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/a56e1da34181619bd109206d795bd7125c110ffc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/613206ea39c31ace52b75eb62d224afa49e79575/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T01:44:59Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T01:44:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(cli): consolidate bos deploy — one command, clean CI train (#296)\n\n* feat(cli): consolidate bos deploy into one command with preflight, image, and Railway legs\n\nbos deploy is now the full train (NEARBuilders/citynode.app#295): preflight\n(config, auth guards, signing, storage/CDN credentials, registry reachability\n— all before any build, fixing the ordering flaw where a missing\nBOS_STORAGE_API_KEY failed only after the build train), the staleness-checked\nbuild train, bundle upload to the R2-backed storage, FastKV publish with\nread-back confirmation, a runtime-image leg pushed to GHCR by short-SHA and\nlatest tags (ci.image -> BOS_IMAGE -> repository derivation), and a pull-only\nRailway deploy pinned to the pushed digest via a generated thin Dockerfile.\n\nbos publish becomes config-only; --deploy/--packages and bos build --deploy\nare removed. The railway redeploy branch (which re-shipped the old image) is\ndeleted. Deploy responses carry image/service; the storage upload response\ndiscloses the resolved backend (s3/memory) and bos deploy hard-fails on\nin-memory storage instead of silently losing bytes on restart.\n\nWorkflows shrink to checkout + bun run bos deploy + verification; docker.yml\nis absorbed. Child templates and scaffolded scripts ship the same shape.\nFixes stale edk_ key-prefix docs; adds the bos login --key CI bootstrap doc.\n\n* refactor(cli): apply code-review fixes to the deploy consolidation\n\n- pass process.env into resolveImageRef so BOS_IMAGE actually takes effect\n  outside unit tests\n- config-only publish test: assert the build train is never invoked\n- API storage backend-disclosure unit test (s3/memory) on StorageLive\n- trim JSDoc blocks to single-line comments per the no-comments standard\n- record spike outcome and review decisions in the sprint tickets\n  (RAILWAY_DOCKERFILE_PATH is Railway''s documented mechanism; prepare step\n  deliberately omitted from deploy workflows — staging empirically builds\n  prerequisites without it, and the effect patch only matters for\n  lint/typecheck)\n\n* feat(cli): authored cdn.origin guard — deploys never promote dev-resolved host URLs\n\nDeploy origins resolve env -> bosConfig.cdn.origin (extends-inherited) -> hard\nerror; the runtimeConfig.host.url derivation that published localhost:3000\nbundle URLs is gone. A session pinned to a local site is a hard error for\nuploads, env-pinned local origins warn, and the storage origin is probed\n(/.well-known/mcp.json) in preflight before the build train. Config-only\npublishes require no origins. ADR 0020 amendment + changeset.\n\n* feat(build): content-hashed deploy artifacts + version-manifest pointers (atomic-deploys 01-02)\n\nTicket 01 - hashed artifacts: entrypoints build as\nremoteEntry.[contenthash].js / remoteEntry.server.[contenthash].js (rsbuild\nweb+node envs, every-plugin rspack builds) with byte-identical legacy\nfixed-name aliases for the rollout window, hashed copies of mf-manifest.json\nand style.css, and a per-dist build-report.json for the deploy leg. Bundle\ncache classification is canonicalized in every-plugin/build/artifact-names:\ncontent-hashed names are immutable regardless of base name; fixed names must\nrevalidate (bundle-fs-resolve + api storage policy now share it). Verified\nagainst real ui (web+ssr) and api builds.\n\nTicket 02 - version manifests: new every-plugin/version-manifest export with\nthe immutable WorkspaceVersionManifest document and composeVersionManifest\n(version id = content-derived, key-order stable, builtAt excluded so\nunchanged bytes keep one id). Config slots gain a manifest pointer (versioned\nmanifest filename; integrity pins the manifest when set) through\nBosConfigSchema, the descriptor schemas, and both roundtrip field maps.\n\nDeploys are not yet additive end-to-end: the deploy leg (ticket 03) and\nderived resolution (ticket 04) consume the report + pointer; until then the\nlegacy aliases keep every existing consumer working. Spec: .scratch/\natomic-deploys/ (MAP + tickets).\n\n* test(config)+docs(adr): manifest pointer review follow-ups (atomic-deploys 01-02)\n\nExtends-merge semantics pinned by test: app slots inherit the parent''s\nmanifest field-wise (child override wins); child plugin entries replace\nparent entries wholesale (existing merge behavior — a child publishes its\nown manifests for every slot it ships). ADR 0020 amendment records the\nhashed-artifact + version-manifest + cache-classification decisions the\nphase-A commit made.\n\n* feat(build): version-manifest deploy leg + derived entry resolution (atomic-deploys 03-04)\n\nTicket 03 - deploy leg: the upload response''s server-computed SRI map plus\nthe ticket-01 build reports compose an immutable WorkspaceVersionManifest,\nuploaded additively at versions/<version>.json; deploy entries pin the slot\nby manifest pointer (manifest field; integrity becomes the manifest SRI when\npinned; legacy production/ssr fields still written during rollout).\nTransport hardening: status-0 retries ride fresh connections (connection:\nclose - the pooled keepalive socket race), 5 attempts with backoff+jitter;\nretryable statuses capped at 3; uploadBundle takes an injectable fetchImpl.\n\nTicket 04 - derived resolution: resolveSlotVersion fetches + SRI-verifies\nthe version manifest behind a content-addressed per-pin process cache (the\ncache is the last-known-good; failures with nothing cached propagate as\nConfigVersionManifestError). buildRuntimeConfigEffect derives entry-level\nfields (entryUrl, hashed browser-manifest entry, entry SRI, ssrEntryUrl,\nssrIntegrity) onto host/ui/api/auth/plugins + ui slots in production/\nstaging; dev untouched; RuntimeConfig.auth keeps its ui field (was silently\nschema-stripped). Consumers prefer the derived hashed URLs with fixed-name\nfallbacks: uiSources webEntry + payload manifestUrl (hydrate registration),\nplugins.ts SSR container loads, ssrEntryUrlOf (no cache-buster on hashed\nURLs), client-config ui.entryUrl, html.ts core+plugin entry scripts, mf.ts\ntype inference.\n\n* feat(host): RuntimeSnapshot service + aborted-train regression lock (atomic-deploys 05-06)\n\nTicket 05 - the train-level tracer: the REAL publishToFastKv runs against a\nlocal mock storage origin (the storage route contract: server-computed SRI,\nbatched base64/JSON, GET serving, the /.well-known/mcp.json probe) with two\nfailure injections - batch-500s and mid-request socket kills (the\n2026-09-30 transport failure). Proven: v1 pins its manifest pointer; an\naborted v2 train leaves v1''s pointer, pinned bytes (byte-identical) and SRI\nfully live; a completed v2 train flips the pointer while v1''s hashed entry +\nmanifest bytes remain exactly servable. Upload failures now abort the train\nas a structured {status:\"error\"} instead of propagating raw.\n\nTicket 06 - the host RuntimeSnapshot service: an atomic Ref over the UI/SSR\nbase state ({fingerprint, config, composeState}) booting from ConfigService;\nget/swap/modify (a throwing modify leaves the state untouched); a\nconcurrency test forks 200 reads across a swap and asserts every\nobservation is one complete state. The SSR fallback and static-asset request\npaths resolve per-request against the snapshot''s current base config via the\nnew getBaseConfig seam; boot-frozen consumers (security CSP origins, API oRPC\nregistration, auth services) are documented as such per MAP decision 3.\n\nReview findings fixed: modify reshaped to a real read-modify-write (f\nreturns [A, next state] - ticket 07''s swap transaction builds on it), the\nmisleading last-good fallback branch removed (the content-addressed cache is\nthe last-known-good), the tautological fingerprint assertion removed, the\nservice alias dropped (.layer like the neighbors).\n\n* feat(host): SnapshotCoordinator swap transaction + SnapshotWatch fiber (atomic-deploys 07-08)\n\nTicket 07 - the adopt transaction: derive the published FastKV pointer\n(buildRuntimeConfig, version manifests fetched + SRI-verified), fingerprint\nno-op when unchanged, pre-warm compose into a FRESH UiComposeCacheState\n(validates compose + digest parity before anything live moves), SRI-verify\nthe pinned entry + SSR entry (hashed URLs), then one atomic snapshot.swap.\nEvery step wraps its cause into SnapshotAdoptError via Effect.catch\ncombinators - a failure leaves the live snapshot untouched. Concurrent\nadopts serialize through a semaphore permit. Exposed as the\nSnapshotCoordinator service.\n\nTicket 08 - the watch fiber replacing the setInterval integrity monitor:\npointer poll (pointerFingerprint over per-slot manifest/integrity pairs -\nno manifest fetch) adopts on change; the unchanged-pointer path SRI-verifies\nthe live slots each tick (own pins for manifest slots; extends-ref slots\nre-read the parent config from FastKV and verify against the parent''s\nlatest integrity - upstream republish noticed without a restart) and alerts\non serving-side corruption with the greppable INTEGRITY FAILURE string.\nBOS_SNAPSHOT_WATCH_INTERVAL_MS (default 30s), production-only, scope-owned\nfiber. integrity-monitor.ts deleted (fully covered).\n\nEffect v4 lessons applied throughout: yield* failures short-circuit\ngenerators (combinator-based catching only); service-instance types are\nX[\"Service\"] (the class type carries the brand, not the members); Context.Service shapes cannot carry generic methods.\n\n* feat(host,ui): integrity-mismatch cache fallback + soft refresh (atomic-deploys 09-10)\n\nTicket 09 - the MF integrity fetch hook (the seam where pinned URLs are\nfetched + verified) treats an SRI mismatch like an origin failure: the\nlast-known-good bytes from the bundle cache (which satisfied the same pin\nwhen cached) serve with x-bundle-cache: stale, and the cache write-through\nbecame pin-checked - corrupted origin bytes never poison it. The host\nprocess now installs the outbound bundle-fetch tier (own-namespace staged\nreads + stale-if-error) via installBundleFetchFromEnv; the\neverything-dev/bundle-fs-resolve export landed.\n\nTicket 10 - soft refresh: the deployment fingerprint rides RuntimeConfig ->\nclient config -> window.__RUNTIME_CONFIG__ (stamped at boot and at every\ncoordinator swap); GET /.well-known/version reads the SNAPSHOT (flips exactly\nat swap, cache-control max-age=30); the startVersionWatch poller\n(everything-dev/ui/version-check - 60s while visible, reports once) and the\nVersionRefreshBanner (mounted in ui''s __root, ClientOnly) offer a reload for\nsigned-in sessions on a fingerprint mismatch - dismiss persists via\nsessionStorage; the reload is always safe because old bytes are retained.\n\n* feat(cli): bos rollback — republish an earlier config pointer (atomic-deploys 11)\n\nfetchConfigHistory reads the FastData exact-key publish history for the\nregistry config key (newest-first, limit clamped to the API''s 200 cap).\nBefore republishing, the safety gate re-fetches every pinned slot''s version\nmanifest from the origin and compares SRI: a 404 or mismatch refuses with a\nper-slot report, and --force cannot override a failed verification — it only\nadmits pre-Phase-A snapshots with no verifiable pins (their bytes were\noverwritten in place). The target goes through the normal publish path\n(build: false — bytes exist, only the pointer moves) stamped with a\nrolledBackFrom annotation (additive config field, ordered last) so the dedup\nguard treats the rollback as distinct state; an identical-to-live target\nshort-circuits before any transaction. CLI: interactive clack select over the\nlisting (timestamp, block height, per-slot pin summary) or --previous /\n--version <block-height|iso-prefix> for scripts.\n\n* feat(host,ui,cli): version observability everywhere (atomic-deploys 12)\n\nThe version endpoint now carries the full deploy state: fingerprint, the\nadopted pointer''s per-slot manifest pins (the snapshot state gained the\npointer), and the watch fiber''s last-tick outcome. pointerFingerprint +\nslotPins moved to everything-dev/fingerprint so the CLI and the host compute\nthe same identity for the same pointer. Every publish writes the per-deploy\nmanifest key (previously wallet-only), prints the fingerprint + pins, and\nreturns them on the result; bos deploy --status lists that audit trail\nnewest-first via FastData history-by-prefix. bos status computes the\ndeployed-vs-served delta - the published pointer''s fingerprint vs what the\nhost''s version endpoint serves - the split-brain detector that would have\ncaught the 2026-09-30 incident in seconds. The admin dashboard gains a\nversion card (admin-version-card), and /llms.txt + /skill.md document the\nversion surface so agents self-serve.\n\n* fix(host,ui): local plugin ui slots must not carry a manifestUrl in the compose payload\n\nThe dev:csr regression suite failed 8/9 auth tests: /login fell through to\nthe dynamic $accountId route because the auth plugin''s login route never\nmounted. The CI trace pinned it: the compose payload carried the auth\nremote''s manifestUrl as the RELATIVE \"/mf-manifest.json\" (a local slot''s\nentry is the client convention), so manifest-driven registration fetched\nthe page origin''s mf-manifest.json - the HOST''s container - and the\nrouteConfig load fell through to the core web container, which has no\n./routeConfig expose: \"Module ./routeConfig does not exist in container\" →\ncore-only fallback. Only dev:csr broke because dev slots are the only ones\nwhose server-side entry is relative; production and start modes carry\nabsolute entries.\n\nFix: clientPayloadOf gates the plugin loop''s browserManifestUrl exactly like\nthe core source already did - local slots omit manifestUrl, so hydrate\nderives the manifest URL from the absolute webEntry (the pre-ticket-08\nbehavior). Defense in depth: hydrate only trusts manifestUrl when it parses\nas an absolute http(s) URL. Regression test: a dev-shaped local plugin ui\n(url set, entry \"/mf-manifest.json\") produces a remote with no manifestUrl;\nthe remote-slot test (absolute entry) keeps it.\n\nAlso: the hashed MF entry filenames in the ui rsbuild config are now\nbuild-only (isBuildInvocation: DEPLOY=true or non-development NODE_ENV) -\ndev servers serve in-memory and every dev consumer appends the legacy fixed\nentry name, so interactive rsbuild dev would otherwise serve the entry at a\nhashed URL nothing resolves. Regression tests cover the filename matrix and\nthat the dist-aliasing plugin only attaches on builds.\n\n* feat(host,ui,cli): explicit slot pins — pin: {manifest, integrity} + full legacy retirement\n\n- config slots carry pin: {manifest, integrity}; top-level integrity is\n  always a direct entry SRI; the flat `manifest` key is retired and scrubbed\n  by deploy write-backs; extends merges the pin atomically\n- outside development every remote slot must pin a version manifest —\n  unpinned remote slots fail resolution loudly; fixed-name entry fallbacks\n  are development-only at every consumer (resolveEntryUrlForEnv)\n- bos plugin publish joins the deploy train (preflight → build → upload →\n  pin → FastKV publish + read-back); image-native applyPluginPublishUrl\n  deleted\n- tenant UI overrides are pin-aware: editor draft/preflight/autofill carry\n  the pin; the host verifies override entries at pin-derived hashed URLs\n- builds stop emitting fixed-name entry aliases (HashEntryAliasPlugin →\n  BuildReportPlugin); deploy aborts on dists that cannot pin; LEGACY_*\n  entry names renamed to the dev-contract names they are\n- snapshot watch adopts pin fingerprints and verifies extends-ref slots\n  against the parent''s resolved entryIntegrity (was manifest-SRI vs entry\n  bytes); coordinator derives via buildRuntimeConfigEffect (no cast)\n- dormant local-prod config helper retired (ADR 0009 amendment); ADR 0020\n  amended; review-comment fixes (comments, optional chains, Promise.all,\n  yield-less gen)\n\n* lint\n\n* fix(every-plugin,host): DEPLOY-only entry gate — dev builds emit fixed remoteEntry.js again\n\n- isBuildInvocation → isDeployInvocation, gated on DEPLOY=true only\n  (NODE_ENV is unusable: vitest runs as test, rspack/rsbuild CLIs\n  default production even for local dev watches)\n- deploy train now flips the signal itself: buildWorkspaceTargets sets\n  DEPLOY=true when deploy:true (matches the documented contract)\n- rspack MF entry filename derived from uiEntryFilename instead of an\n  unconditional hashed literal; EmitPluginManifest fallback + hashed\n  entry discovery use the standard module\n- every remoteEntry.js literal (every-plugin dev serve, runtime\n  normalizers, host plugins.ts/html.ts) imports DEV_ENTRY_FILENAME\n- regression container-build inlines the retired\n  prepareLocalProductionConfig rewrite (ADR 0009 legacy retirement)\n  so the synced script stays self-contained\n\n* fix(every-plugin): dev-stack signal gate — BOS_DEV_SERVER stamps dev bundlers\n\nisBuildInvocation now keys on an explicit BOS_DEV_SERVER=1 stamp instead\nof NODE_ENV/DEPLOY. Dev servers mark their own bundler children (the dev\nserve, the every-plugin dev command, the orchestrator''s no-watch\ndev:built spawn), so NODE_ENV can never misclassify them again — vitest\nruns as test, the rspack/rsbuild CLIs default production even for dev\nwatches. Every non-dev invocation (local builds, host-test production\nbuilds, regression container builds, deploys) emits content-hashed\nentries + build reports, restoring the retired-fixed-names contract the\nhost test helpers and the pin path are built on. Also reverts the\ntrain''s DEPLOY=true env (not needed for naming) and corrects the stale\nresolution-conditions comment.\n\n* fix(host,everything-dev): regression start fixture pins its slots\n\nADR 0009 amendment: version-manifest pins are the only production slot\nshape. The container fixture now pins every slot it serves: the host\nrsbuild config adopts the hashed-entry + build-report contract (making\napp.host pinnable by the deploy train too, which previously aborted at\nthe host leg), and container-build composes per-slot version manifests\nfrom build reports + locally-computed SRI (the staged static servers are\nthe storage boundary here) and stamps pin {manifest, integrity} into the\nvariant configs. Slot pins resolve against the slot''s remote base\n(remoteUrl), not the host''s listening URL — a pinned host slot could\nnever resolve against its own origin. The version manifests'' ssr.entry\ncarries its ssr/ path segment so the derived ssrEntryUrl points at the\nreal bytes.\n\n* lint\n\n* fix(everything-dev): run() drops captured stdout — deploy image leg false git-SHA failure\n\n* fix\n\n* fix\n\n* test(regression): compose specs accept hashed remoteEntry entries","tree":{"sha":"567658edf42e6fad6e2e6b831463613fff4eda29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/trees/567658edf42e6fad6e2e6b831463613fff4eda29"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/commits/613206ea39c31ace52b75eb62d224afa49e79575","verification":{"payload":"tree 567658edf42e6fad6e2e6b831463613fff4eda29\nparent ddbbb792d0c2b1984b2700a978b1397551f89544\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1790905499 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790905499 -0500\n\nfeat(cli): consolidate bos deploy — one command, clean CI train (#296)\n\n* feat(cli): consolidate bos deploy into one command with preflight, image, and Railway legs\n\nbos deploy is now the full train (NEARBuilders/citynode.app#295): preflight\n(config, auth guards, signing, storage/CDN credentials, registry reachability\n— all before any build, fixing the ordering flaw where a missing\nBOS_STORAGE_API_KEY failed only after the build train), the staleness-checked\nbuild train, bundle upload to the R2-backed storage, FastKV publish with\nread-back confirmation, a runtime-image leg pushed to GHCR by short-SHA and\nlatest tags (ci.image -> BOS_IMAGE -> repository derivation), and a pull-only\nRailway deploy pinned to the pushed digest via a generated thin Dockerfile.\n\nbos publish becomes config-only; --deploy/--packages and bos build --deploy\nare removed. The railway redeploy branch (which re-shipped the old image) is\ndeleted. Deploy responses carry image/service; the storage upload response\ndiscloses the resolved backend (s3/memory) and bos deploy hard-fails on\nin-memory storage instead of silently losing bytes on restart.\n\nWorkflows shrink to checkout + bun run bos deploy + verification; docker.yml\nis absorbed. Child templates and scaffolded scripts ship the same shape.\nFixes stale edk_ key-prefix docs; adds the bos login --key CI bootstrap doc.\n\n* refactor(cli): apply code-review fixes to the deploy consolidation\n\n- pass process.env into resolveImageRef so BOS_IMAGE actually takes effect\n  outside unit tests\n- config-only publish test: assert the build train is never invoked\n- API storage backend-disclosure unit test (s3/memory) on StorageLive\n- trim JSDoc blocks to single-line comments per the no-comments standard\n- record spike outcome and review decisions in the sprint tickets\n  (RAILWAY_DOCKERFILE_PATH is Railway''s documented mechanism; prepare step\n  deliberately omitted from deploy workflows — staging empirically builds\n  prerequisites without it, and the effect patch only matters for\n  lint/typecheck)\n\n* feat(cli): authored cdn.origin guard — deploys never promote dev-resolved host URLs\n\nDeploy origins resolve env -> bosConfig.cdn.origin (extends-inherited) -> hard\nerror; the runtimeConfig.host.url derivation that published localhost:3000\nbundle URLs is gone. A session pinned to a local site is a hard error for\nuploads, env-pinned local origins warn, and the storage origin is probed\n(/.well-known/mcp.json) in preflight before the build train. Config-only\npublishes require no origins. ADR 0020 amendment + changeset.\n\n* feat(build): content-hashed deploy artifacts + version-manifest pointers (atomic-deploys 01-02)\n\nTicket 01 - hashed artifacts: entrypoints build as\nremoteEntry.[contenthash].js / remoteEntry.server.[contenthash].js (rsbuild\nweb+node envs, every-plugin rspack builds) with byte-identical legacy\nfixed-name aliases for the rollout window, hashed copies of mf-manifest.json\nand style.css, and a per-dist build-report.json for the deploy leg. Bundle\ncache classification is canonicalized in every-plugin/build/artifact-names:\ncontent-hashed names are immutable regardless of base name; fixed names must\nrevalidate (bundle-fs-resolve + api storage policy now share it). Verified\nagainst real ui (web+ssr) and api builds.\n\nTicket 02 - version manifests: new every-plugin/version-manifest export with\nthe immutable WorkspaceVersionManifest document and composeVersionManifest\n(version id = content-derived, key-order stable, builtAt excluded so\nunchanged bytes keep one id). Config slots gain a manifest pointer (versioned\nmanifest filename; integrity pins the manifest when set) through\nBosConfigSchema, the descriptor schemas, and both roundtrip field maps.\n\nDeploys are not yet additive end-to-end: the deploy leg (ticket 03) and\nderived resolution (ticket 04) consume the report + pointer; until then the\nlegacy aliases keep every existing consumer working. Spec: .scratch/\natomic-deploys/ (MAP + tickets).\n\n* test(config)+docs(adr): manifest pointer review follow-ups (atomic-deploys 01-02)\n\nExtends-merge semantics pinned by test: app slots inherit the parent''s\nmanifest field-wise (child override wins); child plugin entries replace\nparent entries wholesale (existing merge behavior — a child publishes its\nown manifests for every slot it ships). ADR 0020 amendment records the\nhashed-artifact + version-manifest + cache-classification decisions the\nphase-A commit made.\n\n* feat(build): version-manifest deploy leg + derived entry resolution (atomic-deploys 03-04)\n\nTicket 03 - deploy leg: the upload response''s server-computed SRI map plus\nthe ticket-01 build reports compose an immutable WorkspaceVersionManifest,\nuploaded additively at versions/<version>.json; deploy entries pin the slot\nby manifest pointer (manifest field; integrity becomes the manifest SRI when\npinned; legacy production/ssr fields still written during rollout).\nTransport hardening: status-0 retries ride fresh connections (connection:\nclose - the pooled keepalive socket race), 5 attempts with backoff+jitter;\nretryable statuses capped at 3; uploadBundle takes an injectable fetchImpl.\n\nTicket 04 - derived resolution: resolveSlotVersion fetches + SRI-verifies\nthe version manifest behind a content-addressed per-pin process cache (the\ncache is the last-known-good; failures with nothing cached propagate as\nConfigVersionManifestError). buildRuntimeConfigEffect derives entry-level\nfields (entryUrl, hashed browser-manifest entry, entry SRI, ssrEntryUrl,\nssrIntegrity) onto host/ui/api/auth/plugins + ui slots in production/\nstaging; dev untouched; RuntimeConfig.auth keeps its ui field (was silently\nschema-stripped). Consumers prefer the derived hashed URLs with fixed-name\nfallbacks: uiSources webEntry + payload manifestUrl (hydrate registration),\nplugins.ts SSR container loads, ssrEntryUrlOf (no cache-buster on hashed\nURLs), client-config ui.entryUrl, html.ts core+plugin entry scripts, mf.ts\ntype inference.\n\n* feat(host): RuntimeSnapshot service + aborted-train regression lock (atomic-deploys 05-06)\n\nTicket 05 - the train-level tracer: the REAL publishToFastKv runs against a\nlocal mock storage origin (the storage route contract: server-computed SRI,\nbatched base64/JSON, GET serving, the /.well-known/mcp.json probe) with two\nfailure injections - batch-500s and mid-request socket kills (the\n2026-09-30 transport failure). Proven: v1 pins its manifest pointer; an\naborted v2 train leaves v1''s pointer, pinned bytes (byte-identical) and SRI\nfully live; a completed v2 train flips the pointer while v1''s hashed entry +\nmanifest bytes remain exactly servable. Upload failures now abort the train\nas a structured {status:\"error\"} instead of propagating raw.\n\nTicket 06 - the host RuntimeSnapshot service: an atomic Ref over the UI/SSR\nbase state ({fingerprint, config, composeState}) booting from ConfigService;\nget/swap/modify (a throwing modify leaves the state untouched); a\nconcurrency test forks 200 reads across a swap and asserts every\nobservation is one complete state. The SSR fallback and static-asset request\npaths resolve per-request against the snapshot''s current base config via the\nnew getBaseConfig seam; boot-frozen consumers (security CSP origins, API oRPC\nregistration, auth services) are documented as such per MAP decision 3.\n\nReview findings fixed: modify reshaped to a real read-modify-write (f\nreturns [A, next state] - ticket 07''s swap transaction builds on it), the\nmisleading last-good fallback branch removed (the content-addressed cache is\nthe last-known-good), the tautological fingerprint assertion removed, the\nservice alias dropped (.layer like the neighbors).\n\n* feat(host): SnapshotCoordinator swap transaction + SnapshotWatch fiber (atomic-deploys 07-08)\n\nTicket 07 - the adopt transaction: derive the published FastKV pointer\n(buildRuntimeConfig, version manifests fetched + SRI-verified), fingerprint\nno-op when unchanged, pre-warm compose into a FRESH UiComposeCacheState\n(validates compose + digest parity before anything live moves), SRI-verify\nthe pinned entry + SSR entry (hashed URLs), then one atomic snapshot.swap.\nEvery step wraps its cause into SnapshotAdoptError via Effect.catch\ncombinators - a failure leaves the live snapshot untouched. Concurrent\nadopts serialize through a semaphore permit. Exposed as the\nSnapshotCoordinator service.\n\nTicket 08 - the watch fiber replacing the setInterval integrity monitor:\npointer poll (pointerFingerprint over per-slot manifest/integrity pairs -\nno manifest fetch) adopts on change; the unchanged-pointer path SRI-verifies\nthe live slots each tick (own pins for manifest slots; extends-ref slots\nre-read the parent config from FastKV and verify against the parent''s\nlatest integrity - upstream republish noticed without a restart) and alerts\non serving-side corruption with the greppable INTEGRITY FAILURE string.\nBOS_SNAPSHOT_WATCH_INTERVAL_MS (default 30s), production-only, scope-owned\nfiber. integrity-monitor.ts deleted (fully covered).\n\nEffect v4 lessons applied throughout: yield* failures short-circuit\ngenerators (combinator-based catching only); service-instance types are\nX[\"Service\"] (the class type carries the brand, not the members); Context.Service shapes cannot carry generic methods.\n\n* feat(host,ui): integrity-mismatch cache fallback + soft refresh (atomic-deploys 09-10)\n\nTicket 09 - the MF integrity fetch hook (the seam where pinned URLs are\nfetched + verified) treats an SRI mismatch like an origin failure: the\nlast-known-good bytes from the bundle cache (which satisfied the same pin\nwhen cached) serve with x-bundle-cache: stale, and the cache write-through\nbecame pin-checked - corrupted origin bytes never poison it. The host\nprocess now installs the outbound bundle-fetch tier (own-namespace staged\nreads + stale-if-error) via installBundleFetchFromEnv; the\neverything-dev/bundle-fs-resolve export landed.\n\nTicket 10 - soft refresh: the deployment fingerprint rides RuntimeConfig ->\nclient config -> window.__RUNTIME_CONFIG__ (stamped at boot and at every\ncoordinator swap); GET /.well-known/version reads the SNAPSHOT (flips exactly\nat swap, cache-control max-age=30); the startVersionWatch poller\n(everything-dev/ui/version-check - 60s while visible, reports once) and the\nVersionRefreshBanner (mounted in ui''s __root, ClientOnly) offer a reload for\nsigned-in sessions on a fingerprint mismatch - dismiss persists via\nsessionStorage; the reload is always safe because old bytes are retained.\n\n* feat(cli): bos rollback — republish an earlier config pointer (atomic-deploys 11)\n\nfetchConfigHistory reads the FastData exact-key publish history for the\nregistry config key (newest-first, limit clamped to the API''s 200 cap).\nBefore republishing, the safety gate re-fetches every pinned slot''s version\nmanifest from the origin and compares SRI: a 404 or mismatch refuses with a\nper-slot report, and --force cannot override a failed verification — it only\nadmits pre-Phase-A snapshots with no verifiable pins (their bytes were\noverwritten in place). The target goes through the normal publish path\n(build: false — bytes exist, only the pointer moves) stamped with a\nrolledBackFrom annotation (additive config field, ordered last) so the dedup\nguard treats the rollback as distinct state; an identical-to-live target\nshort-circuits before any transaction. CLI: interactive clack select over the\nlisting (timestamp, block height, per-slot pin summary) or --previous /\n--version <block-height|iso-prefix> for scripts.\n\n* feat(host,ui,cli): version observability everywhere (atomic-deploys 12)\n\nThe version endpoint now carries the full deploy state: fingerprint, the\nadopted pointer''s per-slot manifest pins (the snapshot state gained the\npointer), and the watch fiber''s last-tick outcome. pointerFingerprint +\nslotPins moved to everything-dev/fingerprint so the CLI and the host compute\nthe same identity for the same pointer. Every publish writes the per-deploy\nmanifest key (previously wallet-only), prints the fingerprint + pins, and\nreturns them on the result; bos deploy --status lists that audit trail\nnewest-first via FastData history-by-prefix. bos status computes the\ndeployed-vs-served delta - the published pointer''s fingerprint vs what the\nhost''s version endpoint serves - the split-brain detector that would have\ncaught the 2026-09-30 incident in seconds. The admin dashboard gains a\nversion card (admin-version-card), and /llms.txt + /skill.md document the\nversion surface so agents self-serve.\n\n* fix(host,ui): local plugin ui slots must not carry a manifestUrl in the compose payload\n\nThe dev:csr regression suite failed 8/9 auth tests: /login fell through to\nthe dynamic $accountId route because the auth plugin''s login route never\nmounted. The CI trace pinned it: the compose payload carried the auth\nremote''s manifestUrl as the RELATIVE \"/mf-manifest.json\" (a local slot''s\nentry is the client convention), so manifest-driven registration fetched\nthe page origin''s mf-manifest.json - the HOST''s container - and the\nrouteConfig load fell through to the core web container, which has no\n./routeConfig expose: \"Module ./routeConfig does not exist in container\" →\ncore-only fallback. Only dev:csr broke because dev slots are the only ones\nwhose server-side entry is relative; production and start modes carry\nabsolute entries.\n\nFix: clientPayloadOf gates the plugin loop''s browserManifestUrl exactly like\nthe core source already did - local slots omit manifestUrl, so hydrate\nderives the manifest URL from the absolute webEntry (the pre-ticket-08\nbehavior). Defense in depth: hydrate only trusts manifestUrl when it parses\nas an absolute http(s) URL. Regression test: a dev-shaped local plugin ui\n(url set, entry \"/mf-manifest.json\") produces a remote with no manifestUrl;\nthe remote-slot test (absolute entry) keeps it.\n\nAlso: the hashed MF entry filenames in the ui rsbuild config are now\nbuild-only (isBuildInvocation: DEPLOY=true or non-development NODE_ENV) -\ndev servers serve in-memory and every dev consumer appends the legacy fixed\nentry name, so interactive rsbuild dev would otherwise serve the entry at a\nhashed URL nothing resolves. Regression tests cover the filename matrix and\nthat the dist-aliasing plugin only attaches on builds.\n\n* feat(host,ui,cli): explicit slot pins — pin: {manifest, integrity} + full legacy retirement\n\n- config slots carry pin: {manifest, integrity}; top-level integrity is\n  always a direct entry SRI; the flat `manifest` key is retired and scrubbed\n  by deploy write-backs; extends merges the pin atomically\n- outside development every remote slot must pin a version manifest —\n  unpinned remote slots fail resolution loudly; fixed-name entry fallbacks\n  are development-only at every consumer (resolveEntryUrlForEnv)\n- bos plugin publish joins the deploy train (preflight → build → upload →\n  pin → FastKV publish + read-back); image-native applyPluginPublishUrl\n  deleted\n- tenant UI overrides are pin-aware: editor draft/preflight/autofill carry\n  the pin; the host verifies override entries at pin-derived hashed URLs\n- builds stop emitting fixed-name entry aliases (HashEntryAliasPlugin →\n  BuildReportPlugin); deploy aborts on dists that cannot pin; LEGACY_*\n  entry names renamed to the dev-contract names they are\n- snapshot watch adopts pin fingerprints and verifies extends-ref slots\n  against the parent''s resolved entryIntegrity (was manifest-SRI vs entry\n  bytes); coordinator derives via buildRuntimeConfigEffect (no cast)\n- dormant local-prod config helper retired (ADR 0009 amendment); ADR 0020\n  amended; review-comment fixes (comments, optional chains, Promise.all,\n  yield-less gen)\n\n* lint\n\n* fix(every-plugin,host): DEPLOY-only entry gate — dev builds emit fixed remoteEntry.js again\n\n- isBuildInvocation → isDeployInvocation, gated on DEPLOY=true only\n  (NODE_ENV is unusable: vitest runs as test, rspack/rsbuild CLIs\n  default production even for local dev watches)\n- deploy train now flips the signal itself: buildWorkspaceTargets sets\n  DEPLOY=true when deploy:true (matches the documented contract)\n- rspack MF entry filename derived from uiEntryFilename instead of an\n  unconditional hashed literal; EmitPluginManifest fallback + hashed\n  entry discovery use the standard module\n- every remoteEntry.js literal (every-plugin dev serve, runtime\n  normalizers, host plugins.ts/html.ts) imports DEV_ENTRY_FILENAME\n- regression container-build inlines the retired\n  prepareLocalProductionConfig rewrite (ADR 0009 legacy retirement)\n  so the synced script stays self-contained\n\n* fix(every-plugin): dev-stack signal gate — BOS_DEV_SERVER stamps dev bundlers\n\nisBuildInvocation now keys on an explicit BOS_DEV_SERVER=1 stamp instead\nof NODE_ENV/DEPLOY. Dev servers mark their own bundler children (the dev\nserve, the every-plugin dev command, the orchestrator''s no-watch\ndev:built spawn), so NODE_ENV can never misclassify them again — vitest\nruns as test, the rspack/rsbuild CLIs default production even for dev\nwatches. Every non-dev invocation (local builds, host-test production\nbuilds, regression container builds, deploys) emits content-hashed\nentries + build reports, restoring the retired-fixed-names contract the\nhost test helpers and the pin path are built on. Also reverts the\ntrain''s DEPLOY=true env (not needed for naming) and corrects the stale\nresolution-conditions comment.\n\n* fix(host,everything-dev): regression start fixture pins its slots\n\nADR 0009 amendment: version-manifest pins are the only production slot\nshape. The container fixture now pins every slot it serves: the host\nrsbuild config adopts the hashed-entry + build-report contract (making\napp.host pinnable by the deploy train too, which previously aborted at\nthe host leg), and container-build composes per-slot version manifests\nfrom build reports + locally-computed SRI (the staged static servers are\nthe storage boundary here) and stamps pin {manifest, integrity} into the\nvariant configs. Slot pins resolve against the slot''s remote base\n(remoteUrl), not the host''s listening URL — a pinned host slot could\nnever resolve against its own origin. The version manifests'' ssr.entry\ncarries its ssr/ path segment so the derived ssrEntryUrl points at the\nreal bytes.\n\n* lint\n\n* fix(everything-dev): run() drops captured stdout — deploy image leg false git-SHA failure\n\n* fix\n\n* fix\n\n* test(regression): compose specs accept hashed remoteEntry entries","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvwybCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsVgQAA0ZlA/J8Ca7ZZYYSc1V2apK\nmkgNDOGRhEuzHPEL3FKctGjupjvpx7eIP2HaRA5FHLBF/DuhlIlob/7ZTp2Zsozh\nAsERPMtiPDo5ZWWjwCZ6mZKPk1v8nAwr/zhR9pnQk/pd3yu9RwzSiIxdwXn80NjO\np8j2q3wRFLdUSlNAreL3sfcqOqwDBgSEyvPAYvSUlxPxPECZeR78kWYwCxpuf7ui\naC4Qc5Sjh7TFs7N+csmmuKTteigEmdCX1etnnISTZIppFTRQ7O3LI8/soupqxBYA\nCjQLergPjq78mbIdp4yJbhsvV+HrRRIBp9/FPSocMcFF8XwW9j7ur7ee8sVhuTJp\nQBoeP1TsEa3jYCjcKMN+ZDgHZ3LwOxfEeS+x60tLTPWBSfvyM9J9nfvcW6mD9fXZ\nmzitcEBzv+BiI6XkRNmxWIM6yqOg838AplhWVGOQvr5zqKIudqMKXq1PFq6RO3Sf\nkwnjEXImv4hjaHxSjuFr7T/l1qStKqZBZ+E1O2fGDNPAoFjuBSxfrYLCZgVvUVyM\ndPSJpBmR8wsYeiZ4QkLmcTMLRQZM8bW6H9b3I6KqmCSsd9sR0fEgv72n2b1nHHLA\nio/9blRK6/lFPOMMbSKuRG5Td6VD2EvaOONgh5pgUS6fWzUzc9MKDxnNiKLGYo2V\nwuzL/UzLDM+gPB2w0Cfw\n=Oq7H\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T01:45:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.g