ode.app/commits/056031fdc6aa51c26dd122573c8f8cf09a755559"}],"sha":"274541b7194579c7f659587c2e2d956c8e047c19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/274541b7194579c7f659587c2e2d956c8e047c19"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46527178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/itexpert120","id":46527178,"login":"itexpert120","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/056031fdc6aa51c26dd122573c8f8cf09a755559/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T15:46:11Z","email":"itexpert120@outlook.com","name":"Zeeshan Ahmad"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T15:46:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: propose a new community homepage to the DAO (#300)\n\n* feat(ui): stage tenant config proposals with the session wallet (#273)\n\nPromote the session-proposal staging primitives into the shared\nsputnik-proposals lib and add proposeTenantConfigAsMember to the\ntenant-deploy lib.\n\nCloses #273\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(ui): extract shared tenant-config proposal pieces from the Community tab (#274)\n\nPull the org tenant config and pending-proposal hooks, the custom UI\nbundle field group, ConfigField and the integrity preflight out of the\nCommunity tab, which now consumes them unchanged.\n\nCloses #274\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(ui): Homepage tab to propose a new homepage to the DAO (#275)\n\nOrg members propose a new title/description and custom UI bundle to\nthe org''s sputnik DAO with their own session wallet and see live vote\nprogress; platform-owned communities publish directly.\n\nCloses #275\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(ui): propose-homepage deep link on the node page for owning org members (#276)\n\nCloses #276\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): sync tenant name and require mainnet on the Homepage tab\n\nPlatform-owned publishes now update the tenant name like the Community\ntab, and DAO proposals are blocked until the wallet is on mainnet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(near-auth): accept NEP-413 signatures that omit the callback URL\n\nWallets such as Intear sign the NEP-413 payload without the optional\ncallbackUrl, so verifying with it rejected every sign-in as an invalid\nsignature. Verify with the callback URL first, then without it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): refill the Homepage tab when the published config arrives late\n\nA failed first registry read prefilled an empty draft that never\nrefreshed, so proposing would have wiped the community''s repository\nand UI bundles. Keep syncing the draft from the published config until\nthe member edits it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): require an active organization on the Homepage tab\n\nThe tenant API scopes lookups to the session''s active organization, so\nthe node-page deep link could land on an inactive org whose bindings\n403, and proposing then failed with a missing-binding error. Block with\na clear reason until the org is made active, and refetch tenant queries\nwhen the active organization changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e7a23a2e886a800e96b5cb10fd26495721645874","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/trees/e7a23a2e886a800e96b5cb10fd26495721645874"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/commits/056031fdc6aa51c26dd122573c8f8cf09a755559","verification":{"payload":"tree e7a23a2e886a800e96b5cb10fd26495721645874\nparent cf2ab4d138ed6acedac43b87b3abe3d6b8bdeabb\nauthor Zeeshan Ahmad <itexpert120@outlook.com> 1790869571 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790869571 -0500\n\nfeat: propose a new community homepage to the DAO (#300)\n\n* feat(ui): stage tenant config proposals with the session wallet (#273)\n\nPromote the session-proposal staging primitives into the shared\nsputnik-proposals lib and add proposeTenantConfigAsMember to the\ntenant-deploy lib.\n\nCloses #273\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(ui): extract shared tenant-config proposal pieces from the Community tab (#274)\n\nPull the org tenant config and pending-proposal hooks, the custom UI\nbundle field group, ConfigField and the integrity preflight out of the\nCommunity tab, which now consumes them unchanged.\n\nCloses #274\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(ui): Homepage tab to propose a new homepage to the DAO (#275)\n\nOrg members propose a new title/description and custom UI bundle to\nthe org''s sputnik DAO with their own session wallet and see live vote\nprogress; platform-owned communities publish directly.\n\nCloses #275\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(ui): propose-homepage deep link on the node page for owning org members (#276)\n\nCloses #276\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): sync tenant name and require mainnet on the Homepage tab\n\nPlatform-owned publishes now update the tenant name like the Community\ntab, and DAO proposals are blocked until the wallet is on mainnet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(near-auth): accept NEP-413 signatures that omit the callback URL\n\nWallets such as Intear sign the NEP-413 payload without the optional\ncallbackUrl, so verifying with it rejected every sign-in as an invalid\nsignature. Verify with the callback URL first, then without it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): refill the Homepage tab when the published config arrives late\n\nA failed first registry read prefilled an empty draft that never\nrefreshed, so proposing would have wiped the community''s repository\nand UI bundles. Keep syncing the draft from the published config until\nthe member edits it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ui): require an active organization on the Homepage tab\n\nThe tenant API scopes lookups to the session''s active organization, so\nthe node-page deep link could land on an inactive org whose bindings\n403, and proposing then failed with a missing-binding error. Block with\na clear reason until the org is made active, and refetch tenant queries\nwhen the active organization changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvoBDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAa04QAEArvRHyqG1G+q3sliK6YzCN\nCOEL73qat+K1xCgnnh6cABuD2N+jAij/XMKM6PdsrJFhaCtEMiITX+A7/DmfZW10\n7UwzeEQ9gyomBPjBQn7RDdPL8UNYdbYHCx44dFp9qUnnSxSDtsA52nKyGI9/Fhjb\nN7XTwLQa3UZXKNIE6rYcs/u+VYssqv5z3vHxnGHCHOkYNPJfujrjyHRq1aFKsV39\nCctp/5FkFo6l+RcixdOkI9HMa1awb+ZAvzEF1hEKtZ6kkzZLS7w+MEBsrnh1nqlX\nCkIEfdCGeKyenMYw8jPFPOotOIWzGZ4VuZ3