ttps://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/fd8e4b8247c932928e08e6d9175c0d8b9d6cb01a"}],"sha":"ce9999535b29c0ede63c55d3509650726f890ea5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/ce9999535b29c0ede63c55d3509650726f890ea5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/fd8e4b8247c932928e08e6d9175c0d8b9d6cb01a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:47:12Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:47:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(db,plugins): honor sslmode; structured plugin-boot failure pipeline (#253)\n\n* fix(db,plugins): honor sslmode; structured plugin-boot failure pipeline\n\nRoot cause of the Sep 25 production outage: PR #163''s security batch\nflipped the shared DB driver''s TLS verification to on-by-default for\nevery non-local URL, and managed providers'' sslmode=require URLs carry\ncertificates no client CA bundle can verify — the auth plugin''s pool\n(followed by the api''s) failed at connect time. The pre-existing\nboot pipeline then retried silently for 120s per plugin, pushing the\nserver''s port-bind past the container entrypoint''s 180s health gate ->\nexit(1) -> Railway restart loop -> 502.\n\n- db driver: derive TLS from the URL''s sslmode with libpq semantics\n  (require/prefer/allow encrypt WITHOUT verifying; verify-ca/verify-full\n  verify; bare non-local URLs keep the secure default; the env var still\n  overrides) + full ssl-derivation matrix unit tests\n- every-plugin: one shared Effect-native load policy (loadRemoteWithRetry)\n  — capped exponential backoff under a wall-clock budget, per-attempt\n  failure logs deduped by classification signature, poisoned entry-cache\n  purge between attempts, and fail-fast on permanent failures via\n  classifyPluginFailure().retryable; absorbs withRemoteEntryResilience\n  and the dev-serve duplicate loop; readiness poll gets its own budget\n- host: plugin bootstrap failures stay structured end-to-end —\n  PluginBootstrapError exposes operation + classification, bootstrap\n  logs read [Plugins][<key>] Failed to load plugin (<operation>) —\n  permanent|retryable, and /health + /api/_health surface a structured\n  failures array instead of joined strings\n- log formatting: [MF][<pluginId>] prefixes, drop the redundant\n  Effect.annotateLogs({ plugin }) JSON trailer, [Plugins][<key>] short\n  keys in host boot logs\n\nVerification: everything-dev 696, every-plugin 109 unit + 31\nintegration, host 206, ui 75, api 137 all green; bun typecheck and\nbun lint clean. host test:e2e has 3 pre-existing environmental failures\nidentical on pristine main (needs local docker test DBs).\n\n* refactor(every-plugin): shared PluginLoadFailureInfo contract (review)\n\nMove the structured failure shape from host into every-plugin, next to\nclassifyPluginFailure/PluginFailureClassification — it is the\ncross-package failure contract (loader context + classification), with\nhost re-exporting for its health surface. Also fix the retry-test type\nissues surfaced by the build train (unknown ?? {} narrowing and\nnoUncheckedIndexedAccess on mock calls).\n\n* fix(everything-dev): bos build reports unknown targets instead of bare \"Unknown error\"\n\nselectWorkspaceTargets only resolves app/plugin slot keys, so a\nframework-package name (every-plugin) yielded targets=[] -> a messageless\nerror result; all-skipped selections and a missing bos.config.json had\nthe same shape. BuildResultSchema gains the optional error field the CLI\nalready prints, and all three handler error paths now carry messages:\nunknown targets list the valid slots (framework packages build via the\nprerequisite train), nothing-built lists the skipped targets, missing\nconfig says so.","tree":{"sha":"7aa927b7b943b82eac69e9e049df8c245197e8b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/trees/7aa927b7b943b82eac69e9e049df8c245197e8b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/commits/fd8e4b8247c932928e08e6d9175c0d8b9d6cb01a","verification":{"payload":"tree 7aa927b7b943b82eac69e9e049df8c245197e8b7\nparent df70bd6285516515aae76ac922a2ce6e08eddb60\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1790462832 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790462832 -0500\n\nfix(db,plugins): honor sslmode; structured plugin-boot failure pipeline (#253)\n\n* fix(db,plugins): honor sslmode; structured plugin-boot failure pipeline\n\nRoot cause of the Sep 25 production outage: PR #163''s security batch\nflipped the shared DB driver''s TLS verification to on-by-default for\nevery non-local URL, and managed providers'' sslmode=require URLs carry\ncertificates no client CA bundle can verify — the auth plugin''s pool\n(followed by the api''s) failed at connect time. The pre-existing\nboot pipeline then retried silently for 120s per plugin, pushing the\nserver''s port-bind past the container entrypoint''s 180s health gate ->\nexit(1) -> Railway restart loop -> 502.\n\n- db driver: derive TLS from the URL''s sslmode with libpq semantics\n  (require/prefer/allow encrypt WITHOUT verifying; verify-ca/verify-full\n  verify; bare non-local URLs keep the secure default; the env var still\n  overrides) + full ssl-derivation matrix unit tests\n- every-plugin: one shared Effect-native load policy (loadRemoteWithRetry)\n  — capped exponential backoff under a wall-clock budget, per-attempt\n  failure logs deduped by classification signature, poisoned entry-cache\n  purge between attempts, and fail-fast on permanent failures via\n  classifyPluginFailure().retryable; absorbs withRemoteEntryResilience\n  and the dev-serve duplicate loop; readiness poll gets its own budget\n- host: plugin bootstrap failures stay structured end-to-end —\n  PluginBootstrapError exposes operation + classification, bootstrap\n  logs read [Plugins][<key>] Failed to load plugin (<operation>) —\n  permanent|retryable, and /health + /api/_health surface a structured\n  failures array instead of joined strings\n- log formatting: [MF][<pluginId>] prefixes, drop the redundant\n  Effect.annotateLogs({ plugin }) JSON trailer, [Plugins][<key>] short\n  keys in host boot logs\n\nVerification: everything-dev 696, every-plugin 109 unit + 31\nintegration, host 206, ui 75, api 137 all green; bun typecheck and\nbun lint clean. host test:e2e has 3 pre-existing environmental failures\nidentical on pristine main (needs local docker test DBs).\n\n* refactor(every-plugin): shared PluginLoadFailureInfo contract (review)\n\nMove the structured failure shape from host into every-plugin, next to\nclassifyPluginFailure/PluginFailureClassification — it is the\ncross-package failure contract (loader context + classification), with\nhost re-exporting for its health surface. Also fix the retry-test type\nissues surfaced by the build train (unknown ?? {} narrowing and\nnoUncheckedIndexedAccess on mock calls).\n\n* fix(everything-dev): bos build reports unknown targets instead of bare \"Unknown error\"\n\nselectWorkspaceTargets only resolves app/plugin slot keys, so a\nframework-package name (every-plugin) yielded targets=[] -> a messageless\nerror result; all-skipped selections and a missing bos.config.json had\nthe same shape. BuildResultSchema gains the optional error field the CLI\nalready prints, and all three handler error paths now carry messages:\nunknown targets list the valid slots (framework packages build via the\nprerequisite train), nothing-built lists the skipped targets, missing\nconfig says so.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquEtwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA2MQALG2k3ov98IpTPPf4JG6LFP5\n/bdo782lWkND22HgRkho1MfwOGflcxVoLesrG4f6FIiMd09+DklvF99vHdQ1rLEE\nj5DU5jAToexMuFg8WCaaHaPmKZu6wdmgyWvZhdcLDngx/vfd6nkSx8LmZy9OMl3F\n4fo9KvEYoOxmL0cNhfTS7d/dYyT+QoAVz43eFaYwUNLzSE301qm9AiPBFcw+GhHf\nOIkt9RuuWn1Q67VoMBTx4u6BJ9h+jhJR4KPjZ2XEtWH6cYGpPK43nWxo3YFeY/YQ\nIHONf8s8nPeZ9VoyzL5j5XKRA7CkAMbez3z9zX2GbJouqWZPDiCGm0FqK5bHeKaV\nGWEfnTJ/LzAWhASbMy7FAzGP7hkMxbn+43PUfzMbzL5PEPzW48hW355Ak/GzYXgz\nTmLuWQoyhrQM9UuJRJRInwuqMX0xJNNNa0bsrFAze2qW24OdcLbHcJLM1AKf8KCq\n/DDpiXlWzasaCG3D8neBGDjYq3/bZd148h/EadmHRdEqvRbm+txc27DqUPXjIw05\n37Lv6/VLCkPJ4Ag5fDEErkoAJp3ArHfKRvVBwS8Bb2fim8PQ5HgDbLv8CQSbpUue\nHftre7SJloJp4UA6ew0XfqOwM5oVAxTzAtz2gbVozqj2ZnijVlpTKYLQgDtg9k5D\nN3hWGklwT+Ii5h3ty9Qp\n=IuWM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T22:47:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/fd8e4b8247c932928e08e6d9175c0d8b9d6cb01a","node_id":"C_kwDOT-K1MdoAKGZkOGU0YjgyNDdjOTMyOTI4ZTA4ZTZkOTE3NWMwZDhiOWQ2Y2IwMWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/df70bd6285516515aae76ac922a2ce6e08eddb60","sha":"df70bd6285516515aae76ac922a2ce6e08eddb60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/df70bd6285516515aae76ac922a2ce6e08eddb60"}],"sha":"fd8e4b8247c932928e08e6d9175c0d8b9d6cb01a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/fd8e4b8247c932928e08e6d9175c0d8b9d6cb01a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/df70bd6285516515aae76ac922a2ce6e08eddb60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:31:08Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:31:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: audit cleanup — renumber duplicate ADRs, archive done plans, fix stale claims (#254)\n\nADR renumbering (resolves the four duplicate numbers):\n- 0007-platform-bundle-storage → 0015 (superseded by 0011, kept for history)\n- 0011-unified-log-pipeline → 0016\n- 0012-session-gas-keys → 0017\n- 0013-session-single-owner → 0018\n- all 14 external references updated (AGENTS.md, changesets, advisor-plans,\n  scratch issues); 0019 reserved for advisor-plan 042''s spreadability ADR\n\nADR honesty fixes:\n- 0003 amended: tsconfig.contract.json mechanism replaced by EmitPluginManifest\n- 0010 §7 annotated: bos routes inspector not yet implemented\n- 0011 records the landed foreign-namespace proxy + stale-if-error amendment\n- 0007-runtime/0009 status lines note their amendments\n- docs/adr/README.md index with number-assignment discipline\n\nPlans reorganization:\n- plans/done/ archive (mirrors advisor-plans/done/): orpc-v2-effect-migration,\n  effect-native-plugins, tenant-feature-completeness, ui-extends-ui-federation,\n  db-auth-absorption prototype\n- toml-infra-alchemy: status correction (phases 1/3/4 live only on the\n  unmerged upstream/feat/alchemy branch)\n- every-plugin-db-auth-absorption + advisor-plan 017 row: mostly-done status\n  with the databaseLayer/sync-exit remainder\n- wayfinder tickets 01/04/08/09/11/12 re-annotated; beta-v2-map status banner\n- plans/README.md: grafting row marked superseded (ADR 0007/0008), node-map\n  (#233) pointer, offline plans marked unscheduled\n\nGitHub tracker: closed #190/#104 (delivered), #111/#118 (superseded, reasons\nin the close comments); #166''s parallel-builds half checked off","tree":{"sha":"7f4deea762d303523b2526a8c9f214cc8731d5c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/trees/7f4deea762d303523b2526a8c9f214cc8731d5c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/commits/df70bd6285516515aae76ac922a2ce6e08eddb60","verification":{"payload":"tree 7f4deea762d303523b2526a8c9f214cc8731d5c1\nparent b15e2e45815aef96d7f4a05a0d8f9671a89658ee\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1790461868 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790461868 -0500\n\ndocs: audit cleanup — renumber duplicate ADRs, archive done plans, fix stale claims (#254)\n\nADR renumbering (resolves the four duplicate numbers):\n- 0007-platform-bundle-storage → 0015 (superseded by 0011, kept for history)\n- 0011-unified-log-pipeline → 0016\n- 0012-session-gas-keys → 0017\n- 0013-session-single-owner → 0018\n- all 14 external references updated (AGENTS.md, changesets, advisor-plans,\n  scratch issues); 0019 reserved for advisor-plan 042''s spreadability ADR\n\nADR honesty fixes:\n- 0003 amended: tsconfig.contract.json mechanism replaced by EmitPluginManifest\n- 0010 §7 annotated: bos routes inspector not yet implemented\n- 0011 records the landed foreign-namespace proxy + stale-if-error amendment\n- 0007-runtime/0009 status lines note their amendments\n- docs/adr/README.md index with number-assignment discipline\n\nPlans reorganization:\n- plans/done/ archive (mirrors advisor-plans/done/): orpc-v2-effect-migration,\n  effect-native-plugins, tenant-feature-completeness, ui-extends-ui-federation,\n  db-auth-absorption prototype\n- toml-infra-alchemy: status correction (phases 1/3/4 live only on the\n  unmerged upstream/feat/alchemy branch)\n- every-plugin-db-auth-absorption + advisor-plan 017 row: mostly-done status\n  with the databaseLayer/sync-exit remainder\n- wayfinder tickets 01/04/08/09/11/12 re-annotated; beta-v2-map status banner\n- plans/README.md: grafting row marked superseded (ADR 0007/0008), node-map\n  (#233) pointer, offline plans marked unscheduled\n\nGitHub tracker: closed #190/#104 (delivered), #111/#118 (superseded, reasons\nin the close comments); #166''s parallel-builds half checked off","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquEesCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUb4QADRTraEWneQ1HCQ7GAvqJpi6\nZ2bqOCS7bzQJ6verpnndYtSpRJZtvggKNvxfPBuDTizyGa3xApiCkH89eQAcnZjx\nfUahHCxIaxNxB/PW32X4hx1LSA3fPrR6l8hx2r4lj5SNnWdGkKzYkK5QUGfrkBef\nKti1YY2a/ew8vp7aPsr+p7DMEx2V5C6evgqbGeGHX1pg52exYaLm4kam3bs4Rzg0\nYEgJgRqqU6bGGhrfJsYMws/J8tPhHyXeYlTdM7VSo9tHQ8dzHuxCwJhsZO7u8JE/\nznbS8vuKPspyy4no6tnlYfSx9uX3TX+MkbP13quyQbQFL7wPBRCdoAPifC3kxNbs\ngEE/y9iZK/AR3oAS6swJYQKvm+4LyPE62UhuVG0P3Hol5ZRlX+kl0QqTaWJoA5Bu\n6LyExXBjPvf7/RmUKKL4e1gs+Dtp2c6HDYM4mNCEgiEztc7hKH7TTbtREjhakR/M\nMXEhEySXM+USaRIlyB+BhqEtpe0kU/2LY927eP+sl+qufwooMbSnVj2BzcT/5Jwf\nnFL1q6CJvMSeLIHdSQXKyyZgCCIzwwE3U0/Y3MsPwBl2WbRlyVn4T8332EuwRdEt\nd3TmuzzWniFPiAC/nmDeb9zvwfekPy4Rr9K4geK0rUixJC25/eNWv4Enazipz4+w\nuQ0xdbR2c8rGDBvjngwD\n=UB/V\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T22:31:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/df70bd6285516515aae76ac922a2ce6e08eddb60","node_id":"C_kwDOT-K1MdoAKGRmNzBiZDYyODU1MTY1MTVhYWU3NmFjOTIyYTJjZTZlMDhlZGRiNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/b15e2e45815aef96d7f4a05a0d8f9671a89658ee","sha":"b15e2e45815aef96d7f4a05a0d8f9671a89658ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/b15e2e45815aef96d7f4a05a0d8f9671a89658ee"}],"sha":"df70bd6285516515aae76ac922a2ce6e08eddb60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/df70bd6285516515aae76ac922a2ce6e08eddb60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/b15e2e45815aef96d7f4a05a0d8f9671a89658ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:51:16Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:51:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(auth): manage linked NEAR accounts; phone sign-in desktop-only (#251)\n\n* feat(auth): manage linked NEAR accounts; phone sign-in desktop-only\n\n- Settings > Sign-in methods: list all linked NEAR accounts, make\n  primary, unlink with confirmation, link another named account, or\n  create a NEAR account derived from a passkey when none is linked\n  (gated on passkeys + passkey wallet availability). Linking uses the\n  dedicated near.link action instead of a sign-in ceremony.\n- Login page: hide ''Sign in with your phone'' on mobile viewports and\n  adapt the no-passkey hint; add useMediaQuery/useIsDesktop hooks.\n\n* refactor(auth): address two-axis review findings\n\n- Surface account-load failures (error state + retry) instead of\n  rendering the empty state; passkey eligibility requires a successful\n  passkey list rather than swallowing errors\n- Hide ''Make primary'' on the account that is already primary\n- Export isDeterministicAccountId from better-near-auth and use it in\n  the UI instead of duplicating the NEP-616 account regex\n- Add useNetworkId() hook; drop the duplicated networkId casts in\n  login and auth-methods\n- Move query keys to lib/query-keys; collapse the callback-to-promise\n  wrappers into one toPromise helper\n- Cache MediaQueryList per query in useMediaQuery\n- Delete unused plugins/auth/ui/src/lib/use-near-account.ts","tree":{"sha":"a3d052119778eb765256450993d674a85d2ecf9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/trees/a3d052119778eb765256450993d674a85d2ecf9c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/commits/b15e2e45815aef96d7f4a05a0d8f9671a89658ee","verification":{"payload":"tree a3d052119778eb765256450993d674a85d2ecf9c\nparent ead8520f1448b3f8a538f79c5379e309c4f69b0a\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1790459476 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790459476 -0500\n\nfeat(auth): manage linked NEAR accounts; phone sign-in desktop-only (#251)\n\n* feat(auth): manage linked NEAR accounts; phone sign-in desktop-only\n\n- Settings > Sign-in methods: list all linked NEAR accounts, make\n  primary, unlink with confirmation, link another named account, or\n  create a NEAR account derived from a passkey when none is linked\n  (gated on passkeys + passkey wallet availability). Linking uses the\n  dedicated near.link action instead of a sign-in ceremony.\n- Login page: hide ''Sign in with your phone'' on mobile viewports and\n  adapt the no-passkey hint; add useMediaQuery/useIsDesktop hooks.\n\n* refactor(auth): address two-axis review findings\n\n- Surface account-load failures (error state + retry) instead of\n  rendering the empty state; passkey eligibility requires a successful\n  passkey list rather than swallowing errors\n- Hide ''Make primary'' on the account that is already primary\n- Export isDeterministicAccountId from better-near-auth and use it in\n  the UI instead of duplicating the NEP-616 account regex\n- Add useNetworkId() hook; drop the duplicated networkId casts in\n  login and auth-methods\n- Move query keys to lib/query-keys; collapse the callback-to-promise\n  wrappers into one toPromise helper\n- Cache MediaQueryList per query in useMediaQuery\n- Delete unused plugins/auth/ui/src/lib/use-near-account.ts","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquD5UCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhtkQAIwdIo8yzwl7pJI5F5VQ7eKk\ncXttMgZ51hQa44OP6vle/mamYBBjrSMGBjS/dME2fRhcHbpUrcUvwlmsNnTo+7Tr\n1WK4FruY0lTTQ+IBZrbYCfcM/hMYAVBN0d1cm/84P+9yVXpFvEsWvR8wFQZFHF4d\njj5F2eTEpGSZQgrT3BRzMa/jla96Mb5wWSRhUh6l0FxnIAA3Od0rtFJS5UsmTxf1\naD778cZLIRSpdnrQ0tBG0Ydmlv5Qn4ClCAP2Mox7assOCSXbFwRk9C/2mn8u7gqp\npXYVj6DlMHS4q9cGvCmn2XGqiFW2+vceM+oeXp6mZO7C1Vx7svoSYxzQoWD5DWmP\nxbQIeA4xkgKbqS/3Ykpd5SZ6cstmJDrX4ju3xYTJuUfdW1tFyM0mhF36Vn+U7yrm\nu8o2+Yd8YhGjD2uPYU+ql4a2ihvsL8Xkn1Fhbztz+jzZ2MZ0fl56ouqQgSP+0t1h\n+DrAKnFZM28nqnPL98Z0E62wjuMCPg4VXklwcYEH9C8/IJaF6MXQtW8kHMTVilnh\n0Be+nMVR1KX0yhbrsP1