-route-search-validation\n\nfix(every-plugin): plugin routes lose validateSearch and ssr during composition","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqttdWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnMQQAEpH9RVhMc20wU9+iislA6i2\n9E/hKQzeZ5dblQXEi36ynjjxAiRxJmR8G/9mtGX/+L7PHSTlJO2O2vfooZABSdZJ\n+FW8I3cYqjTdjW+9VhCntfmbQ9NTJVTig4Z6ihTB0waYc8auzjNyjPbGY6FWq8km\np1HIs5x64tMpYlCYhFTrXlzEKaPVGfyQXPrSINRobd9oj/gL7/ZmX719zXPvotmN\nQfjS7wUBqLs2LYfnLeXueGloxSFan4F/Nr5b6UdVPAu1ftbtXipMuvI9TRSi3CwD\nePYzcWbcA8Q7e3fbN/o+uGfcwwx0CIK0uCUiHCeLwMzUyVfdi7fU1ZgWuzW0XUwu\ncvKkFzmLXy25gDS2Ivmt4Yij6am+IQhwbQBpuMIBaibquBze/+eCzAHMZAxgUyXG\nbXPGCnqgXfoCQ9OOObAQBMXPFZkDdL5ybZ5YOEPh3BRBSb4kIgtrFWa3vYTKzKUE\nTkWB40rep1wpTwB99bw8Sv6bLmIJBBydvIJjFuhw6gM1VUhA+tYzVJ3bfnjaMPbw\nGhV4Rhnf3JgGAlF74WIAa0Qs984SYDdzF7VogitI8mRXudGwGDYj4qf6PZSG4+6k\n3FRtmnRLACRw8pD6/D7cJGB/UW7/6MWkK66D2/5Q5+9eed7d0PPCZNF/g+0/Hnod\ndqdvr8TOhN1+rDrbrxno\n=9Z+3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T20:19:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/42fbe9a47b7633614d36bb53b4b0d8a567ee278c","node_id":"C_kwDOT-K1MdoAKDQyZmJlOWE0N2I3NjMzNjE0ZDM2YmI1M2I0YjBkOGE1NjdlZTI3OGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/d6c0e26c04e150c5c1852a0fa06397696a8eb83a","sha":"d6c0e26c04e150c5c1852a0fa06397696a8eb83a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/d6c0e26c04e150c5c1852a0fa06397696a8eb83a"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/b18df8bdd3e6d781ecf85e33b58af6d34f787e36","sha":"b18df8bdd3e6d781ecf85e33b58af6d34f787e36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/b18df8bdd3e6d781ecf85e33b58af6d34f787e36"}],"sha":"42fbe9a47b7633614d36bb53b4b0d8a567ee278c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/42fbe9a47b7633614d36bb53b4b0d8a567ee278c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46527178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/itexpert120","id":46527178,"login":"itexpert120","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/b18df8bdd3e6d781ecf85e33b58af6d34f787e36/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T20:11:19Z","email":"itexpert120@outlook.com","name":"Zeeshan Ahmad"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T20:11:19Z","email":"itexpert120@outlook.com","name":"Zeeshan Ahmad"},"message":"refactor(every-plugin): one route-option list for pick and construct\n\nAddress review: the generated pick and constructTree now read a single\nROUTE_OPTION_KEYS list with a type-level completeness check against\nRouteOptionsBundle, add preloadStaleTime/pendingMs/pendingMinMs, carry\nthe core root route''s authored options, and strengthen the tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"adc53edcefce61f1289de04394f5e17f53eade03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/trees/adc53edcefce61f1289de04394f5e17f53eade03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/commits/b18df8bdd3e6d781ecf85e33b58af6d34f787e36","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46527178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/itexpert120","id":46527178,"login":"itexpert120","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/b18df8bdd3e6d781ecf85e33b58af6d34f787e36","node_id":"C_kwDOT-K1MdoAKGIxOGRmOGJkZDNlNmQ3ODFlY2Y4NWUzM2I1OGFmNmQzNGY3ODdlMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/96b00a00b98d11d78304219ca23864a9fb2796b0","sha":"96b00a00b98d11d78304219ca23864a9fb2796b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/96b00a00b98d11d78304219ca23864a9fb2796b0"}],"sha":"b18df8bdd3e6d781ecf85e33b58af6d34f787e36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/b18df8bdd3e6d781ecf85e33b58af6d34f787e36"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46527178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/itexpert120","id":46527178,"login":"itexpert120","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/96b00a00b98d11d78304219ca23864a9fb2796b0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T19:47:45Z","email":"itexpert120@outlook.com","name":"Zeeshan Ahmad"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T19:47:45Z","email":"itexpert120@outlook.com","name":"Zeeshan Ahmad"},"message":"fix(every-plugin): keep plugin route contract through composition\n\nPlugin routes lose validateSearch and ssr during composition: the\ngenerated routeConfig pick and constructTree only carried loader,\nbeforeLoad, head, staticData and components. Carry the authored route\ncontract as well (validateSearch, search middlewares, params, loaderDeps,\ncontext, ssr, staleTime, gcTime, shouldReload) through one shared list so\nmount, layout and leaf routes stay in step.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b309e944b01906b99d3ab31fb060bfc96e816c3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/trees/b309e944b01906b99d3ab31fb060bfc96e816c3d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/commits/96b00a00b98d11d78304219ca23864a9fb2796b0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46527178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/itexpert120","id":46527178,"login":"itexpert120","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/itexpert120","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/96b00a00b98d11d78304219ca23864a9fb2796b0","node_id":"C_kwDOT-K1MdoAKDk2YjAwYTAwYjk4ZDExZDc4MzA0MjE5Y2EyMzg2NGE5ZmIyNzk2YjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/d6c0e26c04e150c5c1852a0fa06397696a8eb83a","sha":"d6c0e26c04e150c5c1852a0fa06397696a8eb83a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/d6c0e26c04e150c5c1852a0fa06397696a8eb83a"}],"sha":"96b00a00b98d11d78304219ca23864a9fb2796b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/96b00a00b98d11d78304219ca23864a9fb2796b0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/d6c0e26c04e150c5c1852a0fa06397696a8eb83a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T17:07:14Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T17:07:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: unified log pipeline, improved dev cli (#163)\n\n* feat(everything-dev): typed mount contract for ui plugin grafting\n\nPlan 023. The graft protocol''s mount vocabulary becomes a compile-time\ncontract instead of a stringly convention:\n\n- mount-registry.ts: MOUNT_REGISTRY now satisfies Record<string, MountEntry>\n  so MountId derives from its canonical keys; MOUNTS exports the union\n  value; MOUNT_ALIASES is typed Record<string, MountId> (moved here from\n  types.ts, which re-exports both for surface stability)\n- define.ts: defineUiPlugin({ name, mounts, tree }) validates the tree at\n  construction — every root child declaring a _mount must resolve to a\n  declared canonical mount, else it throws with the child id and a\n  closest-mount hint; associations ride a module-scoped WeakMap\n- compose.ts: defined modules graft via declared mounts (no\n  re-derivation); raw trees keep the deriveMountId fallback, now the\n  declaredSegment derivation with a MountId return type\n- digest-version.ts: MOUNT_REGISTRY_VERSION -> 2026-09-19.1 (graft input\n  semantics changed; all compose digests invalidate)\n- README row records the agreed deviation (validation covers _-roots\n  only) and the plan-024 note (_template has no ui tree yet)\n\nVerification: everything-dev 489 tests green (compose suite 20 incl. 9\nnew), host 175 green; no new typecheck or lint findings vs baseline.\n\n* feat(api,host): platform bundle storage + publish --cdn platform (plan 029)\n\nPlatform CDN provider so bos publish --deploy needs no Zephyr/Cloudflare\naccount: bundles upload to the platform storage via the CLI session and\nare served publicly from /bundles/* with immutable cache headers.\n\n- api: bundle_objects table + BundleStorage Effect service (R2 drop-in\n  seam), oRPC contract routes POST /storage/bundles (auth''d, ceilings,\n  path allowlist, traversal guard, server-side SRI) and\n  GET /bundles/{account}/{gateway}/{workspace}/{+path} (public, File\n  output)\n- host: route-scoped bodyLimit for uploads, second prefix-symmetric\n  OpenAPIHandler mount at /bundles/* (+ proxy mode), generic\n  ResponseHeadersHandlerPlugin\n- cli: deploy.cdn config (default zephyr), --cdn flag, platform\n  uploader (dist/ artifacts -> platform storage), session requirement,\n  bos login refusal without one\n- docs: ADR 0007 (file transport as oRPC contract concern), plan 033\n  (derived OpenAPI mounts follow-up), AGENTS.md deploy.cdn, changeset\n\nLive dev-stack E2E (bos publish --deploy --cdn platform + bos mf check)\nleft for the operator.\n\n* chore(everything-dev): drop dead cdnUploadHandled param (code-review follow-up)\n\n* refactor(api): effect-native storage handlers — .effect() + yield* StorageTag (code-review follow-ups)\n\n- storage routes follow the template convention: .effect() generators with\n  yield* StorageTag (StorageTag now exposed from initialize''s returned\n  layer); inline auth via Effect.fail(errors.UNAUTHORIZED/FORBIDDEN) with\n  the every-plugin/errors data shapes\n- AGENTS.md ''Adding API Endpoints'': new-route handler convention enforced\n  (.effect + yield* Tag; Context.get reserved for streaming; shared\n  auth middlewares'' .use() typing gap documented)\n- ADR 0007: handler-convention bullet + recorded seam deviation\n  (platform provider skips workspace scripts.deploy; parent uploads\n  dist/ via applyDeployResults)\n\n* chore: pin zephyr plugins to 1.3.0 (deliberate catalog pin, drift guard)\n\n* fix(api): StorageTag Self type parameter (class-self-mismatch rule)\n\n* feat(dev): unified log pipeline (normalize, classify, filter, broadcast)\n\nEvery dev-session process line now flows through a single pure\npipeline that normalizes multi-line blocks, classifies level and\ncategory, and level-filters before broadcasting to the three sinks\n(screen tail, log file, l/shutdown export) so the views agree by\nconstruction.\n\n- normalize: Effect Logger { } objects, stack-trace continuations\n- classify: WARN [Better Auth] stdout lines are warn; legacy\n  LOG_NOISE_PATTERNS folded in as mf/build info; clean exits\n  (code 0) classify as shutdown info, not [ERR]\n- filter: --log-level / BOS_LOG_LEVEL (default warn; DEBUG = all);\n  [Database] startup runs collapse to one db ready per plugin\n- file sink always receives everything; export prints a filtered\n  summary plus a full-logs pointer\n- one ANSI-strip implementation; ADR 0011 records the decision\n\n* feat(dev): stream-driven ANSI TUI — drop ink/react from the CLI package\n\nbos dev''s interactive view is now a pure render function over a single\nsession-state holder (processes, log events). A hand-rolled alt-screen\nrenderer redraws on state change, reads q / l / ctrl+c from raw stdin,\nand restores the terminal on unmount. The piped/non-TTY fallback reuses\nthe same render helpers and prints incrementally — the near-verbatim\nduplicated streaming view is deleted.\n\n- ink, react (peer), gradient-string and their type packages removed\n  from the CLI package manifest; build externals updated\n- banner gradient replaced with a small truecolor ramp in the theme\n  module (colors resolve at call time, so chalk level is honored)\n- renderDevState / renderProcessRow / renderLogLine are unit-tested;\n  renderer handle covered for dedupe, incremental rows, ready-block\n  once, alt-screen enter/exit, and key handling\n\n* feat(dev): one row per plugin in the service table\n\nplugin-ui:* companion rows merge into their parent as an inline\n''· ui :<port>'' annotation (the auth app slot renders as one PLUGINS\nrow, e.g. ''AUTH (local) running :3002 · ui :3011''); SERVICES lists\nonly host/api/ui; a merged row counts as ready only when both its api\nand ui surfaces are ready, and ''All N services running'' counts merged\nrows. Sectioning, display names, colors, and column widths live in the\nshared render module consumed by both the TTY and non-TTY paths — the\nplugin: prefix check that orphaned plugin-ui rows into SERVICES is\ngone.\n\nAuth-mirror detection is single-sourced in isAuthMirrorPluginEntry\n(structural AuthSlotShape signature): the inline copies in the infra\nplanner (allocateServices, buildServiceDescriptors, assigned runtime\nconfig), the dependency DAG, and the api contract bridge are deleted.\nallocateServices now also matches remote-url mirrors, fixing its prior\nallocate/descriptor disagreement; planner tests pin the semantics.\n\n* fix(dev): TUI quit escalation + viewport-bounded repaint — quittable sessions, no scrollback bleed\n\n* docs(plans): CLI audit plans 037-041 + ADR 0012 + plan 036 amendments (env/port truth, registry lock, docs ride-along)\n\n* fix(dev): repaint erase-to-EOL, renderer dead after unmount, shutdown messages visible (plan 037 phase 1)\n\n* fix(every-plugin): watcher kill escalation + parent-death supervision — rspack/rsbuild watchers can never orphan (plan 042)\n\n* fix(dev): quittable at every lifecycle phase — startup quit kills spawned children, no self-SIGKILL, honest exit codes (plan 037 phase 2)\n\n* test(regression): Go teardown suite — run a real dev stack, kill it, prove everything is dead (036/037/042 acceptance)\n\n* refactor(regression): rename teardown suite to framework — home for everything-dev-level regression/e2e\n\n* feat(everything-dev): bos kill escalation + orphan adoption + verified port release (plan 036 phase 1)\n\n* feat(everything-dev): atomic port-block allocation — announced drift, persist-only-explicit, lease-shaped registry (plan 036 phase 2)\n\n* refactor(everything-dev): scope-owned child handles — acquireRelease teardown by construction (plan 036 phase 3)\n\n* docs(agents): port-allocation model matches ADR 0012 — block layout, persist-only-explicit, escalating kill (plan 036 phase 4 docs ride-along)\n\n* docs(plans): 036 DONE — port leases and scoped stack landed through phase 4\n\n* fix(dev): display/lifecycle defect batch — non-TTY log freeze, --interactive non-TTY fallback, post-ready death status, detectStatus false positives, spawn-error surfacing, per-session log files (plan 037 phase 3)\n\n* fix(everything-dev): env & port truth — preflight probes credentialed DB URLs, origin keys generated-owned at every tier, DB ports honor persisted state (plan 038)\n\n* fix(everything-dev): security hardening — validated plugin keys, no shell spawn, TLS default, fail-closed SRI, key file perms, masked drift logs (plan 039)\n\n* perf(verification): root chain runs framework suites; dev spawn unblocked from network checks; config tests stub the network (plan 040)\n\n* chore(everything-dev): CLI hygiene batch — dead deps removed, zod as dependency, catalog pins, no private-API casts, doc truth, dedupes (plan 041)\n\n* docs(plans): 037-041 status rows — all DONE with commit refs\n\n* chore(everything-dev): vitest pool tuning measured and rejected — singleFork doubles wall time and leaks module state; keep isolated parallel forks\n\n* fix(everything-dev): resolve dev-latest by session start time, not mtime (CI-stable tie-break)\n\n* fix(everything-dev): block-allocate the auth mirror''s ui port again\n\nThe atomic port-block allocator (plan 036 phase 2) restructured the\nplugin loop into a whole-entry mirror skip, dropping the plugin-ui:auth\nport allocation that pre-regression allocateServices granted outside the\n!mirror check. With no port, the planner''s patchedUi left the mirror''s\nui.url empty and the host advertised the auth remote as a relative\n/remoteEntry.js — the browser could never load the auth plugin UI, so\n/login never rendered (dev:ssr + dev:csr regression suites red from\n2674acc0 onward).\n\nRestore the pre-regression semantics under the block model: the mirror\nstill gets no plugin:<id> api entry, but a local mirror with a local ui\ngets its plugin-ui:<id> entry allocated, which patches\nruntimeConfig.plugins.auth.ui.url and feeds the folder-form auth\ndescriptor''s BOS_UI_PORT.\n\nAlso sanitize the regression stack log filename (regression-dev-ssr.log)\n— the mode''s colon made upload-artifact reject the whole artifacts\nupload, hiding the very logs needed to debug this.\n\nNew planInfra regression test pins the mirror ui allocation and the\npatched ui.url.\n\n* fix(everything-dev): keep harness-injected origins in config-path production starts\n\nA registry start is a real deployment — localhost CORS_ORIGIN/BASE_URL\nthere are stray dev leftovers and stay purged. An explicit --config-path\nstart (regression harness, local production stack) injects those origins\nas deployment truth; deleting them made the in-process host derive the\nauth origin as https://<domain>, so better-auth issued Secure cookies no\nhttp client could send back (empty sessions, 401s, INVALID_ORIGIN).\n\n* fix(everything-dev): purge localhost origins only on registry starts\n\nThe gate moves from !configPath to a positive isRegistryStart check:\nbare local bos start runs (no --config-path, no BOS_ACCOUNT/BOS_GATEWAY)\nload the local config and are local starts too — their origins are\ndeployment truth, not stray dev leftovers. Adds unit tests for all\nthree config-source outcomes and a changeset.\n\n* fix(dev): quittable TUI — resume raw stdin so q/Ctrl-C reach the key handler\n\nBun''s TTY stdin never enters flowing mode from a bare data listener\nattach. With the dev TUI''s raw mode on, ISIG is disabled, so Ctrl-C\ngenerated no SIGINT, and the \\x03/q bytes never arrived either — the\nsession was unquittable from its own terminal (bos kill from a second\nterminal was the only exit). The renderer now resumes stdin after\nenabling raw mode; unmount pauses it.\n\nQuit-path cleanup in the same sweep:\n- devApp''s SIGINT/SIGTERM handler now delegates to the same\n  requestShutdownEscalating the TUI uses (the two bodies had drifted\n  into twins); signal counting lives in one place\n- emergencyKill reuses reapGroup instead of re-implementing the\n  group-kill fallback\n- suspendForceExitTimer renamed rearmForceExitTimer — it extends the\n  deadline, it does not suspend it\n- l (export logs) no longer counts toward the quit escalation, so\n  l-then-q quits gracefully instead of force-exiting past the export\n- force-exit timer is unref''d on both paths\n\nRegression coverage: the framework suite gains a pty harness\n(creack/pty) and two tests that boot a fully interactive stack, wait\nfor the TUI''s alt-screen mount, then quit via q and via the raw Ctrl-C\nbyte — asserting the CLI exits 0, every service child and watcher\ngrandchild dies, ports free, and the registry cleans up. Both failed\n(red) before the resume fix; both pass after.\n\n* fix(everything-dev): drop the SERVICE_CONFIGS annotation duplicated by the satisfies check\n\nThe rebase merge of main (post-#179) kept BOTH the Record<string,\nPick<...>> annotation and the branch''s trailing `as const satisfies`.\nThe annotation widens the const back to Record, so under\nnoUncheckedIndexedAccess (plugins/apps tsconfig) every dot access\nyields Pick | undefined and the descriptor spreads became optional —\ntypecheck failed on the auth descriptor. Keep only the satisfies form:\nsame contract enforcement, literal keys stay required.\n\n* feat(dev): surface folder-form plugin UIs in the TUI — auth row shows its ui port\n\nFolder-form plugin UIs (ui/ dir inside the plugin workspace, no own\npackage.json) run as a child of the plugin''s dev process via\nBOS_UI_PORT — no plugin-ui:<id> service is spawned, so the one-row-per-\nplugin renderer had nothing to merge and the port was invisible unless\nyou tailed the log stream ([auth] ├─ 🎨 UI: http://localhost:3011).\n\nServiceDescriptor now carries uiPort next to the BOS_UI_PORT env in\nboth folder-form branches (regular plugin + auth mirror);\ngetProcessStates threads it into the process state; mergePluginUiRows\nsynthesizes the same inline annotation package-form companions get.\nThe auth row now reads: AUTH (local) running :3002 · ui :3011.","tree":{"sha":"d0b4641c6cbbf6cf970df17aca649a409e68e0bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/trees/d0b4641c6cbbf6cf970df17aca649a409e68e0bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/commits/d6c0e26c04e150c5c1852a0fa06397696a8eb83a","verification":{"payload":"tree d0b4641c6cbbf6cf970df17aca649a409e68e0bb\nparent e5482b864841270563a8be19e6541be855873b0e\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1790356034 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790356034 -0500\n\nfeat: unified log pipeline, improved dev cli (#163)\n\n* feat(everything-dev): typed mount contract for ui plugin grafting\n\nPlan 023. The graft protocol''s mount vocabulary becomes a compile-time\ncontract instead of a stringly convention:\n\n- mount-registry.ts: MOUNT_REGISTRY now satisfies Record<string, MountEntry>\n  so MountId derives from its canonical keys; MOUNTS exports the union\n  value; MOUNT_ALIASES is typed Record<string, MountId> (moved here from\n  types.ts, which re-exports both for surface stability)\n- define.ts: defineUiPlugin({ name, mounts, tree }) validates the tree at\n  construction — every root child declaring a _mount must resolve to a\n  declared canonical mount, else it throws with the child id and a\n  closest-mount hint; associations ride a module-scoped WeakMap\n- compose.ts: defined modules graft via declared mounts (no\n  re-derivation); raw trees keep the deriveMountId fallback, now the\n  declaredSegment derivation with a MountId return type\n- digest-version.ts: MOUNT_REGISTRY_VERSION -> 2026-09-19.1 (graft input\n  semantics changed; all compose digests invalidate)\n- README row records the agreed deviation (validation covers _-roots\n  only) and the plan-024 note (_template has no ui tree yet)\n\nVerification: everything-dev 489 tests green (compose suite 20 incl. 9\nnew), host 175 green; no new typecheck or lint findings vs baseline.\n\n* feat(api,host): platform bundle storage + publish --cdn platform (plan 029)\n\nPlatform CDN provider so bos publish --deploy needs no Zephyr/Cloudflare\naccount: bundles upload to the platform storage via the CLI session and\nare served publicly from /bundles/* with immutable cache headers.\n\n- api: bundle_objects table + BundleStorage Effect service (R2 drop-in\n  seam), oRPC contract routes POST /storage/bundles (auth''d, ceilings,\n  path allowlist, traversal guard, server-side SRI) and\n  GET /bundles/{account}/{gateway}/{workspace}/{+path} (public, File\n  output)\n- host: route-scoped bodyLimit for uploads, second prefix-symmetric\n  OpenAPIHandler mount at /bundles/* (+ proxy mode), generic\n  ResponseHeadersHandlerPlugin\n- cli: deploy.cdn config (default zephyr), --cdn flag, platform\n  uploader (dist/ artifacts -> platform storage), session requirement,\n  bos login refusal without one\n- docs: ADR 0007 (file transport as oRPC contract concern), plan 033\n  (derived OpenAPI mounts follow-up), AGENTS.md deploy.cdn, changeset\n\nLive dev-stack E2E (bos publish --deploy --cdn platform + bos mf check)\nleft for the operator.\n\n* chore(everything-dev): drop dead cdnUploadHandled param (code-review follow-up)\n\n* refactor(api): effect-native storage handlers — .effect() + yield* StorageTag (code-review follow-ups)\n\n- storage routes follow the template convention: .effect() generators with\n  yield* StorageTag (StorageTag now exposed from initialize''s returned\n  layer); inline auth via Effect.fail(errors.UNAUTHORIZED/FORBIDDEN) with\n  the every-plugin/errors data shapes\n- AGENTS.md ''Adding API Endpoints'': new-route handler convention enforced\n  (.effect + yield* Tag; Context.get reserved for streaming; shared\n  auth middlewares'' .use() typing gap documented)\n- ADR 0007: handler-convention bullet + recorded seam deviation\n  (platform provider skips workspace scripts.deploy; parent uploads\n  dist/ via applyDeployResults)\n\n* chore: pin zephyr plugins to 1.3.0 (deliberate catalog pin, drift guard)\n\n* fix(api): StorageTag Self type parameter (class-self-mismatch rule)\n\n* feat(dev): unified log pipeline (normalize, classify, filter, broadcast)\n\nEvery dev-session process line now flows through a single pure\npipeline that normalizes multi-line blocks, classifies level and\ncategory, and level-filters before broadcasting to the three sinks\n(screen tail, log file, l/shutdown export) so the views agree by\nconstruction.\n\n- normalize: Effect Logger { } objects, stack-trace continuations\n- classify: WARN [Better Auth] stdout lines are warn; legacy\n  LOG_NOISE_PATTERNS folded in as mf/build info; clean exits\n  (code 0) classify as shutdown info, not [ERR]\n- filter: --log-level / BOS_LOG_LEVEL (default warn; DEBUG = all);\n  [Database] startup runs collapse to one db ready per plugin\n- file sink always receives everything; export prints a filtered\n  summary plus a full-logs pointer\n- one ANSI-strip implementation; ADR 0011 records the decision\n\n* feat(dev): stream-driven ANSI TUI — drop ink/react from the CLI package\n\nbos dev''s interactive view is now a pure render function over a single\nsession-state holder (processes, log events). A hand-rolled alt-screen\nrenderer redraws on state change, reads q / l / ctrl+c from raw stdin,\nand restores the terminal on unmount. The piped/non-TTY fallback reuses\nthe same render helpers and prints incrementally — the near-verbatim\nduplicated streaming view is deleted.\n\n- ink, react (peer), gradient-string and their type packages removed\n  from the CLI package manifest; build externals updated\n- banner gradient replaced with a small truecolor ramp in the theme\n  module (colors resolve at call time, so chalk level is honored)\n- renderDevState / renderProcessRow / renderLogLine are unit-tested;\n  renderer handle covered for dedupe, incremental rows, ready-block\n  once, alt-screen enter/exit, and key handling\n\n* feat(dev): one row per plugin in the service table\n\nplugin-ui:* companion rows merge into their parent as an inline\n''· ui :<port>'' annotation (the auth app slot renders as one PLUGINS\nrow, e.g. ''AUTH (local) running :3002 · ui :3011''); SERVICES lists\nonly host/api/ui; a merged row counts as ready only when both its api\nand ui surfaces are ready, and ''All N services running'' counts merged\nrows. Sectioning, display names, colors, and column widths live in the\nshared render module consumed by both the TTY and non-TTY paths — the\nplugin: prefix check that orphaned plugin-ui rows into SERVICES is\ngone.\n\nAuth-mirror detection is single-sourced in isAuthMirrorPluginEntry\n(structural AuthSlotShape signature): the inline copies in the infra\nplanner (allocateServices, buildServiceDescriptors, assigned runtime\nconfig), the dependency DAG, and the api contract bridge are deleted.\nallocateServices now also matches remote-url mirrors, fixing its prior\nallocate/descriptor disagreement; planner tests pin the semantics.\n\n* fix(dev): TUI quit escalation + viewport-bounded repaint — quittable sessions, no scrollback bleed\n\n* docs(plans): CLI audit plans 037-041 + ADR 0012 + plan 036 amendments (env/port truth, registry lock, docs ride-along)\n\n* fix(dev): repaint erase-to-EOL, renderer dead after unmount, shutdown messages visible (plan 037 phase 1)\n\n* fix(every-plugin): watcher kill escalation + parent-death supervision — rspack/rsbuild watchers can never orphan (plan 042)\n\n* fix(dev): quittable at every lifecycle phase — startup quit kills spawned children, no self-SIGKILL, honest exit codes (plan 037 phase 2)\n\n* test(regression): Go teardown suite — run a real dev stack, kill it, prove everything is dead (036/037/042 acceptance)\n\n* refactor(regression): rename teardown suite to framework — home for everything-dev-level regression/e2e\n\n* feat(everything-dev): bos kill escalation + orphan adoption + verified port release (plan 036 phase 1)\n\n* feat(everything-dev): atomic port-block allocation — announced drift, persist-only-explicit, lease-shaped registry (plan 036 phase 2)\n\n* refactor(everything-dev): scope-owned child handles — acquireRelease teardown by construction (plan 036 phase 3)\n\n* docs(agents): port-allocation model matches ADR 0012 — block layout, persist-only-explicit, escalating kill (plan 036 phase 4 docs ride-along)\n\n* docs(plans): 036 DONE — port leases and scoped stack landed through phase 4\n\n* fix(dev): display/lifecycle defect batch — non-TTY log freeze, --interactive non-TTY fallback, post-ready death status, detectStatus false positives, spawn-error surfacing, per-session log files (plan 037 phase 3)\n\n* fix(everything-dev): env & port truth — preflight probes credentialed DB URLs, origin keys generated-owned at every tier, DB ports honor persisted state (plan 038)\n\n* fix(everything-dev): security hardening — validated plugin keys, no shell spawn, TLS default, fail-closed SRI, key file perms, masked drift logs (plan 039)\n\n* perf(verification): root chain runs framework suites; dev spawn unblocked from network checks; config tests stub the network (plan 040)\n\n* chore(everything-dev): CLI hygiene batch — dead deps removed, zod as dependency, catalog pins, no private-API casts, doc truth, dedupes (plan 041)\n\n* docs(plans): 037-041 status rows — all DONE with commit refs\n\n* chore(everything-dev): vitest pool tuning measured and rejected — singleFork doubles wall time and leaks module state; keep isolated parallel forks\n\n* fix(everything-dev): resolve dev-latest by session start time, not mtime (CI-stable tie-break)\n\n* fix(everything-dev): block-allocate the auth mirror''s ui port again\n\nThe atomic port-block allocator (plan 036 phase 2) restructured the\nplugin loop into a whole-entry mirror skip, dropping the plugin-ui:auth\nport allocation that pre-regression allocateServices granted outside the\n!mirror check. With no port, the planner''s patchedUi left the mirror''s\nui.url empty and the host advertised the auth remote as a relative\n/remoteEntry.js — the browser could never load the auth plugin UI, so\n/login never rendered (dev:ssr + dev:csr regression suites red from\n2674acc0 onward).\n\nRestore the pre-regression semantics under the block model: the mirror\nstill gets no plugin:<id> api entry, but a local mirror with a local ui\ngets its plugin-ui:<id> entry allocated, which patches\nruntimeConfig.plugins.auth.ui.url and feeds the folder-form auth\ndescriptor''s BOS_UI_PORT.\n\nAlso sanitize the regression stack log filename (regression-dev-ssr.log)\n— the mode''s colon made upload-artifact reject the whole artifacts\nupload, hiding the very logs needed to debug this.\n\nNew planInfra regression test pins the mirror ui allocation and the\npatched ui.url.\n\n* fix(everything-dev): keep harness-injected origins in config-path production starts\n\nA registry start is a real deployment — localhost CORS_ORIGIN/BASE_URL\nthere are stray dev leftovers and stay purged. An explicit --config-path\nstart (regression harness, local production stack) injects those origins\nas deployment truth; deleting them made the in-process host derive the\nauth origin as https://<domain>, so better-auth issued Secure cookies no\nhttp client could send back (empty sessions, 401s, INVALID_ORIGIN).\n\n* fix(everything-dev): purge localhost origins only on registry starts\n\nThe gate moves from !configPath to a positive isRegistryStart check:\nbare local bos start runs (no --config-path, no BOS_ACCOUNT/BOS_GATEWAY)\nload the local config and are local starts too — their origins are\ndeployment truth, not stray dev leftovers. Adds unit tests for all\nthree config-source outcomes and a changeset.\n\n* fix(dev): quittable TUI — resume raw stdin so q/Ctrl-C reach the key handler\n\nBun''s TTY stdin never enters flowing mode from a bare data listener\nattach. With the dev TUI''s raw mode on, ISIG is disabled, so Ctrl-C\ngenerated no SIGINT, and the \\x03/q bytes never arrived either — the\nsession was unquittable from its own terminal (bos kill from a second\nterminal was the only exit). The renderer now resumes stdin after\nenabling raw mode; unmount pauses it.\n\nQuit-path cleanup in the same sweep:\n- devApp''s SIGINT/SIGTERM handler now delegates to the same\n  requestShutdownEscalating the TUI uses (the two bodies had drifted\n  into twins); signal counting lives in one place\n- emergencyKill reuses reapGroup instead of re-implementing the\n  group-kill fallback\n- suspendForceExitTimer renamed rearmForceExitTimer — it extends the\n  deadline, it does not suspend it\n- l (export logs) no longer counts toward the quit escalation, so\n  l-then-q quits gracefully instead of force-exiting past the export\n- force-exit timer is unref''d on both paths\n\nRegression coverage: the framework suite gains a pty harness\n(creack/pty) and two tests that boot a fully interactive stack, wait\nfor the TUI''s alt-screen mount, then quit via q and via the raw Ctrl-C\nbyte — asserting the CLI exits 0, every service child and watcher\ngrandchild dies, ports free, and the registry cleans up. Both failed\n(red) before the resume fix; both pass after.\n\n* fix(everything-dev): drop the SERVICE_CONFIGS annotation duplicated by the satisfies check\n\nThe rebase merge of main (post-#179) kept BOTH the Record<string,\nPick<...>> annotation and the branch''s trailing `as const satisfies`.\nThe annotation widens the const back to Record, so under\nnoUncheckedIndexedAccess (plugins/apps tsconfig) every dot access\nyields Pick | undefined and the descriptor spreads became optional —\ntypecheck failed on the auth descriptor. Keep only the satisfies form:\nsame contract enforcement, literal keys stay required.\n\n* feat(dev): surface folder-form plugin UIs in the TUI — auth row shows its ui port\n\nFolder-form plugin UIs (ui/ dir inside the plugin workspace, no own\npackage.json) run as a child of the plugin''s dev process via\nBOS_UI_PORT — no plugin-ui:<id> service is spawned, so the one-row-per-\nplugin renderer had nothing to merge and the port was invisible unless\nyou tailed the log stream ([auth] ├─ 🎨 UI: http://localhost:3011).\n\nServiceDescriptor now carries uiPort next to the BOS_UI_PORT env in\nboth folder-form branches (regular plugin + auth mirror);\ngetProcessStates threads it into the process state; mergePluginUiRows\nsynthesizes the same inline annotation package-form companions get.\nThe auth row now reads: AUTH (local) running :3002 · ui :3011.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtqpCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMb0QAF769rgBhHhRtInW8kXADi7Y\nIL1WzFS0GgD2RKJ2Dy1NLTLCURliyoW1uzwJR1/PnOMxxSswc5h/fsSCjK6xq2ZP\ntQPFOSk4eIs2WzR8M1FVY1WiQt9W06EUOiQvVJSS0lUeTwkukhKeFA7JvYsn2wCo\nnFe8qDRLMFyNxHCpOkCOLI5WokYzKHjkXUoDPlvumgUuryi6XTU69ZlxRnc5DxFl\n9h6Oq6VKaEOq6Tb9bs5qSqtBWQWJmITgqZgOvWtNwsvlRJzsk3Um016CFVa3qAHT\n7yGnJmTkfW7+UEITU0Jrj6tPJyRhIsjWqZsoMOon3OnHwwweJhOJGM6a3PIl3Lsn\nSvBRN7foCPYCr5cMdBcp1U9MrllPPPcpg1zZwipP8NEopM/m2ke25jgzsqYCFj3U\npuU5p97kxDnoxnFVwXZbO9tSEmv6Pcd61w1J+y4sc02NGbpVWK5Pa+Nv04akLJ7d\nlWCruPFOlvOa1+6hsMgt6FmwS59P4OGdwnfbtM4fvFcwPzca//3KyqfItpxr8R5t\n2ZDvgeWhAWSGTli4UbTTiKtvYDTZaYJjapGfxy70SHdHQPY+dTDT6fGslZbQxZRd\nPHIGKlDPsBaHWfda/jOv7SJUbRzzuT8VyjgOlDb+OLMJlO0AuXdbW7xDBNpmOYSR\nbTzGDwpZH20q7jIEeICu\n=QQuG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T17:07:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/d6c0e26c04e150c5c1852a0fa06397696a8eb83a","node_id":"C_kwDOT-K1MdoAKGQ2YzBlMjZjMDRlMTUwYzVjMTg1MmEwZmEwNjM5NzY5NmE4ZWI4M2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/e5482b864841270563a8be19e6541be855873b0e","sha":"e5482b864841270563a8be19e6541be855873b0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/e5482b864841270563a8be19e6541be855873b0e"}],"sha":"d6c0e26c04e150c5c1852a0fa06397696a8eb83a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/d6c0e26c04e150c5c1852a0fa06397696a8eb83a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/e5482b864841270563a8be19e6541be855873b0e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:12:25Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:12:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(everything-dev): allow env in SERVICE_CONFIGS type (#179)\n\n* fix(everything-dev): allow env in SERVICE_CONFIGS type\n\n9cfdc4599 added env: { NODE_OPTIONS } to the host SERVICE_CONFIGS entry\nbut the Record<Pick<ServiceDescriptor, ...>> annotation still excludes\nenv. No typecheck currently compiles this file (bos typecheck checks\nhost/ui/api/plugins, which resolve everything-dev sources only when\nimported — and service-descriptor is reachable only from app.ts /\norchestrator.ts / dev-program.ts, none of which are in those tsconfigs''\ngraphs), so the mismatch is latent. It surfaced when PR #163''s dag.ts\nstarted importing isAuthMirrorPluginEntry.\n\nType-only fix; no runtime change.\n\n* fix(everything-dev): clear latent tsc errors in the package sources\n\npackages/everything-dev is not in bos typecheck''s workspace list, so\nthese only surface when the sources are compiled directly:\n\n- plugin.ts: publish input no longer carries cdn (Zephyr sunset) —\n  drop the dead passthrough; publishToFastKv never read it\n- descriptor/resolve.ts: toConfigInput picked a deploy field the\n  descriptor schema no longer has\n- orchestrator.ts: fieldless TaggedErrors used Record<string, never> as\n  props — its string index signature (never) conflicted with the\n  inherited message getter; Record<never, never> carries no fields and\n  the construction sites drop the empty args\n- dev-program.ts: pass only the BOS_ACCOUNT/BOS_GATEWAY pair that\n  resolveStartConfigSource reads; ProcessEnv trips weak-type detection\n- build.ts: buildEverythingDevQuietly returns a did-build boolean,\n  widen the task array to Promise<unknown>\n\nNo runtime behavior change; verified tsc --noEmit clean in\npackages/everything-dev plus full typecheck, lint, and test suites.","tree":{"sha":"a1f3a38ab4dc27603ac24059d2ef459e7461a47f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/trees/a1f3a38ab4dc27603ac24059d2ef459e7461a47f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/commits/e5482b864841270563a8be19e6541be855873b0e","verification":{"payload":"tree a1f3a38ab4dc27603ac24059d2ef459e7461a47f\nparent e682bc04dbd51ccaba64bcd43962e238061bc328\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1790352745 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790352745 -0500\n\nfix(everything-dev): allow env in SERVICE_CONFIGS type (#179)\n\n* fix(everything-dev): allow env in SERVICE_CONFIGS type\n\n9cfdc4599 added env: { NODE_OPTIONS } to the host SERVICE_CONFIGS entry\nbut the Record<Pick<ServiceDescriptor, ...>> annotation still excludes\nenv. No typecheck currently compiles this file (bos typecheck checks\nhost/ui/api/plugins, which resolve everything-dev sources only when\nimported — and service-descriptor is reachable only from app.ts /\norchestrator.ts / dev-program.ts, none of which are in those tsconfigs''\ngraphs), so the mismatch is latent. It surfaced when PR #163''s dag.ts\nstarted importing isAuthMirrorPluginEntry.\n\nType-only fix; no runtime change.\n\n* fix(everything-dev): clear latent tsc errors in the package sources\n\npackages/everything-dev is not in bos typecheck''s workspace list, so\nthese only surface when the sources are compiled directly:\n\n- plugin.ts: publish input no longer carries cdn (Zephyr sunset) —\n  drop the dead passthrough; publishToFastKv never read it\n- descriptor/resolve.ts: toConfigInput picked a deploy field the\n  descriptor schema no longer has\n- orchestrator.ts: fieldless TaggedErrors used Record<string, never> as\n  props — its string index signature (never) conflicted with the\n  inherited message getter; Record<never, never> carries no fields and\n  the construction sites drop the empty args\n- dev-program.ts: pass only the BOS_ACCOUNT/BOS_GATEWAY pair that\n  resolveStartConfigSource reads; ProcessEnv trips weak-type detection\n- build.ts: buildEverythingDevQuietly returns a did-build boolean,\n  widen the task array to Promise<unknown>\n\nNo runtime behavior change; verified tsc --noEmit clean in\npackages/everything-dev plus full typecheck, lint, and test suites.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtp1pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARYcQAA4ZReDj/eSyqYnLecjelFQ6\nWbIDkAZKPcgtHH4Ak38MpMGExMbQMxJ6El1kuRVCdi503wBWmM81vxsM1xkCoH9G\nUpMFsVew0l3aPE9Jm6jaPIOUJnHFt6R2Y3aNqfAUePyI9DhF4HjndM8N7Hjuiuzf\nsWjVYlOgFByORwEG24bB/fwo/U6CL360TXXDQsSbOiaQL0ncEArD2dSUow1JgJrV\nW/UNoSqH8P17ioi3f9x2Ry/ibVNKgiGdToFTAYDwfYGDarn115Ri81nWUb72GHkM\nkZ6hxrppP4D8N8xZcBJlDYDcKA0xCZYO0guVCP37lxa5sUFRAC1NHaHdTaHpNReK\nq9ymRhRTiVzhDD1cueu55q1DvdwdrM/r41LN/Q+FE5jFbcSzm1XE5fZH5sIuRBii\nN4nOJNazhstJiyQFcE7CFnKPMyZMQ0mHI2xg1xXxP3QUyXf5lTWgeD8iPVruWiXe\nNQn2k67zqlLnAwY+xaOKvqt3Qz42O4AuFpSlMfXOqtYBszQk2yIP/sDg574iojGx\nVASqdzIA4WrLKijm80tZm9kwVg6sLsXOm3FRzN1oIZLqaL/FUCfN075d7NZf22Q6\n9J9YgEVVPCXt9NPIp32AuFi2V96yOrh67jINhv9C6sDYkwjUMTGykxQQ9U1gTq4o\njY884oiELMAAi/afVFB2\n=HQxI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T16:12:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/e5482b864841270563a8be19e6541be855873b0e","node_id":"C_kwDOT-K1MdoAKGU1NDgyYjg2NDg0MTI3MDU2M2E4YmUxOWU2NTQxYmU4NTU4NzNiMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commit/e682bc04dbd51ccaba64bcd43962e238061bc328","sha":"e682bc04dbd51ccaba64bcd43962e238061bc328","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/e682bc04dbd51ccaba64bcd43962e238061bc328"}],"sha":"e5482b864841270563a8be19e6541be855873b0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/e5482b864841270563a8be19e6541be855873b0e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/e682bc04dbd51ccaba64bcd43962e238061bc328/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T01:12:05Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T01:12:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Session single read path + session gas keys (NEP-611) as the primary gasless write path (#178)\n\n* fix(auth): single authoritative session read path — post-sign-in redirect loop\n\nAll session reads (route guards, the login route''s beforeLoad, useQuery\nobservers, the post-sign-in refresh) share one queryFn that always calls\ngetSession with disableCookieCache, so every redirect decision sees the same\nanswer and the login <-> dashboard ping-pong (\"Too many redirects\") is\nstructurally impossible. The post-sign-in refresh overrides staleness so a\nfresh signed-out cache entry cannot short-circuit it.\n\nRemoves the login page''s component-level Navigate, loader prefetch, the dead\nrejectAuthed guard, the bootstrap WeakSet bookkeeping, and the initialData\nthreading across call sites. Disables the server-side session cookie cache\noutright (was prod-only, delayed revocation/ban visibility). sanitizeRedirect\nnow rejects /login targets.\n\nRegression tests: unit tests for the refresh-override and guard pass-through\nchain; browser spec asserts every get-session call bypasses the cookie cache.\n\n* fix(test): sanitize regression stack log names + scope browser session assertion\n\nstart-stack.mjs wrote .bos/logs/regression-dev:ssr.log with the raw mode\nstring; the colon is legal on disk but fails actions/upload-artifact\n(invalid character), so every failing dev:* browser leg also lost its\nartifacts. The dev-logs timestamp sanitizer (dev-logs.ts) already\nestablished the dash convention — mirror it here.\n\nThe auth-redirect spec asserted every /get-session request carries\ndisableCookieCache, but better-auth''s internal session atom (subscribed\nvia useNearAccountId) legitimately fetches without query params — the\nassertion failed in all four browser matrix jobs even though the\nredirect-loop fix itself was green. Replace it with the real server-side\ninvariant: no response may set the better-auth session_data cache cookie\n(it only exists when session.cookieCache is enabled).\n\n* feat(auth): swap wallet connector to @fastnear/near-connect 0.14.1 + near-kit 0.20.2\n\nTicket 01 of session-gas-keys (.scratch/session-gas-keys/SPEC.md, ADR 0012):\nthe fastnear fork of the connector lineage can express gas-key actions\n(AddKey gasKeyInfo, TransferToGasKey, WithdrawFromGasKey) and the\nfeatures.gasKeys manifest flag that @hot-labs 0.11.4 lacks; near-kit moves\n^0.19.0 -> ^0.20.2 (no breaking changes; gas-key support already present).\n\nTracked patch (patches/) restores cspNonce threading the fork dropped —\nproduction strict CSP blocks sandbox-wallet executor iframes without it.\nPasskey manifest declares addFunctionCallKey/gasKeys unsupported (refused,\nnot crash). No behavior change on existing flows: typecheck 9/9, unit suites\n(better-near-auth 104, ui 375, api 122, host 207) and dev:ssr browser\nregression (7/7, incl. CSP spec) green.\n\n* feat(auth): session gas key bootstrap + sponsor funding lifecycle\n\nTicket 02 of session-gas-keys (.scratch/session-gas-keys/SPEC.md, ADR 0012).\n\nServer (siwn plugin):\n- POST /near/gas-key/fund — session-gated Sponsor funding: verifies on-chain\n  that the key exists, is GasKeyFunctionCall, and matches the configured scope;\n  refuses when the on-chain balance is at/above the top-up threshold; enforces\n  a per-user lifetime cap over recorded fundings; signs TransferToGasKey from\n  the ephemeral relayer account (receiver = user account via a contained\n  builder-receiver shim) and records a fundedGasKey row\n- POST /near/gas-key/info — balance/lanes/scope at finality + cap remaining\n- GET /near/gas-key/scope — the configured scope for the session network\n- sessionGasKey config (flat or dual-network, like relayer) with defaults:\n  0.05 NEAR top-ups, 0.01 threshold, 0.2 NEAR per-user cap, 4 lanes,\n  __fastdata_kv methods; threaded through plugins/auth config schemas and\n  bos.config.json (FastKV namespace receivers)\n\nClient (better-near-auth):\n- gas-key-store: IndexedDB persistence per network:account (no key material\n  server-side); gas-key-client: gasKeyState atom, wallet features gate,\n  round-robin lane selection\n- authClient.near gains addSessionGasKey (wallet-signed AddKey with\n  gasKeyInfo via the connector directly, refusing wallets without\n  features.gasKeys), sendWithGasKey (wallet-less near-kit local signing on\n  rotating lanes), refreshGasKeyInfo, ensureGasKeyFunded, getGasKeyScope\n\nTests: 19 new (10 route guardrails incl. cap/threshold/scope/session gating;\n9 client: bootstrap refusal + addKey shape, threshold-triggered funding,\nlane rotation, no-key refusal). Typecheck 9/9, lint clean, ui/api/host\nsuites unchanged and green. Manual testnet E2E (Meteor) remains as the\nticket''s human verification step.\n\n* feat(ui): app metadata publish prefers the session gas key\n\nTicket 03 of session-gas-keys: publishing app metadata routes through the\nSession Gas Key when one is Bootstrapped and funded — the browser signs the\nFastKV write locally on a rotating Lane (no relayer, no wallet popup), the\nkey''s balance line shows under the actions and refreshes after sends, and the\nhook opportunistically tops the key up via the Sponsor when the balance dips\nbelow the threshold. Without a funded key the existing delegate + relayer\npath runs unchanged.\n\n- better-near-auth/react gains useGasKeyState; sendWithGasKey now accepts\n  prepared gas strings (yocto-gas digits or Tgas) validated through parseGas\n  (resolveGasUnits)\n- useSessionGasKey hook (ui/src/lib) composes the atom, refresh, and\n  threshold-triggered funding\n- editor: gas-first publish with delegate+relay fallback; balance display\n  (metadata-gas-key-balance testid); toast notes the session-gas-key path\n- component tests exercise the client action seam: gas-first publish\n  (sign/relay untouched), fallback preserved, balance hidden + no funding\n  without a key; near-kit mock gains parseGas for the gas-string test\n\nTypecheck 9/9, lint clean, better-near-auth 124 + ui 378 + api 122 + host 207\ngreen, dev:ssr browser regression 7/7. Manual testnet E2E (Meteor) remains\nthe ticket''s human verification step.\n\n* feat(ui): tenant publish prefers the session gas key + opt-in affordance\n\nTicket 04 of session-gas-keys: platform-owner tenant config publish routes\nthrough the Session Gas Key when one is Bootstrapped and funded (same\nordering as the metadata editor: gas key -> delegate + relayer -> direct\nwallet); DAO/Trezu mode short-circuits before the gas-key check and stays\nuntouched, as do the veNEAR PoC flows.\n\n- tenant-deploy: refreshes the key''s on-chain state at publish time and sends\n  locally via sendWithGasKey when funded; readiness rule shared with the\n  metadata editor hook (hasFundedGasKey)\n- EnableGaslessWrites affordance on the tenant detail page for platform\n  owners: ''Enable gasless writes'' for features.gasKeys wallets (Bootstrap +\n  Sponsor top-up), ready status once bootstrapped, plain-language refusal for\n  non-gasKeys wallets, nothing while unconfigured or while the capability\n  check is pending; cap exhaustion warns once and names the relayer fallback\n- better-near-auth client gains isGasKeyWalletSupported (connected wallet\n  manifest gate, false when unavailable)\n- tests: gas-first vs relayer ordering at the publish seam (relayer untouched\n  on the gas path, delegate+relay on the unfunded path), affordance states\n  (opt-in, ready, refusal, unconfigured, pending capability, cap warning)\n\nTypecheck 9/9, lint clean, better-near-auth 124 + ui 386 green, dev:ssr\nbrowser regression 7/7. Manual testnet E2E (Meteor, second-device cap) remains\nthe ticket''s human verification step.\n\n* refactor(auth): remove legacy sub-account FCAK config — session gas keys are the only key sponsorship\n\nTicket 05 of session-gas-keys (.scratch/session-gas-keys/SPEC.md, ADR 0012).\n\nRemoved end to end: SubAccountConfig.addRelayerFCAK / relayerFCAK and the\nrelayer-FCAK addKey block in sub-account creation; the\nNEAR_SUB_ACCOUNT_PARENT_KEY_* secrets from plugins/auth''s secret schema,\nbos.config.json + bos.citynode.app.ts secret declarations, plugin.dev.ts,\n.env.example, and the README secrets table; the secrets passthrough from\nbuildSiwnOptions. The parent-key field in the generated siwn config is gone\n(plugins/auth no longer wires it); sub-account creation still works with an\nexplicit relayer whose account is the parent, or a parent key passed directly\nvia siwn({ secrets: { parentKey } }) on the server — that option is kept and\nstill tested in better-near-auth.\n\nDocs: AGENTS.md relayer section rewritten to the session-gas-keys-first model\n(Sponsor''s dual role, Bootstrap/TransferToGasKey/lanes, drain-before-delete\nand no-delegate protocol rules, the @fastnear/near-connect connector),\nreferencing ADR 0012 and the CONTEXT.md gasless-transactions vocabulary;\nFCAK references removed from the better-near-auth auth-plugin/subaccount\nskills and everything-dev publish-sync skill; auth-export.ts now re-exports\nthe siwn config types from auth-config.ts instead of duplicating them (the\ncopies had already drifted).\n\nChangeset covers the sprint''s user-facing surface. Typecheck 9/9, lint\nclean, better-near-auth 124 + ui 386 + api 122 + host 207 + plugins/auth 243\ngreen.\n\n* fix(auth): bundle @fastnear/near-connect into the published client\n\nCode-review finding on PR #178: the tsdown alwaysBundle regex still pointed\nat @hot-labs/near-connect after the connector swap, so the published\ndist/client.js no longer inlined the connector and npm consumers would hit\nan unresolvable import (invisible locally, where the development condition\nresolves from src). Point alwaysBundle at @fastnear/near-connect and verify\nthe built bundle carries the connector code with no bare import.\n\n* fix: review follow-ups — agnostic framework golden test, failure-aware gas fallback, fund serialization\n\nPR #178 review findings:\n\n- Framework test made agnostic: the descriptor golden test in\n  packages/everything-dev carried citynode fixtures (citynodeApp import +\n  live bos.config.json comparison). It now builds a generic child-app\n  fixture with the descriptor constructors (no citynode references, no live\n  config read) and asserts the flatten/inheritance/canonicalization\n  machinery. The citynode-specific mirror of the authored config moved into\n  bos.citynode.app.ts itself (sessionGasKey added there, fixing the golden\n  mismatch the sessionGasKey config addition caused).\n- Failure-aware fallback: trySendWithGasKey (ui/src/lib/gas-key.ts) returns\n  null when no funded key OR when the gas-key send fails mid-flight, so\n  delegate + relayer engages — both publish surfaces (metadata editor,\n  tenant config) and covered by new mid-flight failure tests.\n- Fund-route cap race: per-user (userId:network) in-flight lock serializes\n  the verify->cap->sign->record section; concurrent requests no longer both\n  pass the cap. Multi-instance deployments stay bounded by the cap itself.\n- refreshGasKeyInfo distinguishes no-key (null) from RPC failure (throws);\n  404 clears the stale atom so a deleted key demotes to the relayer instead\n  of a silent error loop.\n- EnableGaslessWrites ready status shows the balance amount.\n- Second-device cap sharing: route test funds two different keys for the\n  same user and asserts the shared cap trips with the cap-exceeded message.\n- Cleanups: hasFundedGasKey moved from the react-hook file to the pure lib\n  module; toYocto now returns bigint (folds the parseAmount cast + BigInt\n  conversions); the dual flat/dual config parse logic deduplicated into\n  parseDualNetworkConfig; review-flagged comments removed from\n  everything-dev ui/auth, auth-instance, session-cache, auth-guards, and\n  better-near-auth index.\n\nTypecheck 9/9, lint clean; better-near-auth 125, ui 388, api 122, host 207,\nplugins/auth 243, everything-dev 515 green; dev:ssr browser regression 7/7.\n\n* merge origin/main: session read path + tenant spawn land, comment-free resolution\n\nPR #175 (the session single-read-path fix, identical work to this branch''s\ne7aa4b230) and #176 (user-owned tenant spawn, localhost passkey rpID) merged\nfrom main. The three conflicts were this branch''s comment-removals in the\nsession-read-path files vs main''s commented versions — resolved to the\ncomment-free side per the repo''s no-comments standard.\n\nAlso: the passkey rpID unit test on main was stale against #176''s localhost\nskip (an invalid custom rpID no longer throws on localhost dev origins) —\nit now asserts the throw on a production origin and the localhost skip\nseparately. The remaining plugins/auth integration timeout is the known\nload flake (passes in isolation).\n\n* fix(cli): strip patchedDependencies from scaffolded child package.json\n\nbos init scaffolding from a source dir copies the parent''s root\npackage.json verbatim; since the repo added patchedDependencies (the\n@fastnear/near-connect cspNonce patch), the copied child declared a patch\nwhose file is never copied — bun install fails instantly with a missing\npatch file (CI Framework tests / init.full). Child projects consume\nbetter-near-auth from npm with the connector already bundled into its dist,\nso the parent''s build-time patch must not propagate. Verified with\nCI=true init.full: fails without the strip, passes with it.","tree":{"sha":"aa0d5e57ed0b21e2123675a3def240a01b7748d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/trees/aa0d5e57ed0b21e2123675a3def240a01b7748d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/commits/e682bc04dbd51ccaba64bcd43962e238061bc328","verification":{"payload":"tree aa0d5e57ed0b21e2123675a3def240a01b7748d7\nparent 5ec019adb8aa4f32132e6c7100084dbbe5906f43\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1790298725 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790298725 -0500\n\nSession single read path + session gas keys (NEP-611) as the primary gasless write path (#178)\n\n* fix(auth): single authoritative session read path — post-sign-in redirect loop\n\nAll session reads (route guards, the login route''s beforeLoad, useQuery\nobservers, the post-sign-in refresh) share one queryFn that always calls\ngetSession with disableCookieCache, so every redirect decision sees the same\nanswer and the login <-> dashboard ping-pong (\"Too many redirects\") is\nstructurally impossible. The post-sign-in refresh overrides staleness so a\nfresh signed-out cache entry cannot short-circuit it.\n\nRemoves the login page''s component-level Navigate, loader prefetch, the dead\nrejectAuthed guard, the bootstrap WeakSet bookkeeping, and the initialData\nthreading across call sites. Disables the server-side session cookie cache\noutright (was prod-only, delayed revocation/ban visibility). sanitizeRedirect\nnow rejects /login targets.\n\nRegression tests: unit tests for the refresh-override and guard pass-through\nchain; browser spec asserts every get-session call bypasses the cookie cache.\n\n* fix(test): sanitize regression stack log names + scope browser session assertion\n\nstart-stack.mjs wrote .bos/logs/regression-dev:ssr.log with the raw mode\nstring; the colon is legal on disk but fails actions/upload-artifact\n(invalid character), so every failing dev:* browser leg also lost its\nartifacts. The dev-logs timestamp sanitizer (dev-logs.ts) already\nestablished the dash convention — mirror it here.\n\nThe auth-redirect spec asserted every /get-session request carries\ndisableCookieCache, but better-auth''s internal session atom (subscribed\nvia useNearAccountId) legitimately fetches without query params — the\nassertion failed in all four browser matrix jobs even though the\nredirect-loop fix itself was green. Replace it with the real server-side\ninvariant: no response may set the better-auth session_data cache cookie\n(it only exists when session.cookieCache is enabled).\n\n* feat(auth): swap wallet connector to @fastnear/near-connect 0.14.1 + near-kit 0.20.2\n\nTicket 01 of session-gas-keys (.scratch/session-gas-keys/SPEC.md, ADR 0012):\nthe fastnear fork of the connector lineage can express gas-key actions\n(AddKey gasKeyInfo, TransferToGasKey, WithdrawFromGasKey) and the\nfeatures.gasKeys manifest flag that @hot-labs 0.11.4 lacks; near-kit moves\n^0.19.0 -> ^0.20.2 (no breaking changes; gas-key support already present).\n\nTracked patch (patches/) restores cspNonce threading the fork dropped —\nproduction strict CSP blocks sandbox-wallet executor iframes without it.\nPasskey manifest declares addFunctionCallKey/gasKeys unsupported (refused,\nnot crash). No behavior change on existing flows: typecheck 9/9, unit suites\n(better-near-auth 104, ui 375, api 122, host 207) and dev:ssr browser\nregression (7/7, incl. CSP spec) green.\n\n* feat(auth): session gas key bootstrap + sponsor funding lifecycle\n\nTicket 02 of session-gas-keys (.scratch/session-gas-keys/SPEC.md, ADR 0012).\n\nServer (siwn plugin):\n- POST /near/gas-key/fund — session-gated Sponsor funding: verifies on-chain\n  that the key exists, is GasKeyFunctionCall, and matches the configured scope;\n  refuses when the on-chain balance is at/above the top-up threshold; enforces\n  a per-user lifetime cap over recorded fundings; signs TransferToGasKey from\n  the ephemeral relayer account (receiver = user account via a contained\n  builder-receiver shim) and records a fundedGasKey row\n- POST /near/gas-key/info — balance/lanes/scope at finality + cap remaining\n- GET /near/gas-key/scope — the configured scope for the session network\n- sessionGasKey config (flat or dual-network, like relayer) with defaults:\n  0.05 NEAR top-ups, 0.01 threshold, 0.2 NEAR per-user cap, 4 lanes,\n  __fastdata_kv methods; threaded through plugins/auth config schemas and\n  bos.config.json (FastKV namespace receivers)\n\nClient (better-near-auth):\n- gas-key-store: IndexedDB persistence per network:account (no key material\n  server-side); gas-key-client: gasKeyState atom, wallet features gate,\n  round-robin lane selection\n- authClient.near gains addSessionGasKey (wallet-signed AddKey with\n  gasKeyInfo via the connector directly, refusing wallets without\n  features.gasKeys), sendWithGasKey (wallet-less near-kit local signing on\n  rotating lanes), refreshGasKeyInfo, ensureGasKeyFunded, getGasKeyScope\n\nTests: 19 new (10 route guardrails incl. cap/threshold/scope/session gating;\n9 client: bootstrap refusal + addKey shape, threshold-triggered funding,\nlane rotation, no-key refusal). Typecheck 9/9, lint clean, ui/api/host\nsuites unchanged and green. Manual testnet E2E (Meteor) remains as the\nticket''s human verification step.\n\n* feat(ui): app metadata publish prefers the session gas key\n\nTicket 03 of session-gas-keys: publishing app metadata routes through the\nSession Gas Key when one is Bootstrapped and funded — the browser signs the\nFastKV write locally on a rotating Lane (no relayer, no wallet popup), the\nkey''s balance line shows under the actions and refreshes after sends, and the\nhook opportunistically tops the key up via the Sponsor when the balance dips\nbelow the threshold. Without a funded key the existing delegate + relayer\npath runs unchanged.\n\n- better-near-auth/react gains useGasKeyState; sendWithGasKey now accepts\n  prepared gas strings (yocto-gas digits or Tgas) validated through parseGas\n  (resolveGasUnits)\n- useSessionGasKey hook (ui/src/lib) composes the atom, refresh, and\n  threshold-triggered funding\n- editor: gas-first publish with delegate+relay fallback; balance display\n  (metadata-gas-key-balance testid); toast notes the session-gas-key path\n- component tests exercise the client action seam: gas-first publish\n  (sign/relay untouched), fallback preserved, balance hidden + no funding\n  without a key; near-kit mock gains parseGas for the gas-string test\n\nTypecheck 9/9, lint clean, better-near-auth 124 + ui 378 + api 122 + host 207\ngreen, dev:ssr browser regression 7/7. Manual testnet E2E (Meteor) remains\nthe ticket''s human verification step.\n\n* feat(ui): tenant publish prefers the session gas key + opt-in affordance\n\nTicket 04 of session-gas-keys: platform-owner tenant config publish routes\nthrough the Session Gas Key when one is Bootstrapped and funded (same\nordering as the metadata editor: gas key -> delegate + relayer -> direct\nwallet); DAO/Trezu mode short-circuits before the gas-key check and stays\nuntouched, as do the veNEAR PoC flows.\n\n- tenant-deploy: refreshes the key''s on-chain state at publish time and sends\n  locally via sendWithGasKey when funded; readiness rule shared with the\n  metadata editor hook (hasFundedGasKey)\n- EnableGaslessWrites affordance on the tenant detail page for platform\n  owners: ''Enable gasless writes'' for features.gasKeys wallets (Bootstrap +\n  Sponsor top-up), ready status once bootstrapped, plain-language refusal for\n  non-gasKeys wallets, nothing while unconfigured or while the capability\n  check is pending; cap exhaustion warns once and names the relayer fallback\n- better-near-auth client gains isGasKeyWalletSupported (connected wallet\n  manifest gate, false when unavailable)\n- tests: gas-first vs relayer ordering at the publish seam (relayer untouched\n  on the gas path, delegate+relay on the unfunded path), affordance states\n  (opt-in, ready, refusal, unconfigured, pending capability, cap warning)\n\nTypecheck 9/9, lint clean, better-near-auth 124 + ui 386 green, dev:ssr\nbrowser regression 7/7. Manual testnet E2E (Meteor, second-device cap) remains\nthe ticket''s human verification step.\n\n* refactor(auth): remove legacy sub-account FCAK config — session gas keys are the only key sponsorship\n\nTicket 05 of session-gas-keys (.scratch/session-gas-keys/SPEC.md, ADR 0012).\n\nRemoved end to end: SubAccountConfig.addRelayerFCAK / relayerFCAK and the\nrelayer-FCAK addKey block in sub-account creation; the\nNEAR_SUB_ACCOUNT_PARENT_KEY_* secrets from plugins/auth''s secret schema,\nbos.config.json + bos.citynode.app.ts secret declarations, plugin.dev.ts,\n.env.example, and the README secrets table; the secrets passthrough from\nbuildSiwnOptions. The parent-key field in the generated siwn config is gone\n(plugins/auth no longer wires it); sub-account creation still works with an\nexplicit relayer whose account is the parent, or a parent key passed directly\nvia siwn({ secrets: { parentKey } }) on the server — that option is kept and\nstill tested in better-near-auth.\n\nDocs: AGENTS.md relayer section rewritten to the session-gas-keys-first model\n(Sponsor''s dual role, Bootstrap/TransferToGasKey/lanes, drain-before-delete\nand no-delegate protocol rules, the @fastnear/near-connect connector),\nreferencing ADR 0012 and the CONTEXT.md gasless-transactions vocabulary;\nFCAK references removed from the better-near-auth auth-plugin/subaccount\nskills and everything-dev publish-sync skill; auth-export.ts now re-exports\nthe siwn config types from auth-config.ts instead of duplicating them (the\ncopies had already drifted).\n\nChangeset covers the sprint''s user-facing surface. Typecheck 9/9, lint\nclean, better-near-auth 124 + ui 386 + api 122 + host 207 + plugins/auth 243\ngreen.\n\n* fix(auth): bundle @fastnear/near-connect into the published client\n\nCode-review finding on PR #178: the tsdown alwaysBundle regex still pointed\nat @hot-labs/near-connect after the connector swap, so the published\ndist/client.js no longer inlined the connector and npm consumers would hit\nan unresolvable import (invisible locally, where the development condition\nresolves from src). Point alwaysBundle at @fastnear/near-connect and verify\nthe built bundle carries the connector code with no bare import.\n\n* fix: review follow-ups — agnostic framework golden test, failure-aware gas fallback, fund serialization\n\nPR #178 review findings:\n\n- Framework test made agnostic: the descriptor golden test in\n  packages/everything-dev carried citynode fixtures (citynodeApp import +\n  live bos.config.json comparison). It now builds a generic child-app\n  fixture with the descriptor constructors (no citynode references, no live\n  config read) and asserts the flatten/inheritance/canonicalization\n  machinery. The citynode-specific mirror of the authored config moved into\n  bos.citynode.app.ts itself (sessionGasKey added there, fixing the golden\n  mismatch the sessionGasKey config addition caused).\n- Failure-aware fallback: trySendWithGasKey (ui/src/lib/gas-key.ts) returns\n  null when no funded key OR when the gas-key send fails mid-flight, so\n  delegate + relayer engages — both publish surfaces (metadata editor,\n  tenant config) and covered by new mid-flight failure tests.\n- Fund-route cap race: per-user (userId:network) in-flight lock serializes\n  the verify->cap->sign->record section; concurrent requests no longer both\n  pass the cap. Multi-instance deployments stay bounded by the cap itself.\n- refreshGasKeyInfo distinguishes no-key (null) from RPC failure (throws);\n  404 clears the stale atom so a deleted key demotes to the relayer instead\n  of a silent error loop.\n- EnableGaslessWrites ready status shows the balance amount.\n- Second-device cap sharing: route test funds two different keys for the\n  same user and asserts the shared cap trips with the cap-exceeded message.\n- Cleanups: hasFundedGasKey moved from the react-hook file to the pure lib\n  module; toYocto now returns bigint (folds the parseAmount cast + BigInt\n  conversions); the dual flat/dual config parse logic deduplicated into\n  parseDualNetworkConfig; review-flagged comments removed from\n  everything-dev ui/auth, auth-instance, session-cache, auth-guards, and\n  better-near-auth index.\n\nTypecheck 9/9, lint clean; better-near-auth 125, ui 388, api 122, host 207,\nplugins/auth 243, everything-dev 515 green; dev:ssr browser regression 7/7.\n\n* merge origin/main: session read path + tenant spawn land, comment-free resolution\n\nPR #175 (the session single-read-path fix, identical work to this branch''s\ne7aa4b230) and #176 (user-owned tenant spawn, localhost passkey rpID) merged\nfrom main. The three conflicts were this branch''s comment-removals in the\nsession-read-path files vs main''s commented versions — resolved to the\ncomment-free side per the repo''s no-comments standard.\n\nAlso: the passkey rpID unit test on main was stale against #176''s localhost\nskip (an invalid custom rpID no longer throws on localhost dev origins) —\nit now asserts the throw on a production origin and the localhost skip\nseparately. The remaining plugins/auth integration timeout is the known\nload flake (passes in isolation).\n\n* fix(cli): strip patchedDependencies from scaffolded child package.json\n\nbos init scaffolding from a source dir copies the parent''s root\npackage.json verbatim; since the repo added patchedDependencies (the\n@fastnear/near-connect cspNonce patch), the copied child declared a patch\nwhose file is never copied — bun install fails instantly with a missing\npatch file (CI Framework tests / init.full). Child projects consume\nbetter-near-auth from npm with the connector already bundled into its dist,\nso the parent''s build-time patch must not propagate. Verified with\nCI=true init.full: fails without the strip, passes with it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtcplCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcHoQAGfZoq0Wr/ib7cgQLRKREL3C\nacV9kvzC5700C3WRzc8/eKdTfmrRfsuTOgpcx7GTDp3xXTKJPA8PyL6Zm8DtmhuL\nZO3swLlLM1Md9BGY5c8RBj7gL4suw5omnD6PLsYSpVmMdFQKAC1opuJvhk1ShooL\neooZa4v8YwfJrKGCd7mcRu+4Ca+RQ8gahTM4x+kp6oe4KVo3Rono/LG067/zr0tX\n7/QH7pyN4CHjiRUQfV9c3TmrfXaqHdnHvp2os1+ENwutEhFseJgPTeyQ2/iBAorQ\n79fpTWw57x5+U36n1TVj4ji8vWNX8I5Ne6A7jHaJFEQfta6NMFhvica0Q71Iz3NN\nQCn0mbbfHz9fwi0BSmPSsoG3RxrikV2xVsuI4Eh8cra5QuDuSnIYEWowZH19l+XC\nI5FI7FHHmC+ch4H47nHO2/+IQfCXavP7ax2lGHJTdqM1mtKwjEKw/XHpsSI7QxvQ\ni8KpNZZO8vHY994D1advxMy59jv5xp5v5I4C2xIRO+61RFTXA/Ua/cmKS0bH0fWk\nLwQUGhBTmtMNbt/KWXDvI6o3XH2ohDPiGvionttkYRj6GqwvHsm0gHDk6PrHsbWL\nhTAlUcLGE1ttGOuxBhne1Jye7Pz/CvGRsa7KEeTdCd8fVOdipwHcvXQZZz8R4d