"events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/commits/a1e1cba8c34cff6ee17627a66ec2077beef8ef13/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T21:21:22Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T21:21:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(auth): single authoritative session read path — post-sign-in redirect loop (#175)\n\n* fix(auth): single authoritative session read path — post-sign-in redirect loop\n\nAll session reads (route guards, the login route''s beforeLoad, useQuery\nobservers, the post-sign-in refresh) share one queryFn that always calls\ngetSession with disableCookieCache, so every redirect decision sees the same\nanswer and the login <-> dashboard ping-pong (\"Too many redirects\") is\nstructurally impossible. The post-sign-in refresh overrides staleness so a\nfresh signed-out cache entry cannot short-circuit it.\n\nRemoves the login page''s component-level Navigate, loader prefetch, the dead\nrejectAuthed guard, the bootstrap WeakSet bookkeeping, and the initialData\nthreading across call sites. Disables the server-side session cookie cache\noutright (was prod-only, delayed revocation/ban visibility). sanitizeRedirect\nnow rejects /login targets.\n\nRegression tests: unit tests for the refresh-override and guard pass-through\nchain; browser spec asserts every get-session call bypasses the cookie cache.\n\n* fix(test): sanitize regression stack log names + scope browser session assertion\n\nstart-stack.mjs wrote .bos/logs/regression-dev:ssr.log with the raw mode\nstring; the colon is legal on disk but fails actions/upload-artifact\n(invalid character), so every failing dev:* browser leg also lost its\nartifacts. The dev-logs timestamp sanitizer (dev-logs.ts) already\nestablished the dash convention — mirror it here.\n\nThe auth-redirect spec asserted every /get-session request carries\ndisableCookieCache, but better-auth''s internal session atom (subscribed\nvia useNearAccountId) legitimately fetches without query params — the\nassertion failed in all four browser matrix jobs even though the\nredirect-loop fix itself was green. Replace it with the real server-side\ninvariant: no response may set the better-auth session_data cache cookie\n(it only exists when session.cookieCache is enabled).","tree":{"sha":"2390556bcea066b78a689b0cd2e0019d9332e8a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/trees/2390556bcea066b78a689b0cd2e0019d9332e8a9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/citynode.app/git/commits/a1e1cba8c34cff6ee17627a66ec2077beef8ef13","verification":{"payload":"tree 2390556bcea066b78a689b0cd2e0019d9332e8a9\nparent fb4883a5005490ec00a4b733805ae01c051d0d14\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1790284882 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790284882 -0500\n\nfix(auth): single authoritative session read path — post-sign-in redirect loop (#175)\n\n* fix(auth): single authoritative session read path — post-sign-in redirect loop\n\nAll session reads (route guards, the login route''s beforeLoad, useQuery\nobservers, the post-sign-in refresh) share one queryFn that always calls\ngetSession with disableCookieCache, so every redirect decision sees the same\nanswer and the login <-> dashboard ping-pong (\"Too many redirects\") is\nstructurally impossible. The post-sign-in refresh overrides staleness so a\nfresh signed-out cache entry cannot short-circuit it.\n\nRemoves the login page''s component-level Navigate, loader prefetch, the dead\nrejectAuthed guard, the bootstrap WeakSet bookkeeping, and the initialData\nthreading across call sites. Disables the server-side session cookie cache\noutright (was prod-only, delayed revocation/ban visibility). sanitizeRedirect\nnow rejects /login targets.\n\nRegression tests: unit tests for the refresh-override and guard pass-through\nchain; browser spec asserts every get-session call bypasses the cookie cache.\n\n* fix(test): sanitize regression stack log names + scope browser session assertion\n\nstart-stack.mjs wrote .bos/logs/regression-dev:ssr.log with the raw mode\nstring; the colon is legal on disk but fails actions/upload-artifact\n(invalid character), so every failing dev:* browser leg also lost its\nartifacts. The dev-logs timestamp sanitizer (dev-logs.ts) already\nestablished the dash convention — mirror it here.\n\nThe auth-redirect spec asserted every /get-session request carries\ndisableCookieCache, but better-auth''s internal session atom (subscribed\nvia useNearAccountId) legitimately fetches without query params — the\nassertion failed in all four browser matrix jobs even though the\nredirect-loop fix itself was green. Replace it with the real server-side\ninvariant: no response may set the better-auth session_data cache cookie\n(it only exists when session.cookieCache is enabled).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtZRSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjt4QAF66xHMTkfn1YU6ecqX0CWhi\nGLfec6VTG3itEgP6ovvixl2sW5N3VUBEXFhyWhkkbrajMawS/LA8CVS2T5nIkapX\nz3yqae